-      "volume_pdf": "sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_02_Research_Strategy_and_Risk.pdf",
-      "original_required_outcome": "- An innovation brief stating the opportunity, affected parties, desired outcome, exclusions, and decision owner.\n- A current-state and prior-art baseline sufficient to distinguish a real gap from rediscovery or misunderstanding.\n- Multiple materially different solution hypotheses, including the no-change option and at least one reversible experiment where practical.\n- Explicit assumptions, unknowns, failure hypotheses, dependencies, ethical constraints, and evidence thresholds.\n- Selection criteria authorized by the human rather than inferred from model preference.\n- A smallest-safe experiment plan with expected information gain, resource limits, stop conditions, and recovery.\n- A decision record to continue, revise, hold, reject, transfer, or escalate the opportunity.\n- A continuity package allowing another human or AI role to reproduce what was considered and why.",
-      "original_applicability": "- A problem remains materially unsolved or existing solutions fail important users, environments, or constraints.\n- A new technology, model, material, method, dataset, interface, or organizational capability may change what is feasible.\n- A mission or product requires a step-change rather than routine optimization.\n- Existing assumptions have failed and alternative approaches must be explored.\n- A proposed capability may alter human-AI roles, authority, trust, work, or responsibility.\n- The work includes experimentation whose results may affect later strategy, architecture, or investment.",
