-      "original_required_outcome": "- A bounded feasibility question identifying the objective, decision owner, scope, options, exclusions, environment, horizon, and required confidence.\n- A current-state baseline distinguishing confirmed capability, available capacity, existing obligations, missing prerequisites, unresolved assumptions, and inaccessible evidence.\n- A multidimensional feasibility assessment covering technical, architectural, data, AI or model, operational, human, accessibility, security, privacy, safety, legal, regulatory, economic, schedule, resource, supply-chain, integration, migration, support, maintenance, and retirement concerns as applicable.\n- An option-by-option constraint map identifying mandatory conditions, disqualifying conditions, dependencies, tradeoffs, reversibility, points of no return, and evidence strength.\n- A cheapest-safe resolution plan for material unknowns using inspection, prototype, simulation, proof of concept, benchmark, pilot, test, consultation, or staged experiment.\n- A truthful determination such as FEASIBLE, FEASIBLE WITH CONDITIONS, LIMITED PILOT ONLY, ADDITIONAL EVIDENCE REQUIRED, NOT FEASIBLE WITHIN DECLARED CONSTRAINTS, or OUT OF SCOPE.\n- A handoff package stating which conditions must become requirements, architecture obligations, risk treatments, acceptance criteria, owner decisions, or stop conditions.",
