-      "original_required_outcome": "- A bounded risk-management context identifying objective, scope, assets and values at risk, affected parties, authority, risk owners, time horizon, environments, lifecycle stages, and governing constraints.\n- A common taxonomy distinguishing risk, issue, hazard, threat, vulnerability, exposure, defect, control failure, assumption, unknown, dependency, blocker, opportunity, and residual risk.\n- A traceable risk register containing source, cause, event, consequence, affected objective or party, likelihood basis, impact basis, uncertainty, velocity, detectability, interdependencies, owner, treatment, trigger, threshold, evidence, status, and review date.\n- Explicit treatment decisions: avoid, reduce, transfer or share where legitimate, accept, exploit or enable an opportunity, defer with conditions, escalate, or prohibit.\n- Control and contingency plans covering prevention, protection, detection, response, recovery, communication, rollback, restore, fallback, and safe halt.\n- Risk aggregation and dependency analysis addressing correlated, cascading, systemic, concentration, common-mode, supply-chain, model, data, human, and lifecycle risks.\n- A truthful residual-risk statement and an attributable human acceptance, rejection, or escalation decision where acceptance authority exists.\n- A handoff package that turns risk treatment into requirements, architecture controls, tests, observability, operational procedures, maintenance obligations, and retirement conditions.",
