+{"edition_archive_sha256":"1b7230f30f28753e0ce50219d563079cff7bc5c4b11a3a7026b662837532ae78","coverage_state":"406_SOURCE_SECTIONS_PRESENT_406_APPLICABILITY_ASSESSED_0_PENDING","sections":[{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/001_RESEARCH.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/001_RESEARCH.txt","sha256":"9122ab5b1e2ab728703accb91f7e08fd13f43c7af2bafb096b622cf348d503ff","bytes":19586,"section":"001","original_title":"SECTION 001 — Research","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":2,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_02_Research_Strategy_and_Risk.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A bounded research package that allows the human and assigned agents to answer:\n\n- What is the actual objective?\n- What problem or opportunity is being addressed?\n- Who is affected, accountable, authorized, or exposed to risk?\n- What current system, workflow, environment, market, domain, or physical reality already exists?\n- Which sources are authoritative, current, traceable, and relevant?\n- What assumptions and unknowns materially affect feasibility or design?\n- What conflicting evidence or dissent exists?\n- What must be learned next before consequential design or implementation can proceed?\n- What safe work may continue while unresolved research remains open?","original_applicability":"Research applies whenever the work depends on facts, needs, behavior, constraints, environments, technology, law, risk, feasibility, prior art, user experience, market conditions, physical conditions, or source state that are not already adequately established.\n\nDepth is proportional to consequence, novelty, uncertainty, disagreement, cost, and reversibility. A small reversible script may need a brief source and requirement check. A production system, safety-critical device, governance mechanism, AI system, public product, or irreversible change requires deeper and independently challenged research.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-01-01","REQ-01-02","REQ-01-03","REQ-01-04","REQ-01-05","REQ-04-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-35-02","REQ-35-03","REQ-42-01","REQ-42-03"],"decision_reason":"Whole rebuild depends on material source/runtime/model/migration facts not yet established; complete 354-line source read; current findings/unknowns separated, full outcomes and independent review remain open.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261006_03.md"],"bounded_working_artifact_refs":["handoff/research_and_futures_20261006.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/002_FORESIGHT_OR_FUTURES.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/002_FORESIGHT_OR_FUTURES.txt","sha256":"ac6952b9b410b26197a39b551bc6d62ba05f663d03fc892fc87acb65d414846a","bytes":34305,"section":"002","original_title":"SECTION 002 — Foresight / Futures","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":2,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_02_Research_Strategy_and_Risk.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A bounded futures package that allows the human and assigned agents to answer:\n\n- What time horizons matter to this objective?\n- Which present conditions are being treated as stable, and what evidence supports that treatment?\n- Which drivers, trends, constraints, dependencies, and emerging signals could materially change the objective or its implementation?\n- Which uncertainties are both highly consequential and genuinely unresolved?\n- What multiple plausible futures should be considered rather than collapsed into one forecast?\n- What opportunities, harms, second-order effects, lock-ins, or path dependencies could emerge?\n- Which present decisions remain useful across several futures?\n- Which decisions are fragile, irreversible, or dependent on one narrow scenario?\n- What indicators, thresholds, and review triggers would show that assumptions are failing?\n- What should be preserved so future humans and AI systems can understand, challenge, continue, or reverse today's decisions?\n- Which value conflicts or long-term consequences require explicit human judgment?\n\nThe output is not a claim that the future has been discovered. It is a transparent map of uncertainty, plausible conditions, strategic options, and monitored commitments.","original_applicability":"Foresight applies when one or more of the following are material:\n\n- the system or decision is expected to persist, scale, or be inherited;\n- the work creates long-lived data, infrastructure, interfaces, standards, dependencies, or governance rules;\n- the objective depends on changing technology, markets, regulation, security conditions, resource availability, public trust, or social behavior;\n- the project involves AI, autonomous agents, robotics, connected devices, critical infrastructure, public systems, safety, privacy, identity, or high-consequence decisions;\n- present choices may create lock-in, irreversible effects, concentrated power, exclusion, environmental burden, or difficult retirement obligations;\n- the system must remain useful across uncertain operating environments;\n- the human requests strategic, long-range, resilient, adaptive, or future-facing design;\n- a decision is sensitive to assumptions about capability growth, cost decline, adoption, regulation, interoperability, or institutional response;\n- future owners, users, operators, affected communities, or intelligent systems may need to understand or contest the inherited structure.\n\nDepth is proportional to time horizon, consequence, uncertainty, irreversibility, novelty, disagreement, and the cost of being wrong. Foresight for a disposable personal script may be brief. Foresight for a public platform, constitutional AI system, safety mechanism, long-lived dataset, physical device, or infrastructure layer requires wider scenarios, stronger challenge, explicit monitoring, and long-term recovery thinking.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-01","REQ-03-02","REQ-03-03","REQ-03-04","REQ-04-03","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-29-03","REQ-30-04","REQ-35-02","REQ-38-01","REQ-38-02","REQ-38-03","REQ-38-04"],"decision_reason":"Persistent history, authority and model dependencies require change/reversal analysis; complete 495-line source read; working scenarios are proposals rather than predictions or accepted risk.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261006_03.md"],"bounded_working_artifact_refs":["handoff/research_and_futures_20261006.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/003_INNOVATION.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/003_INNOVATION.txt","sha256":"24467ec91fcd1505833ad4ea77d60364dac2d56d6077b0006742b8b254ad4c56","bytes":19297,"section":"003","original_title":"SECTION 003 — Innovation","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":2,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_02_Research_Strategy_and_Risk.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- An innovation brief stating the opportunity, affected parties, desired outcome, exclusions, and decision owner.\n- A current-state and prior-art baseline sufficient to distinguish a real gap from rediscovery or misunderstanding.\n- Multiple materially different solution hypotheses, including the no-change option and at least one reversible experiment where practical.\n- Explicit assumptions, unknowns, failure hypotheses, dependencies, ethical constraints, and evidence thresholds.\n- Selection criteria authorized by the human rather than inferred from model preference.\n- A smallest-safe experiment plan with expected information gain, resource limits, stop conditions, and recovery.\n- A decision record to continue, revise, hold, reject, transfer, or escalate the opportunity.\n- A continuity package allowing another human or AI role to reproduce what was considered and why.","original_applicability":"- A problem remains materially unsolved or existing solutions fail important users, environments, or constraints.\n- A new technology, model, material, method, dataset, interface, or organizational capability may change what is feasible.\n- A mission or product requires a step-change rather than routine optimization.\n- Existing assumptions have failed and alternative approaches must be explored.\n- A proposed capability may alter human-AI roles, authority, trust, work, or responsibility.\n- The work includes experimentation whose results may affect later strategy, architecture, or investment.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-02","REQ-03-03","REQ-04-04","REQ-24-01","REQ-24-02","REQ-24-03","REQ-24-04","REQ-24-05","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-02","REQ-36-03","REQ-36-04","REQ-39-02"],"decision_reason":"Unresolved reasoning/inference/security hypotheses and unmet quality outcomes require bounded experiments; complete 284-line source read; routine contract tests do not establish novelty, pilot, market or adoption claims.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261006_03.md"],"bounded_working_artifact_refs":["handoff/research_and_futures_20261006.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/004_MISSION_STRATEGY.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/004_MISSION_STRATEGY.txt","sha256":"12fa59010e25bc6073d9254dddf85c248e0c3f13d9c700cc5b91fe710d2630ae","bytes":16751,"section":"004","original_title":"SECTION 004 — Mission Strategy","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"SUPPORTING","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":2,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_02_Research_Strategy_and_Risk.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A mission charter stating purpose, intended beneficiaries, affected parties, time horizon, and final decision owner.\n- A mission problem statement and theory of change grounded in evidence rather than rhetoric.\n- Explicit values, invariants, non-goals, prohibited means, and unacceptable harms.\n- Decision principles for resolving recurring tradeoffs without inventing hidden priorities.\n- Outcome indicators, anti-metrics, failure indicators, and review triggers.\n- A map from mission to strategic capabilities, obligations, and downstream sections without preselecting implementation.\n- A drift and amendment process preserving historical rationale and human authority.","original_applicability":"- A product, program, organization, platform, research effort, or long-lived system needs a durable direction.\n- Multiple initiatives or agents must make consistent decisions under changing conditions.\n- The work carries meaningful social, ethical, safety, environmental, or human-AI consequences.\n- Success may be distorted by short-term business, technical, engagement, or performance metrics.\n- Mission drift, conflicting objectives, or value ambiguity has already appeared.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-00-01","REQ-00-02","REQ-00-03","REQ-00-04","REQ-00-05","REQ-04-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-39-04"],"decision_reason":"Preserve the supplied owner mission and its change/drift boundaries; complete 267-line source read; no new mission/value ordering/moral status or ratification is invented; mission amendment activity is outside this increment.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261006_03.md"],"bounded_working_artifact_refs":["handoff/research_and_futures_20261006.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/005_BUSINESS_STRATEGY.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/005_BUSINESS_STRATEGY.txt","sha256":"894acdc4432d3f7531d03656d73e7feab56c25f3349d94d1c0e290b2faf7b404","bytes":17823,"section":"005","original_title":"SECTION 005 — Business Strategy","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"SUPPORTING","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":2,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_02_Research_Strategy_and_Risk.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A strategy statement defining chosen arena, intended customers or beneficiaries, value mechanism, differentiation, and explicit exclusions.\n- A business model or sustainability model with assumptions, cost and resource drivers, revenue or funding logic where applicable, and evidence quality.\n- A capability and dependency map showing what must exist internally, what may be partnered or purchased, and what remains unknown.\n- Strategic options evaluated under consistent human-authorized criteria, including no-action and staged options.\n- A risk-adjusted sequence of strategic bets, experiments, decision gates, and stop conditions.\n- Mission, stakeholder, legal, ethical, security, privacy, accessibility, and human-AI implications made explicit.\n- A strategy review and change-control process tied to evidence and environmental change.","original_applicability":"- The work must choose markets, customer groups, channels, partnerships, funding, pricing, or operating models.\n- A mission or product requires sustainable resources beyond a one-time build.\n- Multiple strategic alternatives compete for scarce capital, time, talent, infrastructure, or attention.\n- Vendor, platform, model-provider, supply-chain, or regulatory dependencies materially shape viability.\n- The business model may affect privacy, autonomy, safety, accessibility, labor, or human-AI interaction.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-01","REQ-03-02","REQ-23-01","REQ-23-02","REQ-23-03","REQ-23-04","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-29-03","REQ-34-01","REQ-34-02","REQ-34-03","REQ-34-04","REQ-38-01","REQ-38-02","REQ-38-03","REQ-38-04","REQ-38-05"],"decision_reason":"Complete 278-line original read; inherited CETA direction with dependency/resource/license/support viability obligations, no new commercial strategy or commitment; actual costs/capacity/market/partner evidence remain unestablished.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261006_04.md"],"bounded_working_artifact_refs":["handoff/strategy_and_delivery_20261006.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/006_PRODUCT_STRATEGY.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/006_PRODUCT_STRATEGY.txt","sha256":"dc19c5d57a84fc6bc41c21799cb3acc61ae3490d76b77d285967e02a9f517551","bytes":17743,"section":"006","original_title":"SECTION 006 — Product Strategy","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":2,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_02_Research_Strategy_and_Risk.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A product strategy statement identifying intended users, owners, operators, affected parties, contexts, problems, and outcomes.\n- An evidence-backed value proposition and explicit product non-goals.\n- A prioritized capability model rather than an ungoverned feature list.\n- Product principles covering agency, trust, accessibility, privacy, safety, security, reliability, recovery, and human-AI interaction where applicable.\n- A product hypothesis and outcome framework with anti-metrics, risks, and evidence thresholds.\n- A staged product lifecycle and roadmap logic tied to learning, not arbitrary dates.\n- Build, buy, integrate, partner, hold, and retire decision boundaries.","original_applicability":"- A product or product family must choose users, problems, capabilities, positioning, or lifecycle direction.\n- Multiple feature, platform, AI, design, or operational options compete for investment.\n- The product mediates consequential decisions, data, automation, or human-AI interaction.\n- Existing product behavior has drifted from mission, user evidence, or owner control.\n- A new market, platform, user group, or capability requires a product-level decision.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-00-01","REQ-00-02","REQ-00-03","REQ-00-04","REQ-00-05","REQ-03-01","REQ-03-02","REQ-03-03","REQ-03-04","REQ-04-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-04-03","REQ-04-04","REQ-31-01","REQ-31-02","REQ-31-03","REQ-31-04","REQ-31-05","REQ-32-01","REQ-32-02","REQ-32-03","REQ-32-04","REQ-41-01","REQ-41-02","REQ-41-03","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Complete 281-line original read; native persistent governed product affects authority, data and complete human journeys; preserve full supplied product objective and distinguish pure source capability from required real outcomes.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261006_04.md"],"bounded_working_artifact_refs":["handoff/strategy_and_delivery_20261006.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/007_PORTFOLIO_MANAGEMENT.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/007_PORTFOLIO_MANAGEMENT.txt","sha256":"5e7169b7f0b2dfad060c0ae5f0885d06ec19ca3995c938991de16c4e2fff627e","bytes":16488,"section":"007","original_title":"SECTION 007 — Portfolio Management","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"SUPPORTING","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":2,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_02_Research_Strategy_and_Risk.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A complete portfolio inventory with stable identities, owners, purpose, state, evidence, dependencies, commitments, and lifecycle status.\n- Human-authorized selection, balance, prioritization, and termination criteria.\n- A capacity and resource model that distinguishes available, committed, constrained, and hypothetical resources.\n- A dependency and shared-risk map covering platforms, data, vendors, models, people, infrastructure, governance, and customers.\n- Explicit portfolio decisions: initiate, continue, accelerate, hold, reduce, merge, separate, transfer, retire, or reject.\n- A benefits, risk, concentration, and mission-alignment view that preserves uncertainty and dissent.\n- A review cadence and trigger-based rebalancing process with evidence-backed change control.","original_applicability":"- More than one initiative competes for shared resources, platforms, data, customers, operators, or authority.\n- The organization must balance exploration, delivery, maintenance, compliance, resilience, and retirement.\n- Dependencies or risks cross product, program, project, or system boundaries.\n- AI agents or automated workflows may create work faster than humans can govern or fund it