external law, contract or certification applies requires an actual identified scope and authority.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_09.md"],"bounded_working_artifact_refs":["handoff/privacy_assurance_reconciliation_20261007_09.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/050_SAFETY_ARCHITECTURE.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/050_SAFETY_ARCHITECTURE.txt","sha256":"f80c5d7f6bacf067645da58bc347e3a818a32774ee7c46176505ad180a9d88d4","bytes":8521,"section":"050","original_title":"SECTION 050 — Safety Architecture","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":3,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_03_Requirements_through_Hardware_Architecture.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A hazard and harm model with affected parties, operating conditions, controls, safe states, evidence, owners, and residual risk.\n- Explicit prevention, detection, mitigation, stop, emergency, recovery, and change-assurance behavior.\n- Traceability from mission and requirements through design, operation, incidents, testing, and retirement.","original_applicability":"- A system can affect health, bodily safety, property, environment, public services, rights, or high-consequence decisions.\n- Failure, misuse, delay, automation, or human interaction could create material harm.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-04-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-04-03","REQ-04-04","REQ-08-01","REQ-08-02","REQ-08-03","REQ-08-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-19-02","REQ-19-03","REQ-19-04","REQ-19-05","REQ-20-01","REQ-20-02","REQ-20-03","REQ-20-04","REQ-21-01","REQ-21-02","REQ-21-03","REQ-21-04","REQ-21-05","REQ-24-01","REQ-24-02","REQ-24-03","REQ-24-04","REQ-24-05","REQ-25-01","REQ-25-02","REQ-25-03","REQ-25-04","REQ-26-01","REQ-26-02","REQ-26-03","REQ-26-04","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-29-03","REQ-30-01","REQ-30-02","REQ-30-03","REQ-30-04","REQ-32-01","REQ-32-02","REQ-32-03","REQ-32-04","REQ-33-01","REQ-33-02","REQ-33-03","REQ-34-01","REQ-34-02","REQ-34-03","REQ-34-04","REQ-35-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-35-03","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-02","REQ-36-03","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-37-02","REQ-37-03","REQ-37-04","REQ-41-01","REQ-41-02","REQ-41-03","REQ-41-04","REQ-42-01","REQ-42-02","REQ-42-03"],"decision_reason":"Complete 138-line original read. Data loss, unintended effects, misleading decisions, unavailable stop/recovery, rights impacts and the explicitly retained device/actuator lanes create material consequence hazards. A software-only development step does not discharge those hazards.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_09.md"],"bounded_working_artifact_refs":["handoff/privacy_assurance_reconciliation_20261007_09.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/051_RELIABILITY_ARCHITECTURE.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/051_RELIABILITY_ARCHITECTURE.txt","sha256":"02e975dcaf4f43cff43f7d53a5c02ec5cf7f690b661c3dd3337d78d945c0a9d1","bytes":7593,"section":"051","original_title":"SECTION 051 — Reliability Architecture","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":3,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_03_Requirements_through_Hardware_Architecture.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- Reliability objectives, failure models, dependencies, margins, measures, controls, tests, maintenance, and lifecycle are explicit.\n- Claims distinguish design intent, prediction, demonstration, measurement, operational history, and accepted residual risk.","original_applicability":"- Failure frequency, durability, availability, service continuity, maintainability, or evidence validity materially affects outcome.\n- Components operate over time, load, environmental stress, change, or maintenance cycles.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-07-01","REQ-07-02","REQ-07-03","REQ-07-04","REQ-07-05","REQ-08-01","REQ-08-02","REQ-08-03","REQ-08-04","REQ-20-01","REQ-20-02","REQ-20-03","REQ-20-04","REQ-21-01","REQ-21-02","REQ-21-03","REQ-21-04","REQ-21-05","REQ-22-01","REQ-22-02","REQ-22-03","REQ-22-04","REQ-23-01","REQ-23-02","REQ-23-03","REQ-23-04","REQ-24-01","REQ-24-02","REQ-24-03","REQ-24-04","REQ-24-05","REQ-27-01","REQ-27-02","REQ-27-03","REQ-27-04","REQ-28-01","REQ-28-02","REQ-28-03","REQ-30-01","REQ-30-02","REQ-30-03","REQ-30-04","REQ-31-01","REQ-31-02","REQ-31-03","REQ-31-04","REQ-31-05","REQ-34-01","REQ-34-02","REQ-34-03","REQ-34-04","REQ-35-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-35-03","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-02","REQ-36-03","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-37-02","REQ-37-03","REQ-37-04","REQ-38-01","REQ-38-02","REQ-38-03","REQ-38-04","REQ-38-05","REQ-41-01","REQ-41-02","REQ-41-03","REQ-41-04","REQ-42-01","REQ-42-02","REQ-42-03"],"decision_reason":"Complete 134-line original read. Persistent tasks, memory, authority, user data and effects must remain correct under actual workload, resource, maintenance and failure conditions over time. Uptime or a passing unit suite does not demonstrate outcome reliability.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_09.md"],"bounded_working_artifact_refs":["handoff/privacy_assurance_reconciliation_20261007_09.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/052_RESILIENCE_ARCHITECTURE.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/052_RESILIENCE_ARCHITECTURE.txt","sha256":"ebd0638bab0a33a13a6183fd9d60352978b747a4d3d0448c6ff1038dbaab9917","bytes":8084,"section":"0