nal_title":"SECTION 064 — Mechanical Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":4,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_04_Electrical_Engineering_through_User_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A traceable mechanical design with loads, materials, tolerances, joints, motion limits, interfaces, environmental ratings, human access, hazard controls, manufacturing, inspection, maintenance, recovery, and evidence for the declared use conditions.","original_applicability":"Applies to structures, mechanisms, enclosures, mounts, rotating or moving parts, thermal and fluid interfaces, materials, packaging, tooling, facilities, devices, vehicles, and physical service environments.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-04-01","REQ-05-01","REQ-08-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-20-01","REQ-24-01","REQ-25-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-32-04","REQ-33-03","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-04","REQ-38-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Complete 100-line original read. Explicit physical lanes can involve motion, loads, enclosures, access, temperature and service hazards. Their qualification cannot be inferred from desktop contract tests.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_10.md"],"bounded_working_artifact_refs":["handoff/volume_iv_reconciliation_20261007_10.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/065_INDUSTRIAL_DESIGN.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/065_INDUSTRIAL_DESIGN.txt","sha256":"f487e95ff93a81194445c31c70e47bbd14ef49eed21c2451cb1989f4200d9840","bytes":6039,"section":"065","original_title":"SECTION 065 — Industrial Design","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":4,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_04_Electrical_Engineering_through_User_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A documented industrial design baseline linking user needs, form, ergonomics, materials, interfaces, production, quality, service, evidence, and lifecycle decisions.","original_applicability":"Applies to physical products, devices, enclosures, controls, packaging, tools, public-facing artifacts, and connected products where human use or physical realization matters.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-04-01","REQ-24-01","REQ-25-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-32-01","REQ-32-04","REQ-33-03","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-04","REQ-38-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Complete 95-line original read. The retained device lane has physical human-use, accessibility, safety and service implications; aesthetic or digital renderings cannot validate them.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_10.md"],"bounded_working_artifact_refs":["handoff/volume_iv_reconciliation_20261007_10.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/066_SEMICONDUCTOR_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/066_SEMICONDUCTOR_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"6d53edd15d8002722144ec30bb738e28f04779278fbe15f5e54284ebc5260922","bytes":5799,"section":"066","original_title":"SECTION 066 — Semiconductor Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"SUPPORTING","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":4,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_04_Electrical_Engineering_through_User_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A traceable device or process baseline with device behavior, process limits, masks or equivalent design artifacts, packaging, test, yield, qualification, supply, and retirement controls.","original_applicability":"Applies to integrated circuits, dies, process nodes, memory, sensors, power devices, accelerators, packaging, wafer or device test, and semiconductor supply decisions.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-01","REQ-22-01","REQ-23-01","REQ-24-01","REQ-26-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-04","REQ-38-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Complete 95-line original read. CETA relies on supplied processors, memory, accelerators and possible hardware anchors. It does not currently own silicon/process/mask/foundry engineering.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_10.md"],"bounded_working_artifact_refs":["handoff/volume_iv_reconciliation_20261007_10.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/067_PCB_DESIGN.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/067_PCB_DESIGN.txt","sha256":"9d1800f0c9d719f17a2f4e9d7df296219a0b67f3e39e1bc4a5014415a08c9816","bytes":5542,"section":"067","original_title":"SECTION 067 — PCB Design","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"SUPPORTING","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":4,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_04_Electrical_Engineering_through_User_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A controlled PCB baseline with stackup, placement, routing, power and signal integrity, thermal and EMC constraints, manufacturability, test access, revision identity, and evidence.","original_applicability":"Applies to rigid, flexible, rigid-flex, high-speed, power, RF, mixed-signal, prototype, production, and assembled PCB designs.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-05-01","REQ-06-02","REQ-21-03","REQ-23-01","REQ-24-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-33-03","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-04","REQ-38-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Complete 95-line original read. Selected devices may rely on board revision, electrical/firmware interfaces and as-built behavior. The current CETA scope creates no PCB geometry, stackup or fabrication output.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_10.md"],"bounded_working_artifact_refs":["handoff/volume_iv_reconciliation_20261007_10.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/068_FIRMWARE_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/068_FIRMWARE_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"46c9b8febde65d44e70774093dcce251be33afa87a8ba1ef31eec32a2f3befdb","bytes":5755,"section":"068","original_title":"SECTION 068 — Firmware Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":4,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_04_Electrical_Engineering_through_User_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A traceable firmware baseline with hardware contracts, boot, timing, interrupts, drivers, state, update, diagnostics, security, recovery, test, and evidence controls.","original_applicability":"Applies to boot code, device firmware, microcontroller software, drivers, board support, bootloaders, update agents, diagnostics, and safety or security monitors.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-03","REQ-06-02","REQ-08-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-21-03","REQ-23-01","REQ-25-01","REQ-26-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-33-03","REQ-34-04","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-04","REQ-38-01","REQ-38-03","REQ-38-04"],"decision_reason":"Complete 95-line original read. Physical adapters and hardware custody can depend on boot, firmware, drivers, image and update semantics. Compilation alone cannot establish those semantics.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_10.md"],"bounded_working_artifact_refs":["handoff/volume_iv_reconciliation_20261007_10.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/069_EMBEDDED_SOFTWARE_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/069_EMBEDDED_SOFTWARE_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"2857dac63d65a4d9121ffd12e7f57111240b61f7c3fe16c9c0b0b3396335c166","bytes":9114,"section":"069","original_title":"SECTION 069 — Embedded Software Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":4,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_04_Electrical_Engineering_through_User_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A bounded embedded-software scope, hardware boundary, operating modes, timing model, resource budget, ownership, and lifecycle.\n - Requirements, architecture, interfaces, state behavior, build provenance, configuration, tests, evidence, update, recovery, and retirement records.\n - Explicit human authority for safety, security, release, field update, degraded operation, and acceptance.","original_applicability":"Applies when software runs on a device, controller, appliance, instrument, vehicle, industrial asset, sensor, actuator, or constrained compute target, or when software depends materially on hardware timing, interrupts, peripherals, boot state, power, or physical environment.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-05-01","REQ-06-02","REQ-08-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-21-03","REQ-23-01","REQ-25-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-33-03","REQ-34-04","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-04","REQ-38-01","REQ-38-03","REQ-38-04","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Complete 112-line original read. An actual device/controller variant of the retained physical lane must respect target timing, power, interrupts, resource, update and safety boundaries.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_10.md"],"bounded_working_artifact_refs":["handoff/volume_iv_reconciliation_20261007_10.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/070_INTERNET_OF_THINGS_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/070_INTERNET_OF_THINGS_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"ffae0cfade8526dd2fdef19db661d7aa719a73418a983f530801989113e7762a","bytes":7999,"section":"070","original_title":"SECTION 070 — Internet of Things Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"SUPPORTING","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":4,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_04_Electrical_Engineering_through_User_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A bounded device, network, cloud, edge, data, user, operator, and lifecycle scope.\n - Governed identity, provisioning, telemetry, command, firmware, privacy, security, resilience, interoperability, and retirement contracts.\n - Traceable evidence from device behavior through service outcome and owner control.","original_applicability":"Applies to networked sensors, actuators, appliances, vehicles, facilities, industrial assets, wearables, gateways, edge devices, device fleets, and services that provision, monitor, command, or retire them.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-06-02","REQ-08-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-20-01","REQ-21-03","REQ-24-01","REQ-25-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-33-03","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-04","REQ-38-04","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Complete 106-line original read. The manifested device/physical adapter contract can cover connected devices, but no fleet, device class, enrollment service, cloud provider or collection scope is selected.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_10.md"],"bounded_working_artifact_refs":["handoff/volume_iv_reconciliation_20261007_10.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/071_TELECOMMUNICATIONS_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/071_TELECOMMUNICATIONS_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"4aceaefd7bfc7f92d8a4d037290408f3c32cddb6dd99ec0d20454081d0d7ced1","bytes":7880,"section":"071","original_title":"SECTION 071 — Telecommunications Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"SUPPORTING","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":4,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_04_Electrical_Engineering_through_User_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A bounded service, endpoint, medium, protocol, spectrum, traffic, user, operator, jurisdiction, and lifecycle scope.\n - Explicit interfaces, identity, authorization, quality, capacity, availability, privacy, security, emergency, and recovery obligations.\n - Evidence linking network behavior to user and service outcomes.","original_applicability":"Applies to wired, wireless, optical, satellite, radio, cellular, voice, messaging, media, signaling, control, and carrier or private communications systems with material service or physical consequences.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-04-01","REQ-08-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-21-03","REQ-24-01","REQ-25-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-33-03","REQ-34-04","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-04","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Complete 107-line original read. The local product has communications dependencies and retained network/device adapters. It does not become a carrier, radio service or telephony product by applying this source.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_10.md"],"bounded_working_artifact_refs":["handoff/volume_iv_reconciliation_20261007_10.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/072_SIGNAL_PROCESSING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/072_SIGNAL_PROCESSING.txt","sha256":"80696630f46dcd7141280b4a32ebda72a5aa2c1d8a41b28ae631f435fa8120b5","bytes":7887,"section":"072","original_title":"SECTION 072 — Signal Processing","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":4,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_04_Electrical_Engineering_through_User_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A declared signal, sensor, sampling, processing, output, environment, latency, resource, and lifecycle scope.\n - Versioned algorithms, calibration, transforms, models, thresholds, interfaces, evidence, failure, and recovery records.\n - Human authority over interpretation, thresholds, physical action, and acceptance of signal-derived outcomes.","original_applicability":"Applies to sensing, communications, audio, image, radar, biomedical, industrial, control, scientific, or machine-learning pipelines that acquire or transform signals into information or action.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-06-02","REQ-08-01","REQ-09-01","REQ-11-01","REQ-13-03","REQ-19-01","REQ-22-01","REQ-24-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-33-01","REQ-33-02","REQ-34-04","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-04","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Complete 106-line original read. Explicit voice, selected-screen and device observations transform signals into uncertain information. Processing outputs and model confidence are not ground truth.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_10.md"],"bounded_working_artifact_refs":["handoff/volume_iv_reconciliation_20261007_10.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/073_CONTROL_SYSTEMS_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/073_CONTROL_SYSTEMS_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"a0665d79141f9873ffb921519844db9e1225effad5dc8b96b9aaad1e22cda891","bytes":5923,"section":"073","original_title":"SECTION 073 — Control Systems Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":4,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_04_Electrical_Engineering_through_User_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A scoped plant, controller, sensor, actuator, timing, safety, stability, authority, and lifecycle model.\n - Traceable control laws, interfaces, simulations, tests, margins, failure modes, recovery, and acceptance evidence.","original_applicability":"Applies to automatic, supervisory, adaptive, robotic, industrial, vehicle, energy, medical, environmental, and software control loops.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-04-01","REQ-05-01","REQ-07-01","REQ-08-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-20-01","REQ-21-03","REQ-25-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-33-03","REQ-34-04","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-04","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Complete 96-line original read. CETA supervises an operating cycle and retains physical actuation. Feedback capability does not supply authority or prove robustness on an actual plant.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_10.md"],"bounded_working_artifact_refs":["handoff/volume_iv_reconciliation_20261007_10.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/074_ROBOTICS_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/074_ROBOTICS_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"e5f83441134913c6b65e0a11a0fa9d8f04dec27237cc3a068bb8e9d1536b3c30","bytes":6140,"section":"074","original_title":"SECTION 074 — Robotics Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":4,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_04_Electrical_Engineering_through_User_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A scoped robot, environment, mission, human, sensor, actuator, autonomy, safety, security, and lifecycle model.\n - Traceable behavior, motion, task, interaction, update, recovery, verification, field, and acceptance evidence.","original_applicability":"Applies to mobile, stationary, collaborative, industrial, service, medical, aerial, marine, space, and simulated robots with material autonomy or physical effect.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-04-01","REQ-06-02","REQ-09-01","REQ-15-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-20-01","REQ-24-01","REQ-25-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-32-04","REQ-33-03","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-04","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Complete 96-line original read. REQ-33-03 retains physical devices and interlocks; any selected robot variant needs mission, environment, autonomy, human-proximity and physical-outcome qualification.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_10.md"],"bounded_working_artifact_refs":["handoff/volume_iv_reconciliation_20261007_10.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/075_HUMAN_COMPUTER_INTERACTION.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/075_HUMAN_COMPUTER_INTERACTION.txt","sha256":"79d7af361584a3ef6f8e0b0ddd7d6b7f79ce4624400501cdf134ba50a9085b50","bytes":6045,"section":"075","original_title":"SECTION 075 — Human–Computer Interaction","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":4,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_04_Electrical_Engineering_through_User_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A declared population, context, task, device, modality, accessibility, risk, and lifecycle scope.\n - Evidence-backed interaction requirements, flows, feedback, error recovery, authority, privacy, and acceptance criteria.","original_applicability":"Applies when people interact with software, devices, services, agents, physical systems, dashboards, tools, or automation, especially where comprehension, access, decision, or recovery matters.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-09-01","REQ-10-01","REQ-13-05","REQ-19-01","REQ-24-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-32-01","REQ-32-03","REQ-32-04","REQ-33-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-02","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Complete 96-line original read. Users/operators must understand and control the requested native system across ordinary, ambiguous, denied, interrupted and assistive paths.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_10.md"],"bounded_working_artifact_refs":["handoff/volume_iv_reconciliation_20261007_10.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/076_INTERACTION_DESIGN.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/076_INTERACTION_DESIGN.txt","sha256":"93609be54550af812ca44e645f14cee7683ca7dd3d207926ee4291769f416e6a","bytes":5492,"section":"076","original_title":"SECTION 076 — Interaction Design","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":4,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_04_Electrical_Engineering_through_User_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A scoped interaction model tied to users, tasks, system states, modalities, content, permissions, and outcomes.\n - Prototypes, specifications, evidence, accessibility, failure, recovery, and acceptance records.","original_applicability":"Applies to user, operator, admin, assistive, conversational, physical, spatial, or multimodal controls and transitions.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-07-01","REQ-13-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-24-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-32-01","REQ-32-03","REQ-32-04","REQ-33-01","REQ-34-04","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-02","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Complete 96-line original read. The native experience needs explicit understandable states, pending authority, errors and accessible cancellation/correction rather than a polished nominal flow.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_10.md"],"bounded_working_artifact_refs":["handoff/volume_iv_reconciliation_20261007_10.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/077_EXPERIENCE_DESIGN.txt","