":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":4,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_04_Electrical_Engineering_through_User_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A bounded service ecosystem, actors, value exchange, frontstage and backstage, dependencies, outcomes, and lifecycle.\n - Service blueprint, ownership, measures, controls, accessibility, failure, continuity, and acceptance records.","original_applicability":"Applies to public, commercial, internal, digital, physical, assisted, subscription, support, and multi-party services.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-04-01","REQ-05-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-21-03","REQ-23-01","REQ-24-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-32-01","REQ-34-04","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-02","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Complete 96-line original read. The local product coordinates people, processes, policy, model/tool suppliers and support/recovery. Outsourcing a dependency does not outsource outcome accountability.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_10.md"],"bounded_working_artifact_refs":["handoff/volume_iv_reconciliation_20261007_10.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/079_UX_STRATEGY.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/079_UX_STRATEGY.txt","sha256":"ee347bd09853d23f98f5f4fe5baf18be2c11bb4c552adf0d90c11a710ca641ee","bytes":5490,"section":"079","original_title":"SECTION 079 — UX Strategy","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":4,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_04_Electrical_Engineering_through_User_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A declared experience ambition, users, business or mission outcomes, constraints, portfolio choices, measures, and horizon.\n - Prioritized experience principles, evidence, investment decisions, risks, governance, and acceptance criteria.","original_applicability":"Applies when experience is a material source of value, adoption, safety, trust, inclusion, service quality, differentiation, or change priority.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-01","REQ-04-01","REQ-13-05","REQ-24-01","REQ-32-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-02","REQ-39-04","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04","REQ-42-03"],"decision_reason":"Complete 96-line original read. Experience decisions must support the owner's complete CETA outcome and retained controls, rather than shrink the product to a convenient demonstrable subset.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_10.md"],"bounded_working_artifact_refs":["handoff/volume_iv_reconciliation_20261007_10.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/080_UX_RESEARCH.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/080_UX_RESEARCH.txt","sha256":"3e1b6c6d0dba902c855ac40c465ebd1e719648a228eae41bec22f3ed9b6343d3","bytes":5438,"section":"080","original_title":"SECTION 080 — UX Research","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":4,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_04_Electrical_Engineering_through_User_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A research question, population, context, method, consent and protection plan, evidence record, analysis, limitation, and decision link.\n - Reproducible findings that distinguish observation, interpretation, hypothesis, and recommendation.","original_applicability":"Applies to discovery, evaluation, accessibility, service, product, operational, safety, and post-release questions involving people or affected communities.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-06-02","REQ-09-01","REQ-13-03","REQ-19-01","REQ-24-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-29-03","REQ-32-04","REQ-33-02","REQ-35-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-02","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Complete 96-line original read. User/assistive acceptance claims require actual method, population, context and evidence; synthetic examples and AI summaries cannot fabricate participants or representative results.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_10.md"],"bounded_working_artifact_refs":["handoff/volume_iv_reconciliation_20261007_10.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/081_UX_ARCHITECTURE.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/081_UX_ARCHITECTURE.txt","sha256":"05ba286ebf015c9f627a7ebd3311ad4f258ac197a12bbc909286e70aa13a42bf","bytes":5277,"section":"081","original_title":"SECTION 081 — UX Architecture","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":4,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_04_Electrical_Engineering_through_User_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A scoped UX landscape connecting user outcomes to journeys, interaction structures, content, systems, services, and governance.\n - Stable experience models, principles, patterns, evidence, controls, measures, and lifecycle handoffs.","original_applicability":"Applies to products, platforms, services, suites, multi-channel ecosystems, design systems, and complex user or operator journeys.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-04-01","REQ-05-01","REQ-07-01","REQ-11-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-24-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-32-01","REQ-32-03","REQ-32-04","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-02","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Complete 96-line original read. Conversation, current work, approvals, memory/evidence, models and recovery need one experience structure connected to actual domain state and ownership.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_10.md"],"bounded_working_artifact_refs":["handoff/volume_iv_reconciliation_20261007_10.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/082_UX_DESIGN.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/082_UX_DESIGN.txt","sha256":"22ce15df1f614d0d8647b4d307ae33be9a60868c7f6cd84f6b584627ed1228fe","bytes":5051,"section":"082","original_title":"SECTION 082 — UX Design","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":4,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_04_Electrical_Engineering_through_User_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A declared user, task, context, journey, interaction, content, accessibility, risk, and outcome scope.\n - Tested designs and specifications with traceable evidence, decisions, limitations, and implementation handoff.","original_applicability":"Applies to user, operator, admin, support, assistive, mobile, desktop, physical, conversational, and multimodal experiences.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-10-01","REQ-13-05","REQ-19-01","REQ-2