on_Volume_04_Electrical_Engineering_through_User_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A scoped locale model, language, data, formatting, content, architecture, workflow, testing, ownership, and lifecycle baseline.\n - Explicit variation points, defaults, fallback, evidence, and acceptance criteria.","original_applicability":"Applies to products, platforms, data, content, APIs, services, operations, and systems expected to support more than one locale or cultural context.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-06-03","REQ-08-01","REQ-10-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-24-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-32-04","REQ-33-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-02","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Complete 96-line original read. The product processes user language, timestamps, units and formatted data; hidden global locale assumptions could alter content or exact security semantics.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_10.md"],"bounded_working_artifact_refs":["handoff/volume_iv_reconciliation_20261007_10.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/103_ACCESSIBILITY_DESIGN.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/103_ACCESSIBILITY_DESIGN.txt","sha256":"d3711668ee9a1ab7e40776a3338ae8ad1e96213d5bb66824a29a05220d117511","bytes":5386,"section":"103","original_title":"SECTION 103 — Accessibility Design","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":4,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_04_Electrical_Engineering_through_User_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A scoped population, task, context, technology, access need, standard, risk, and lifecycle model.\n - Accessibility requirements, alternatives, evidence, tests, exceptions, and owner controls.","original_applicability":"Applies to products, services, content, physical or digital interfaces, devices, documents, environments, and owner or operator controls.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-13-05","REQ-19-01","REQ-24-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-32-01","REQ-32-02","REQ-32-04","REQ-33-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-02","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Complete 96-line original read. The explicit native accessibility requirement spans setup, authentication, review, memory, models, failures, stop, correction and recovery.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_10.md"],"bounded_working_artifact_refs":["handoff/volume_iv_reconciliation_20261007_10.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/104_DESIGN_SYSTEMS.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/104_DESIGN_SYSTEMS.txt","sha256":"029dec5e4929c917a45334ad4bc3f95c292e0457bb20354622288459fffb04a9","bytes":5245,"section":"104","original_title":"SECTION 104 — Design Systems","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":4,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_04_Electrical_Engineering_through_User_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A scoped system, consumers, primitives, patterns, ownership, versioning, contribution, accessibility, evidence, and lifecycle model.\n - Governed components and documentation with tests, exceptions, migration, and acceptance records.","original_applicability":"Applies to shared UI, interaction, content, visual, motion, voice, code, token, and service patterns.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-04-01","REQ-05-01","REQ-07-01","REQ-24-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-31-01","REQ-32-01","REQ-32-04","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-02","REQ-38-04","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Complete 96-line original read. Common native patterns can propagate state, accessibility, content or timing defects across all required workflows; reuse must preserve context and ownership.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_10.md"],"bounded_working_artifact_refs":["handoff/volume_iv_reconciliation_20261007_10.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/105_PROTOTYPING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/105_PROTOTYPING.txt","sha256":"834f6ea90bafe8be0666e7e1b30fbb4388ca3ab7c8c515f44b5a39b82d1cd117","bytes":21999,"section":"105","original_title":"SECTION 105 — Prototyping","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":4,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_04_Electrical_Engineering_through_User_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A declared prototype question, learning objective, scope, audience, fidelity, time horizon, owner, authority, and stop condition.\n- A prototype plan that identifies what is represented, what is intentionally omitted, what is simulated, what is real, and what claims the artifact cannot support.\n- A traceable relationship from the prototype to requirements, user needs, processes, functions, architecture, risks, decisions, and next actions.\n- A usable prototype artifact or experiment that allows the intended question to be examined under stated conditions.\n- Evidence from observation, inspection, measurement, technical execution, or user interaction that is bounded by method, sample, environment, and limitations.\n- A decision record stating what was learned, what remains unknown, which assumptions changed, whether the prototype should be discarded, revised, promoted, or stopped, and who has authority for that decision.","original_applicability":"- A proposed outcome, requirement, interaction, workflow, service, architecture, component, integration, model, or operational concept contains material uncertainty.\n- Stakeholders need to compare alternatives, expose assumptions, or inspect a future state before committing to implementation.\n- A change affects users, operators, maintainers, support, accessibility, safety, privacy, security, data, reliability, cost, or lifecycle obligations.\n- A technical or service risk can be reduced through a bounded experiment, simulation, spike, mock, pilot, or rehearsal.\n- AI, automation, tools, data, external providers, or human review are proposed for a consequential workflow.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-04-01","REQ-15-01","REQ-15-02","REQ-15-03","REQ-19-01","REQ-24-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-32-04","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-02","REQ-40-03","REQ-41-04","REQ-42-03"],"decision_reason":"Complete 222-line original read. The rebuild contains material technical/user/containment/migration uncertainty; isolated fixtures and rehearsals must answer explicit questions with honest limits.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_10.md"],"bounded_working_artifact_refs":["handoff/volume_iv_reconciliation_20261007_10.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/106_USER_VALIDATION.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/106_USER_VALIDATION.txt","sha256":"1bad1e012067455a232ac6ce544eeb0e60a2230088e00a1bafd0a3e89a0de6c9","bytes":22547,"section":"106","original_title":"SECTION 106 — User Validation","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":4,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_04_Electrical_Engineering_through_User_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A declared validation question, intended user and affected-party outcome, population, context, version, owner, authority, and decision boundary.\n- A participant and evidence plan that addresses representativeness, accessibility, safety, privacy, consent or authorization, bias, and limitations.\n- Reproducible tasks, scenarios, instruments, observation methods, and acceptance criteria appropriate to the decision.\n- Evidence showing what users and affected people could understand, accomplish, experience, challenge, correct, or recover from under stated conditions.\n- Analysis that separates observed behavior, participant report, interpretation, recommendation, and owner decision.\n- A decision record identifying validated outcomes, failed or unresolved outcomes, affected groups, required changes, residual risk, and the authority to accept, defer, narrow, reject, or reopen.","original_applicability":"- A change may affect user goals, comprehension, workflow, accessibility, safety, privacy, security, dignity, rights, trust, burden, or recovery.\n- A product, service, system, process, content, interaction, AI behavior, policy, or operating model is proposed for a defined population or context.\n- Requirements or acceptance depend on user outcomes, task performance, comprehension, accessibility, satisfaction, confidence, correction, appeal, or harm reduction.\n- Different populations, environments, devices, languages, abilities, roles, or operating conditions may experience materially different results.\n- AI, automation, recommendation, ranking, generation, or decision support may change what users see, decide, or can control.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-04-01","REQ-06-02","REQ-09-01","REQ-13-03","REQ-19-01","REQ-24-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-32-04","REQ-33-02","REQ-35-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-02","REQ-40-03","REQ-41-04","REQ-42-03"],"decision_reason":"Complete 221-line original read. The requested native product must support real comprehension, task outcomes, access, control, privacy, correction and recovery under declared contexts.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_10.md"],"bounded_working_artifact_refs":["handoff/volume_iv_reconciliation_20261007_10.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/107_SOFTWARE_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/107_SOFTWARE_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"d13dbc6f183f4a84fa363bdc8e4a783b98845cff35165872e93fcb48dc069a46","bytes":12033,"section":"107","original_title":"SECTION 107 — Software Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A bounded software scope, quality model, lifecycle, ownership, and engineering plan.\n- Traceable requirements, design, source, dependencies, configuration, builds, tests, releases, runtime evidence, defects, and retirement records.\n- Reproducible development and build conditions with review, secure supply chain, accessibility, observability, and recovery controls.\n- Explicit treatment of human, AI-assisted, generated, third-party, and machine-produced code.\n- Verification evidence that distinguishes code inspection, test results, build success, deployment, and user or operational acceptance.","original_applicability":"- Software is designed, coded, configured, generated, integrated, tested, released, operated, maintained, migrated, or retired.\n- A change affects behavior, interfaces, data, permissions, performance, reliability, accessibility, security, privacy, safety, or evidence.\n- Source, dependencies, build tools, models, generated artifacts, or external services create supply-chain or reproducibility concerns.\n- The work requires controlled collaboration, code review, branching, release, rollback, maintenance, or defect management.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-00-01","REQ-00-04","REQ-03-01","REQ-04-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-05-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-37-01"],"decision_reason":"CETA is a ground-up software implementation whose source, dependencies, artifacts, defects and recovery must remain attributable. Retain exact source/tool/dependency/build identities and generated-code provenance; complete material review, clean builds, integration, hostile-input, compatibility, accessibility and recovery evidence. Test, build, runtime, user acceptance, support and retirement remain separate. No generated code or passing test is owner acceptance.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/108_COMPUTER_SCIENCE.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/108_COMPUTER_SCIENCE.txt","sha256":"50075e22762e9734c69fe4c98263e0f9092701fb8144505c368ef52438c04162","bytes":6482,"section":"108","original_title":"SECTION 108 — Computer Science","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"The result is a bounded computational question, model or proof basis, assumptions, complexity analysis, reproducible method, evidence, limitations, and handoff to engineering or architecture.","original_applicability":"Applies when computational complexity, correctness, formal models, algorithms, data structures, languages, concurrency, distributed behavior, information representation, or theoretical limits affect a design or decision.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-04-01","REQ-06-01","REQ-08-01","REQ-13-03","REQ-16-01","REQ-17-01","REQ-34-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The kernel, canonical representations, scheduling, concurrency and graph semantics depend on computational models and resource limits. State the exact question, definitions, assumptions, correctness and termination/resource properties. Keep proof, conjecture, reference, simulation and actual implementation distinct; retain counterexamples and qualified review. No universal formalism or proof of correctness was invented.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/109_ALGORITHM_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/109_ALGORITHM_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"4f1d9f77273b4c2833eb8d321ba6872c417e1ee7dda3e28fee17acb8ea51ffaf","bytes":6587,"section":"109","original_title":"SECTION 109 — Algorithm Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A specified algorithm with contract, assumptions, complexity, resource limits, implementation, test evidence, alternatives, failure behavior, monitoring, and acceptance boundaries.","original_applicability":"Applies to deterministic, randomized, heuristic, optimization, search, ranking, scheduling, control, cryptographic, statistical, or learned algorithms with material system effects.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-11-02","REQ-12-01","REQ-14-01","REQ-16-01","REQ-18-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-24-01","REQ-34-01","REQ-34-04","REQ-35-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Retrieval, ranking, scheduling, policy evaluation and model execution produce material outputs in the required product. Specify objective, input distribution, invariants, alternatives, worst-case resource/error behavior, test oracle, version/configuration and drift. Evaluate malformed, missing, duplicate, shifted and adversarial inputs. Ranking and optimization do not grant authority; benchmark speed does not prove useful or safe outcomes.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/110_PROGRAMMING_LANGUAGE_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/110_PROGRAMMING_LANGUAGE_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"ede9904af1912009190599577df44bd4c00ea40bf14bb9cdc1bceb74632a8441","bytes":6584,"section":"110","original_title":"SECTION 110 — Programming Language Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A versioned language and toolchain contract with intended users, semantics, safety and security properties, implementation status, conformance evidence, compatibility policy, migration path, and retirement conditions.","original_applicability":"Applies when a language, dialect, DSL, compiler, interpreter, virtual machine, standard library, formatter, linter, debugger, package ecosystem, or compatibility guarantee is designed or changed.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-03","REQ-04-01","REQ-06-01","REQ-16-01","REQ-16-02","REQ-16-03","REQ-17-01","REQ-31-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-38-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"REQ-16-02 explicitly requires compilation of policy sources into bounded typed IR; consuming Python and Rust does not require a separate general-purpose language project. Define the actual supported policy grammar, types, effects, evaluation, errors, limits and migration; retain the carried-forward 23-operation semantics and differential fixtures. Reject ambiguity and nondeterministic authority. Pin consumed host-language/toolchain baselines without importing another repository or inventing universal conformance.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/111_COMPILER_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/111_COMPILER_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"261110a28a59e01cb6d2ff334d5fea304fdabccb638a56b626d39c2e099031b8","bytes":5783,"section":"111","original_title":"SECTION 111 — Compiler Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A versioned compiler contract, implementation, target matrix, conformance suite, reproducible build, diagnostics, security model, compatibility statement, and evidence-backed release boundary.","original_applicability":"Applies to compiler, interpreter, assembler, linker, optimizer, code generator, transpiler, static analyzer, debugger, build backend, or language-toolchain change.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-04-01","REQ-05-01","REQ-06-01","REQ-14-01","REQ-15-01","REQ-16-01","REQ-16-02","REQ-17-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-38-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The required policy compiler and graph-to-supported-plan translation change executable meaning at a trust boundary. Bind original source, compiler/version/flags, effective policy, typed IR, supported operations and target. Verify passes, resource bounds, invalid input, diagnostics, reference comparisons, deterministic output and compatibility. Reject unsupported mappings; no separate compiler ecosystem or conformance certification is required.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/112_RUNTIME_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/112_RUNTIME_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"0cd8e02420d9267227b52fc9e51eb02c64a6224e4c457b0209776a014f167b89","bytes":5350,"section":"112","original_title":"SECTION 112 — Runtime Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A versioned runtime contract covering execution semantics, resources, isolation, compatibility, observability, failure, recovery, security, support, and evidence.","original_applicability":"Applies to virtual machines, interpreters, managed runtimes, containers, schedulers, garbage collectors, loaders, plugin hosts, sandboxes, and execution libraries.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-02","REQ-03-03","REQ-07-01","REQ-08-01","REQ-10-01","REQ-18-01","REQ-21-01","REQ-21-02","REQ-23-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-34-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"CETA owns supervised model/worker execution, resource admission, cancellation and recovery rather than merely consuming an unchanged runtime. Specify startup/shutdown, scheduling, quotas, backpressure, memory/I/O, signals, upgrade and failure contracts. Exercise overload, adversarial work, interrupted shutdown and dependency loss on actual hosts. A healthy process or pure unit test does not qualify execution or isolation.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/113_OPERATING_SYSTEMS_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/113_OPERATING_SYSTEMS_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"7520d77ae970bd77cc084dd788e21a6e8ff0902d1eaa6c3627af0fdf709abd33","bytes":5413,"section":"113","original_title":"SECTION 113 — Operating Systems Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A versioned OS contract, kernel and user-space boundaries, security model, driver and hardware assumptions, compatibility, test evidence, update, recovery, and retirement plan.","original_applicability":"Applies to kernels, system services, distributions, boot systems, filesystems, process models, security subsystems, device support, and OS-level configuration or update.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-01","REQ-03-03","REQ-05-01","REQ-21-01","REQ-21-02","REQ-21-03","REQ-21-04","REQ-21-05","REQ-23-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"REQ-21 requires actual Windows process, identity, file, handle, device and isolation controls; CETA remains an application on the host OS. Bind actual supported OS/hardware/driver configuration and qualify narrow principal, process, file/handle, storage, resource, update and recovery interfaces. Job Objects alone do not prove file/network isolation. Do not alter boot, replace the host kernel or invent a distribution; privileged installation/control retains its concrete authority gate.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/114_KERNEL_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/114_KERNEL_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"0100dce5683ef1d1bc11a5b3f32587d0fea4e06d103a21639a3eb0a881718baa","bytes":5545,"section":"114","original_title":"SECTION 114 — Kernel Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"SUPPORTING","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A bounded kernel contract with privilege and threat model, invariants, hardware assumptions, interfaces, performance limits, test evidence, update and recovery path, and explicit acceptance authority.","original_applicability":"Applies to kernel code, hypervisor-like privileged layers, schedulers, memory managers, interrupt paths, system-call interfaces, and kernel configuration or extensions.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-03","REQ-16-01","REQ-21-01","REQ-21-02","REQ-23-01","REQ-25-01","REQ-27-04","REQ-35-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"CETA does not build or replace a privileged OS kernel; its deterministic governance kernel is application policy code using qualified host mechanisms. Retain actual OS kernel/configuration/driver trust assumptions and affected security/resource/recovery evidence. No custom syscall ABI, boot chain, interrupt handler, kernel module or kernel signing operation is inferred. Reopen direct privileged-code clauses on a real host-kernel/module/trust-boundary change; no same-privilege simulation proves OS separation.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/115_DRIVER_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/115_DRIVER_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"6f0952390d466945e69078f5cc01060436bc997d1a80316f8f941db6f58d1691","bytes":5092,"section":"115","original_title":"SECTION 115 — Driver Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A versioned driver contract covering hardware assumptions, discovery, permissions, I/O, timing, errors, isolation, compatibility, tests, update, recovery, and evidence.","original_applicability":"Applies to kernel, user-space, firmware-adjacent, virtual, bus, device, sensor, actuator, and compatibility drivers.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-06-02","REQ-08-01","REQ-21-03","REQ-23-01","REQ-25-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-33-03","REQ-35-02","REQ-37-04","REQ-38-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"REQ-33-03 retains qualified device/sensor/actuator adapters with hardware-access, timing, permission and safe-state consequences. Bind actual selected device, bus/protocol, firmware/driver/OS revisions, discovery, I/O, timeouts, disconnects, power, diagnostics and recovery. Test representative devices and qualified interlocks before operation. Preserve consumed vendor driver baselines; no custom kernel driver, flash, field update or electrical behavior was invented.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/116_MIDDLEWARE_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/116_MIDDLEWARE_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"f9dcd4df884b74d53c1bbd85ef8b7bad58635e161c8e103997eed823ec32dcc1","bytes":4993,"section":"116","original_title":"SECTION 116 — Middleware Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A versioned middleware contract with supported patterns, interfaces, compatibility, security, observability, failure, recovery, performance, and ownership.","original_applicability":"Applies to brokers, RPC layers, service meshes, transaction managers, serializers, workflow engines, caches, configuration services, and shared libraries.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-04-01","REQ-05-01","REQ-05-04","REQ-06-01","REQ-07-01","REQ-08-01","REQ-20-01","REQ-21-03","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Common record and IPC contracts connect independently responsible application components. Specify actual identities, ordering/delivery, errors, retry/idempotency, backpressure, transactions, compatibility and consumer ownership. Test poison input, duplicates, delay/reorder, loss, replay, overload, partial work and recovery. Framing or delivery alone proves neither peer authenticity nor completed effects.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/117_APPLICATION_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/117_APPLICATION_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"bcd6e57670e9b6cc21ff0cf19fcbaf7d677a46590f736462ab3fc188714d1573","bytes":5269,"section":"117","original_title":"SECTION 117 — Application Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An application baseline with behavior, interfaces, data, configuration, dependencies, tests, accessibility, security, deployment, support, recovery, and retirement evidence.","original_applicability":"Applies to application design, implementation, configuration, integration, testing, release, support, modernization, migration, and retirement.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-00-01","REQ-03-01","REQ-04-01","REQ-09-01","REQ-12-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-31-01","REQ-32-01","REQ-32-04","REQ-29-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"CETA must deliver actual local conversation/work/memory/model/recovery outcomes in one coherent native product. Trace required journeys through code, data, interfaces, controls, errors, accessibility, release and support. Test denied, duplicate, degraded, migration and recovery paths. Preserve local user data and historical work. No isolated contract fixture or deployment status establishes exact user acceptance.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/118_FRONTEND_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/118_FRONTEND_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"8e46d4638665a8761252c603b83d1082233ccc5015031171f67a0cf4a9337838","bytes":5610,"section":"118","original_title":"SECTION 118 — Frontend Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A versioned frontend contract covering journeys, state, rendering, input, accessibility, localization, permissions, performance, errors, telemetry, offline or degraded behavior, tests, and release evidence.","original_applicability":"Applies to web, client, mobile, embedded, terminal, and rendered user or operator interfaces, including state, interaction, accessibility, and client-side integration.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-01","REQ-05-01","REQ-09-01","REQ-10-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-20-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-32-01","REQ-32-03","REQ-32-04","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The required PySide6 client is a user-control surface with states, input, local data and service interactions. Keep draft/client/cache/rendered state distinct from committed service authority; enforce approval and effects in the kernel/broker. Verify keyboard, assistive access, focus, scaling, localization, stale callbacks, denied access, slow/degraded/offline and recovery behavior. Screenshots cannot prove usability or accessibility.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/119_BACKEND_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/119_BACKEND_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"6a9589be1eaa100b6d5adbedad985c8b1e71c152c058c6a9ce5a9e15a126ed1a","bytes":5028,"section":"119","original_title":"SECTION 119 — Backend Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A versioned backend contract covering APIs, processes, data, authorization, validation, transactions, observability, scaling, failure, recovery, tests, release, and retirement.","original_applicability":"Applies to services, server applications, workers, jobs, APIs, domain logic, data access, and backend configuration.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-04","REQ-07-01","REQ-08-01","REQ-16-04","REQ-18-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-20-01","REQ-21-03","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-31-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The store/kernel/supervisor/broker responsibilities are backend service boundaries even in an offline Windows product. Implement server/service-side identity, current authority, validation, transactions, jobs, resource/error bounds, migrations and observability. Test concurrent, denied, duplicate, partial, failed-dependency and restore paths. No HTTP/cloud backend or hidden provider is required; UI success cannot certify a committed external outcome.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/120_FULL_STACK_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/120_FULL_STACK_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"ed1aee6ec93593afaa826fe1b0b50c1ccac09968a2394e041fb0e4769181fac3","bytes":4894,"section":"120","original_title":"SECTION 120 — Full-Stack Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A traceable end-to-end baseline connecting journey, client, backend, data, dependencies, security, tests, release, runtime, recovery, and retirement.","original_applicability":"Applies when one work item or team owns material behavior across two or more application layers or when an end-to-end outcome crosses frontend, backend, data, or operations.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-04","REQ-04-01","REQ-04-04","REQ-05-01","REQ-05-04","REQ-07-01","REQ-20-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-31-01","REQ-32-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-41-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01"],"decision_reason":"Mandatory end-to-end cycles cross native client, supervisor, context/model, kernel, store, broker and independent observation. Bind compatible versions, shared scope/request/effect identities, exact data ownership, correlation and recovery. Test stale clients, contract mismatch, double submission, denied authority, partial effects, offline recovery, migrations and accessibility. Layer-local green tests do not prove the full product.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/121_WEB_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/121_WEB_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"455d7430b4730e60e6b078093bd32b7d11e70dafabfd48e8a29b38f2df09373c","bytes":5116,"section":"121","original_title":"SECTION 121 — Web Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A versioned web baseline with routes, rendering, content, APIs, state, security, accessibility, compatibility, performance, observability, deployment, recovery, and retirement evidence.","original_applicability":"Applies to websites, web apps, browser APIs, server-rendered or client-rendered applications, web delivery, and web-specific configuration.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-01","REQ-06-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-20-01","REQ-21-03","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-33-03","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"REQ-33-03 explicitly includes browser and network-service adapters; this does not change the native local-first product into a website. For an enabled web adapter, pin actual provider/browser/route/origin/session/cache/content/API behavior and scope. Verify authorization, injection, stale caches, lost network, denied access and recovery; require exact action authority before sends/publication. No public site, server stack, session credentials or browser profile was read or created here.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/122_DESKTOP_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/122_DESKTOP_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"68f27c02ff5e37d1862aa86dcf2ca594d0536854a9ffd9ab52e9ecb52e2ed06f","bytes":5076,"section":"122","original_title":"SECTION 122 — Desktop Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A versioned desktop contract covering supported hosts, local data, permissions, offline behavior, updates, compatibility, security, accessibility, diagnostics, recovery, and retirement.","original_applicability":"Applies to desktop GUI, tray, background, command-line, workstation, and local agent software.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-01","REQ-07-01","REQ-21-01","REQ-21-03","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-31-01","REQ-32-01","REQ-32-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-03","REQ-38-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The explicit delivery target is a native Windows x64 desktop application with user-owned local data and offline operation. Qualify selected hosts, least privilege, local storage/IPC/devices, accessible interaction, crash/restore, interrupted updates, signed distribution and safe uninstall. Preserve user data, credentials and evidence through migration and retirement. Successful installation is separate from safe update/recovery; actual installed qualification remains unrun.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/123_MOBILE_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/123_MOBILE_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"7696c4fe1c7e018f9cc3c1853f00a87ace702548e811fa56b8065ee180368cdb","bytes":7217,"section":"123","original_title":"SECTION 123 - Mobile Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"NOT_APPLICABLE","implementation_status":"NOT_APPLICABLE","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An approved mobile engineering baseline with platform scope, supported devices and versions, user journeys, offline and recovery behavior, release controls, evidence, ownership, and handoff conditions.","original_applicability":"Applies when software runs on phones, tablets, wearables, mobile-connected devices, or mobile-specific services and the design depends on mobile hardware, operating-system APIs, app stores, sensors, notifications, intermittent connectivity, or mobile user journeys.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-01","REQ-04-01","REQ-33-03","REQ-36-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The selected product is Windows x64 desktop; no phone/tablet/wearable client, mobile-specific service or mobile device adapter has been selected in the supplied component/work-package inventory. Do not create a mobile app/store release, phone permission policy or unsupported mobile coverage. General offline/data/privacy/recovery duties remain mandatory through desktop/native contracts. REQ-33-03 device lanes remain open. Reopen this decision before any actual mobile client/device-specific workflow, mobile data consequence, target or support claim.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/124_CROSS_PLATFORM_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/124_CROSS_PLATFORM_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"baa5b24b3ed4b6b6ef386a1629ff699a9affbb44c2ffb01ae4a819faedc801f5","bytes":6377,"section":"124","original_title":"SECTION 124 - Cross-Platform Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A cross-platform baseline with shared contracts, explicit platform variations, parity decisions, build reproducibility, compatibility evidence, ownership, release sequencing, and safe divergence rules.","original_applicability":"Applies when a shared codebase, framework, component system, generated client, shared service, or common release serves two or more platforms or device families.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-01","REQ-03-03","REQ-04-01","REQ-05-01","REQ-06-01","REQ-21-05","REQ-24-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The same application contracts cross Python and the locked native Rust infrastructure; Windows-specific enforcement and other-platform reference behavior must remain distinct. Test comparable semantic/error/canonicalization scenarios across actual selected runtimes; bind versions, targets, dependencies and allowed differences. Existing serializer agreement is bounded historical evidence. Do not infer macOS/Linux/mobile support, native UI parity, distributed authority or installed qualification from shared code or compilation.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/125_NATIVE_APPLICATION_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/125_NATIVE_APPLICATION_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"e7a78a143f655024ab0ac71428baede99b10c3913f28425ad7a8b1f20f4564e8","bytes":6391,"section":"125","original_title":"SECTION 125 - Native Application Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An approved native baseline with platform contracts, lifecycle states, permissions, hardware use, accessibility, security, performance, build and signing provenance, release evidence, support, and retirement conditions.","original_applicability":"Applies to applications, agents, services, extensions, or device software intentionally implemented against a specific OS, runtime, hardware, or native distribution channel.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-01","REQ-03-03","REQ-21-01","REQ-21-02","REQ-21-03","REQ-23-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-32-04","REQ-35-02","REQ-38-03","REQ-38-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"CETA deliberately uses native Windows/PySide6 behavior and a narrow native helper where actual enforcement requires it. Version actual OS/SDK/API/driver/binary/signing identities, handles, permissions, background behavior and callbacks. Verify API availability, denial, interruption, accessible interaction, secure storage, IPC, upgrade, offline and recovery on declared hosts. Production signing/distribution, privileged installation and device effects retain their exact authority gates.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/126_BROWSER_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/126_BROWSER_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"7a8e93087d49c506ef02391d9b6eb8a35a545a2aabcc1a01c97d831f151b02ef","bytes":6417,"section":"126","original_title":"SECTION 126 - Browser Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A browser engineering baseline with supported engines and versions, web contracts, progressive behavior, security and privacy controls, accessibility, performance, compatibility evidence, deployment identity, and recovery paths.","original_applicability":"Applies to web applications, browser clients, extensions, workers, WebAssembly, browser APIs, rendering, client storage, service workers, and browser-specific user or operator journeys.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-06-02","REQ-11-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-20-01","REQ-21-03","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-33-03","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The required manifested browser lane has browser-specific identity, origin, permission, state and compatibility consequences. Select and qualify actual engine/version/provider, origins, navigation, assets, cookies/storage/workers/cache and APIs only where used. Prevent untrusted page/client validation from granting effects or disclosing data; test injection, stale context, failed scripts, denied permissions and engine differences. No extension, web frontend, profile, cookies or browser credentials were accessed here.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/127_EXTENSION_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/127_EXTENSION_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"8803bf138ed8a7d328099ea3a1238a3bd6ac92e6f8f61023cc1e74395346462f","bytes":5621,"section":"127","original_title":"SECTION 127 - Extension Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An extension baseline with host contract, permissions, trust boundary, activation, compatibility, update, uninstall, evidence, owner, and recovery conditions.","original_applicability":"Applies to plugins, browser extensions, editor extensions, add-ons, modules, integrations, and package-based augmentations loaded by a host.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-03","REQ-14-01","REQ-17-01","REQ-17-02","REQ-17-03","REQ-19-01","REQ-21-03","REQ-22-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Approved capability/template/adapter registration augments CETA under explicit contracts rather than arbitrary plugin import. Bind actual host/capability/package/source/version, activation, permissions, APIs, resources, data, compatibility, disablement and retirement. Verify hostile messages, permission revocation, host failure, update/rollback and independent disable controls. No marketplace/browser extension or unrestricted dynamic module loader is mandated; unsupported augmentation is rejected.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/128_API_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/128_API_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"3762db3a227e5ce936ad884f0eb9c4654b53eab001114ec79e59e10eaed63c37","bytes":5792,"section":"128","original_title":"SECTION 128 - API Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A versioned API baseline with purpose, consumers, schemas, errors, security, limits, observability, compatibility, test evidence, owner, change policy, and retirement path.","original_applicability":"Applies to REST, GraphQL, RPC, command, query, event, file, SDK, internal, partner, or machine interfaces that cross a responsibility or trust boundary.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-04-01","REQ-05-04","REQ-06-01","REQ-06-02","REQ-08-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-20-01","REQ-21-03","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Internal commands/events/queries, broker ports and modality adapters cross responsibility and trust boundaries. Specify exact caller/peer authority, schemas, errors, limits, ordering/replay/idempotency, deadlines, compatibility and consumers. Validate before dispatch and revalidate current authority/state at effect admission. Test abuse, denied calls, duplicates, partial outcomes and compensation. No UI/chat route bypasses controls; successful response does not prove observed effect.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/129_INTEGRATION_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/129_INTEGRATION_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"8330e7b350fd7ce362c306c9cc9bd18e1eba3473dabf90c6d5972a51b03d9433","bytes":5637,"section":"129","original_title":"SECTION 129 - Integration Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An integration baseline with participants, contracts, mappings, ownership, ordering, reliability, security, observability, reconciliation, migration, and retirement conditions.","original_applicability":"Applies whenever two or more systems, services, teams, suppliers, devices, data stores, or processes exchange information, commands, events, or responsibility.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-04","REQ-05-01","REQ-05-04","REQ-06-01","REQ-07-01","REQ-20-01","REQ-20-03","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-31-01","REQ-33-03","REQ-19-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"One operating cycle exchanges state, evidence and commands among scoped services, model workers and manifested external adapters. Identify actual source/target/owner, transformation/version, ordering, retry, deduplication, credentials, dead letters and reconciliation authority. Preserve unmatched, duplicate, delayed, failed and corrected evidence. Reconcile against actual authoritative readback and admit compensation separately; delivery does not establish business completion.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/130_MICROSERVICES_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/130_MICROSERVICES_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"f032ac23b119fdb97cbde2c5c845bf448fb80f2e69c65e4eae6decec68a65e9a","bytes":5770,"section":"130","original_title":"SECTION 130 - Microservices Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A service baseline with bounded contexts, ownership, APIs and events, data authority, deployment, failure, scaling, security, observability, compatibility, and retirement evidence.","original_applicability":"Applies when a solution uses multiple independently deployed services, service teams, containers, queues, or provider components with separate lifecycles.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-03","REQ-03-04","REQ-05-01","REQ-05-02","REQ-05-04","REQ-07-01","REQ-08-01","REQ-21-03","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The prescribed isolated processes/services/providers have distinct authority, data ownership, supervised lifecycle and version boundaries. Keep shared contracts, compatible versions, one state/effect owner per scope, timeouts, bounded retries, tracing, secret separation and recovery explicit. Test dependency loss, partial work, deployment/version mismatch and retirement. This imposes no cloud cluster, container platform, service per table, additional product or independent data authority.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/131_DISTRIBUTED_SYSTEMS_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/131_DISTRIBUTED_SYSTEMS_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"bf6f8f5bb61246e7af897148debedf0714c8609ae33c46a1d30d1f73217a4ad7","bytes":5336,"section":"131","original_title":"SECTION 131 - Distributed Systems Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A distributed-systems baseline with ownership, consistency, timing, partition, identity, coordination, observability, recovery, and evidence boundaries.","original_applicability":"Applies to distributed storage, services, actors, queues, clusters, replicated state, multi-region systems, and federated operations.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-04","REQ-07-01","REQ-08-01","REQ-20-01","REQ-26-01","REQ-26-02","REQ-26-03","REQ-26-04","REQ-27-03","REQ-27-04","REQ-30-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Required isolated execution and CBCC span independently responsible processes/domains with freshness, replay and divergence constraints. Specify actual topology, actors, trusted domains, state authority, timing, messages, failure/partition model, consistency and recovery. Test duplicate/reorder/skew/stale-node/authority outage and reconciled effects. Local tests under one host/admin cannot establish independent root domains or compromise resilience; quorum protected-object release remains qualified separately.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/132_REAL_TIME_SYSTEMS_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/132_REAL_TIME_SYSTEMS_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"596efcee8c611aefe38ac5d788b26dbb53f2c3feb6746fc46b1436c94f8575bb","bytes":5331,"section":"132","original_title":"SECTION 132 - Real-Time Systems Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A real-time baseline with timing classes, workloads, clocks, scheduling, resource budgets, safety margins, evidence, degradation, and recovery ownership.","original_applicability":"Applies to hard, firm, or soft real-time software, control, communications, trading, telemetry, interactive, embedded, or operational systems.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-08-01","REQ-08-02","REQ-08-04","REQ-10-01","REQ-18-01","REQ-23-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-33-03","REQ-34-01","REQ-34-03","REQ-34-04","REQ-35-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Permit freshness, cancellation, interactive response, resource leases and selected physical actions have material timing consequences. Declare actual timing class, clock/boot/synchronization, workload, deadline, admission, priority and safe overload behavior. Measure distributions, misses and relevant worst cases; test inversion, clock discontinuity, late outputs and independent stop/status. No hard-real-time or physical-safety guarantee follows from average latency or current unit fixtures.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/133_HIGH_PERFORMANCE_COMPUTING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/133_HIGH_PERFORMANCE_COMPUTING.txt","sha256":"e2d275a69dc26384026bd61cf22fcb4817a09aa611514209c9669ea1ef6d3a7a","bytes":5462,"section":"133","original_title":"SECTION 133 - High-Performance Computing","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An HPC baseline with workload, correctness, resource allocation, scaling, performance evidence, cost and energy limits, reproducibility, operations, and recovery.","original_applicability":"Applies to clusters, supercomputers, accelerators, batch systems, large simulations, analytics, rendering, training, and throughput-critical services.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-02","REQ-18-01","REQ-23-01","REQ-23-02","REQ-24-01","REQ-34-01","REQ-34-02","REQ-34-04","REQ-35-02","REQ-37-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Actual GGUF model execution and CPU/GPU placement have substantial memory, latency, acceleration and resource-admission implications. Pin model/runtime/template/tokenizer/configuration, hardware/driver/precision, workload, baseline, resource and energy assumptions. Qualify correctness and semantic quality separately from throughput, liveness and latency; retain failed samples. No cluster, training budget, accelerator claim or captured benchmark was invented; historical quality failures require real new qualification.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/134_PARALLEL_COMPUTING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/134_PARALLEL_COMPUTING.txt","sha256":"0d986f4aae8820c1925e520063ff1968be98a6f6fc0c646d2c7efd72a591d220","bytes":5244,"section":"134","original_title":"SECTION 134 - Parallel Computing","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A parallel-computing baseline with decomposition, data ownership, synchronization, race controls, scalability, reproducibility, resource limits, and recovery evidence.","original_applicability":"Applies to multithreaded, vectorized, GPU, actor, task, map-reduce, distributed, and concurrent algorithms or services.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-05-01","REQ-07-01","REQ-08-01","REQ-10-01","REQ-18-01","REQ-20-01","REQ-21-03","REQ-30-01","REQ-32-04","REQ-34-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"CETA runs concurrent native interaction, observations, preparation, model work and effect/recovery responsibilities. Specify shared-state ownership, memory visibility, ordering, worker/generation identities, leases, fencing, budgets, backpressure and cancellation. Test races, deadlocks, varied schedules/worker counts, late callbacks, partial output and recovery. Preserve nondeterministic evidence; speedup does not justify changed results or duplicate effects.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/135_SCIENTIFIC_COMPUTING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/135_SCIENTIFIC_COMPUTING.txt","sha256":"665636c2ab2f203c5f1192a23a687796defc522c78c6e96fd291d311447f7d28","bytes":5416,"section":"135","original_title":"SECTION 135 - Scientific Computing","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"SUPPORTING","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A scientific-computing baseline with model purpose, equations or algorithms, inputs, units, numerical methods, uncertainty, validation, reproducible environment, and decision limits.","original_applicability":"Applies to computational science, numerical analysis, research software, scientific workflows, experiment analysis, and domain simulations.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-13-03","REQ-14-01","REQ-15-01","REQ-24-01","REQ-34-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Evaluation, predictions and domain-qualified work may use numerical/research methods; the current product does not specify a scientific solver or universal physical model. For an actual scientific claim bind question, domain authority, equations/model, units, data, precision, seed, method, environment, validation and interpretation limits. Preserve failed runs and sensitivity. Generic software tests do not establish scientific truth; no dataset, publication mandate, numerical tolerance or domain acceptance was invented.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/136_SIMULATION_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/136_SIMULATION_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"51f8a1e18b8dc95f7daf4d9a18571b88dc4fad03c91f965e20c5775df4ee1bff","bytes":5261,"section":"136","original_title":"SECTION 136 - Simulation Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A simulation baseline with purpose, fidelity, boundaries, assumptions, parameters, scenarios, calibration, validation, uncertainty, controls, and decision-use limits.","original_applicability":"Applies to discrete-event, continuous, agent-based, Monte Carlo, training, operational, design, and scenario simulations.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-14-01","REQ-15-01","REQ-15-02","REQ-15-03","REQ-19-01","REQ-20-01","REQ-24-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"REQ-15 requires isolated proposal staging and supported tests with predictions compared to outcomes. Bind actual purpose, source/model/scenario, time, parameters, fidelity, environmental assumptions and uncertainty. Preserve exact candidate bytes, mismatches and negative runs. Qualify host differences and actual adapters before promotion; simulation cannot confer authority or replace real observed effects, hardware safety or model quality.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/137_DIGITAL_TWIN_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/137_DIGITAL_TWIN_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"f817f19751f62e797cab925d6ca2437bc82afb03365ef8c2180a29b754e1a87a","bytes":5478,"section":"137","original_title":"SECTION 137 - Digital Twin Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A digital-twin baseline with counterpart identity, synchronization, provenance, fidelity, authority, safety boundaries, commands, model drift, and retirement conditions.","original_applicability":"Applies to physical assets, facilities, processes, infrastructure, devices, organizations, or environments represented and linked to a digital system.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-06-02","REQ-07-01","REQ-08-01","REQ-12-01","REQ-14-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-20-01","REQ-24-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-33-03","REQ-35-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"CETA's observed world/task/resource models represent actual counterparts for planning, freshness and supported device actions. Bind actual counterpart/source identity, time, provenance, measurement versus inference, calibration, synchronization, uncertainty and permitted use. Reject stale/missing/contradictory state for dependent actions; independently read back effects. No physical twin fleet, sensor quality or digital representation is proof of physical state or command authority.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/138_GAME_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/138_GAME_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"d700e74bb61652731f90f2a7197f8aa33c95b389ef0057c289a25b6acad2e771","bytes":5688,"section":"138","original_title":"SECTION 138 - Game Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"NOT_APPLICABLE","implementation_status":"NOT_APPLICABLE","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A game-engineering baseline with authoritative state, client behavior, content and asset provenance, performance, accessibility, privacy, anti-abuse, release, telemetry, recovery, and retirement rules.","original_applicability":"Applies to games, interactive simulations, game services, engines, clients, servers, multiplayer systems, tools, and live content platforms.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-01","REQ-04-01","REQ-15-01","REQ-32-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The supplied native conversation/work system and bounded proposal staging have no player/mechanics/levels/economy/multiplayer/anti-cheat/live-game requirement. Master Volume V prohibits adding machinery solely from topic names. Keep real state authority, input, timing, replay, access, asset rights and recovery obligations under runtime/application/simulation/media contracts. Do not add gameplay, purchases, moderation, game engine or playable world. Reopen before any actual game-like simulation/game product, player outcome or distribution/live-game commitment.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/139_GRAPHICS_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/139_GRAPHICS_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"cd68dca2a322c0578213da8e5e765de0e2dd6f9189d572be016403e6d5055f56","bytes":5184,"section":"139","original_title":"SECTION 139 - Graphics Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A graphics baseline with scene, asset, shader, rendering, device, color, performance, accessibility, security, build, evidence, and recovery contracts.","original_applicability":"Applies to 2D or 3D graphics, real-time visualization, game graphics, UI rendering, GPU compute, asset pipelines, and display output.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-01","REQ-24-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-32-01","REQ-32-04","REQ-33-01","REQ-33-02","REQ-34-04","REQ-35-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"CETA produces native UI visual output and interprets explicitly selected screen content; GPU/display failures can affect required workflows. Bind actual rendered content/assets/rights, framework/device/API/color/scaling configuration, resources, accessible semantics and fallback. Test malformed assets, memory pressure, device loss and real assistive access. No custom 3D scene/shader engine is required; pixel similarity or polished visuals do not prove meaning or usability.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/140_RENDERING_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/140_RENDERING_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"041be8db53533b41da35e058a0aa8cd8bb8b90351275ba0338ae9e7f45367c45","bytes":4918,"section":"140","original_title":"SECTION 140 - Rendering Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A rendering baseline with pipeline stages, resource ownership, output contract, device support, performance, fallback, evidence, and recovery.","original_applicability":"Applies to raster, vector, 3D, offline, real-time, server-side, browser, GPU, display, and visualization renderers.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-01","REQ-08-01","REQ-10-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-32-01","REQ-32-03","REQ-32-04","REQ-33-01","REQ-34-01","REQ-34-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Actual native rendering must preserve control/state visibility, responsiveness, access and recovery under supported device conditions. Specify real pipeline/output/resource ownership and frame/memory budgets; test scaling/color, stale output, ordering, UI-thread blocking, malformed content, device loss and software fallback. Keep source-state and capture lineage; do not claim accessible controls or deadline compliance from snapshots or mean frame rate.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/141_ANIMATION_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/141_ANIMATION_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"1f98348c56ac6ba150349da03cc73ee12c292949385da39ae088c8c4426b2adb","bytes":4866,"section":"141","original_title":"SECTION 141 - Animation Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A baseline with animation state, timing, assets, controls, transitions, cancellation, reduced-motion behavior, device support, evidence, and lifecycle.","original_applicability":"Applies to UI, games, film, visualization, avatars, motion graphics, simulations, and procedural or generated animation.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-08-01","REQ-10-01","REQ-18-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-32-01","REQ-32-03","REQ-32-04","REQ-34-04","REQ-29-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Native state transitions/loading/stream displays have time-dependent interaction; any motion must remain optional and accessible. Define actual triggers, timings, interruption, cancellation, reduced motion and static/low-resource alternatives. Verify keyboard, late frames, input and state consistency. Do not create avatars, film/game animation or mandatory motion; animation completion cannot grant approval, commit state or hide an independent stop/status path.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/142_AUDIO_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/142_AUDIO_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"808b35409ecf7683e59b4b159c580da18dd4db38538c04e3a8208da84222efbd","bytes":5163,"section":"142","original_title":"SECTION 142 - Audio Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A sound baseline with sources, assets, mixing, spatialization, timing, device support, captions or alternatives, privacy, evidence, and recovery.","original_applicability":"Applies to games, applications, devices, media, voice interfaces, spatial audio, alerts, synthesis, recording, and audio pipelines.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-06-02","REQ-08-01","REQ-11-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-32-04","REQ-33-01","REQ-33-02","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The required local voice lane captures/processes or produces audio under the shared modality and privacy contracts. Bind actual source/device/session, consent, samples/formats/channels/levels, timing, source/derivative provenance, uncertainty, retention and cancellation. Test mute, device loss, malformed media, offline, captions/text alternatives and deletion. No recording, microphone access, unsafe alert/level or publication occurred; recognition and fidelity do not establish consent or comprehension.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/143_VIDEO_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/143_VIDEO_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"6d01824c15d3d474cf644bf6b055cd32330a837a474041edb152160a84caa7ec","bytes":5194,"section":"143","original_title":"SECTION 143 - Video Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A video baseline with source, rights, codecs, timing, quality, captions, delivery, storage, processing, evidence, recovery, and retirement.","original_applicability":"Applies to capture, editing, encoding, playback, conferencing, surveillance, broadcast, computer vision input, and video delivery systems.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-06-02","REQ-08-01","REQ-11-01","REQ-11-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-32-04","REQ-33-01","REQ-33-02","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The required selected-screen lane can process time-varying screen frames and computer-vision input; it is not unbounded surveillance. Bind actual selected source/region/session, consent, frame time/rate/resolution/color, transformations, storage/access/retention, uncertainty and source-to-interpretation lineage. Verify stale/dropped/malformed frames, timing, cancellation and alternative text/access. No camera, conferencing, publication or capture scope was activated; clear frames or detections do not prove consequential facts.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/144_MEDIA_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/144_MEDIA_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"fe6dc7de69fbaa5e7120afeebb0895d36e86e597c5e4b585574c7062d2c90ea7","bytes":5098,"section":"144","original_title":"SECTION 144 - Media Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A media baseline with asset identity, rights, provenance, synchronization, formats, accessibility, delivery, quality, security, evidence, and lifecycle.","original_applicability":"Applies to media repositories, production, editing, publishing, digital experiences, asset pipelines, archives, and multi-format delivery.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-06-02","REQ-11-02","REQ-12-01","REQ-12-04","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-29-03","REQ-30-01","REQ-31-01","REQ-33-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Conversation/work attachments and text/image/audio/screen interpretations create scoped media source/derivative relationships. Catalog actual source/assets/rights/consent, hashes, formats, transformations, tool/model, timings, access and lifecycle. Preserve originals and corrections while bounding storage and authorized derivative/cache/index/backup retention. No licensed dataset, generated media asset, public delivery or deletion result was invented.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/145_STREAMING_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/145_STREAMING_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"7d29e43c06a43722fbbaef351909dc9cafc2b5cc2d069e5d52a00029e072a3ac","bytes":5182,"section":"145","original_title":"SECTION 145 - Streaming Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A streaming baseline with source, segments, manifests, timing, authorization, adaptation, buffering, observability, accessibility, evidence, and retirement.","original_applicability":"Applies to live, on-demand, interactive, event, media, telemetry, and data streaming systems.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-06-01","REQ-06-02","REQ-08-01","REQ-10-01","REQ-18-01","REQ-21-03","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-33-01","REQ-34-04","REQ-35-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"CETA's streamed model output, event observations and time-based voice/screen lanes have ordering, time, freshness, cancellation and resource contracts. Bind actual stream/source/request/worker/generation, sequence/clock, access, buffer and deadline/resource limits. Test stalls, reordering, duplicates, late output, reconnect, backpressure, cancellation and partial records. Preserve text/status alternatives; no CDN, DRM, broadcast audience, external recording or streaming provider is required.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/146_SEARCH_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/146_SEARCH_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"3d4e42789dd0eaab71a5948f4574fea5eace8c8e8ed8e017781e228a2903ab18","bytes":5374,"section":"146","original_title":"SECTION 146 - Search Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A search baseline with sources, indexing, schemas, ranking, permissions, freshness, recall and precision evidence, explanations, abuse controls, and retirement.","original_applicability":"Applies to keyword, semantic, federated, enterprise, media, code, geospatial, log, and AI-assisted search systems.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-07-01","REQ-11-02","REQ-11-04","REQ-12-01","REQ-12-02","REQ-12-04","REQ-13-01","REQ-16-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-35-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"REQ-11 and REQ-12 require selective current scoped history/memory/evidence retrieval for context and user inspection. Bind actual source/index/query/user/scope/policy versions, freshness, citations, language and correction/deletion propagation. Enforce access before retrieval/ranking/cache/disclosure; test cross-scope denial, prompt injection, stale corrections, no results, source loss and restore. Evaluate real recall/precision/task outcomes; rank and citation presence do not prove truth.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/147_RECOMMENDATION_SYSTEMS_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/147_RECOMMENDATION_SYSTEMS_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"19b68d440075284fb50de685ca5d43c775cc349001c672a16eb76df3a0b2ff52","bytes":5507,"section":"147","original_title":"SECTION 147 - Recommendation Systems Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A recommendation baseline with objectives, candidates, ranking, feedback, permissions, explanations, evaluation, controls, drift, and lifecycle ownership.","original_applicability":"Applies to content, products, people, routes, actions, alerts, jobs, treatments, learning, personalization, and automated prioritization systems.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-09-04","REQ-11-02","REQ-12-01","REQ-13-02","REQ-13-03","REQ-13-05","REQ-14-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-24-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"CETA ranks plans/actions/context and provides user-controlled Companion recommendations without turning suggestions into approved commitments. Bind candidate source/permissions, objective/constraints, policy/model/context, uncertainty, exclusions, feedback and exposure evidence. Preserve nonpersonalized choice, override, appeal and meaningful alternatives. Test unsafe candidates, proxy objectives, drift, feedback loops and hidden preference changes; agreement, clicks or engagement cannot prove benefit or create authority.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/148_GEOGRAPHIC_INFORMATION_SYSTEMS.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/148_GEOGRAPHIC_INFORMATION_SYSTEMS.txt","sha256":"8661e2c6b959b97b26c676cf23aac21ceb3852ddbe27a04cb944cda987cf308d","bytes":5394,"section":"148","original_title":"SECTION 148 - Geographic Information Systems","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"SUPPORTING","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A GIS baseline with spatial reference, data lineage, accuracy, access, analysis, visualization, update, interoperability, evidence, and recovery rules.","original_applicability":"Applies to mapping, geocoding, remote sensing, routing, spatial analytics, cadastral, environmental, logistics, asset, and location-aware systems.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-06-02","REQ-08-01","REQ-14-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-33-03","REQ-35-02","REQ-37-04","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"A future selected device/physical adapter may need actual geographic/spatial reference; the present inventory defines no GIS map/layer/geocoder/routing service or geographic support claim. Before actual geographic use identify counterpart/source authority, coordinates/projection/units, timestamp, accuracy/uncertainty, privacy zones, transformation and physical consequences. Screen pixels are not geographic positions. No real location was collected, map inferred, official boundary adopted or GIS product created; reopen direct clauses on actual location-dependent work.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/149_BLOCKCHAIN_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/149_BLOCKCHAIN_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"c958849b60151fa26a219011b910b4487d0b9302a327b45531b4110f25c38f87","bytes":5522,"section":"149","original_title":"SECTION 149 - Blockchain Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"NOT_APPLICABLE","implementation_status":"NOT_APPLICABLE","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A blockchain baseline with network purpose, consensus, assets, keys, transaction semantics, privacy, governance, observability, recovery, upgrade, and retirement controls.","original_applicability":"Applies to permissioned or public ledgers, blockchain infrastructure, wallets, nodes, tokens, proofs, on-chain records, and ledger-connected applications.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-01","REQ-04-01","REQ-26-01","REQ-26-03","REQ-26-04","REQ-27-01","REQ-27-02","REQ-27-03","REQ-36-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The master Volume V instruction excludes topic-driven blockchain additions. SPEC-26 specifies a quorum protected-object protocol, not token assets, blockchain consensus, a wallet or on-chain ledger. Preserve canonical transcripts, replay, quorum classes, independent authority domains, confidential object-key lineage, audit and compensation under SPEC-26/27. Hashes and signatures remain neither secret entropy nor truth. No public/permissioned chain, mempool, validator consensus, fees or token transfer is mandated. Reopen on an actual ledger/network/asset/finality requirement.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/150_SMART_CONTRACT_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/150_SMART_CONTRACT_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"e42c5f83d6b1f8e65d8a1c4a5b31e2ff9995327d38cb529feb86650a9b7965fc","bytes":5739,"section":"150","original_title":"SECTION 150 - Smart Contract Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"NOT_APPLICABLE","implementation_status":"NOT_APPLICABLE","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":5,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_05_Software_Systems_through_Smart_Contracts.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A smart-contract baseline with specification, invariants, authority, keys, interfaces, gas or resource limits, upgrade policy, verification, monitoring, and compensation path.","original_applicability":"Applies to on-chain programs, tokens, escrow, DAOs, governance, automated settlement, wallets, or ledger-connected contracts.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-04-01","REQ-16-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-20-01","REQ-26-03","REQ-27-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The specified kernel and CBCC authorization protocol have no chain address, ledger VM, gas, escrow/token/DAO or on-chain bytecode deployment. Master Volume V prohibits topic-driven smart-contract machinery. Keep required policy invariants, exact signature/transcript binding, key custody, replay, bounded resources, partial effects and separately admitted compensation under kernel/effect/cryptographic contracts. This assessment does not exempt cryptographic signing or irreversible-effect controls. Reopen before actual ledger-connected executable settlement, assets, chain/VM/address or on-chain deployment.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_11.md","handoff/volume_v_reconciliation_20261007_11.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/151_DATABASE_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/151_DATABASE_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"f00062cf9624fbcf9df3bb1f0a75320b69a192f07e31495d079dffe38df87453","bytes":7272,"section":"151","original_title":"SECTION 151 — Database Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An approved database design with schemas, constraints, indexes, transactions, access paths, backup and restore behavior, operational ownership, lifecycle state, and bounded evidence.","original_applicability":"Apply when a database stores, transforms, serves, replicates, audits, or governs material data, or when schema, query, transaction, availability, or recovery behavior affects outcomes.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-07-01","REQ-07-02","REQ-07-03","REQ-07-04","REQ-07-05","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-30-03","REQ-31-01","REQ-31-02","REQ-31-04","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The required local authority store persists events, grants, intents, admissions and projections; database behavior directly controls CETA outcomes. Specify actual engine/library, schemas, constraints, indexes, isolation, serialized writes, durability and workload. Test concurrent/stale writes, injection/denied access, failed commits, power-loss recovery, actual backup restoration and migration equivalence. Account for payload, index and backup deletion. Query success or backup existence alone proves none of these.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/152_STORAGE_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/152_STORAGE_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"8b9f03f73696581fd7e4961aa782e45049121c1d5e7eecf57e5aafb4dd89d8ea","bytes":6765,"section":"152","original_title":"SECTION 152 — Storage Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A storage design covering media, namespaces, capacity, performance, durability, availability, access, encryption, lifecycle, backup, restore, portability, and disposal with owners and evidence.","original_applicability":"Apply when files, objects, blocks, volumes, caches, archives, backups, or physical media carry material data or service state.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-07-01","REQ-07-02","REQ-22-04","REQ-23-01","REQ-23-03","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-29-03","REQ-30-03","REQ-31-04","REQ-34-03","REQ-19-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"CETA stores user-authorized payloads, model assets, evidence, projections and recovery material on local storage. Inventory actual storage classes, locations, copies, sensitivity, quotas, permissions, encryption and lifecycle. Measure workload, failure, integrity, availability and portability on selected media/filesystems. Exercise actual restore and residual-copy deletion; redundancy, a vendor promise or a copied archive is not restoration or complete forgetting. No new provider or region is selected.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/153_DATA_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/153_DATA_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"231446ca67fbd88e5738f74705d11830f21a82090bd4848fe16d7f89916b9a74","bytes":6545,"section":"153","original_title":"SECTION 153 — Data Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A versioned data-flow design with source and destination contracts, pipelines, schedules, state, lineage, quality gates, idempotency, recovery, ownership, and evidence.","original_applicability":"Apply when data is ingested, transformed, enriched, joined, streamed, batched, exported, synchronized, or published across a material boundary.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-07-01","REQ-07-04","REQ-10-01","REQ-11-02","REQ-12-01","REQ-12-03","REQ-20-03","REQ-29-01","REQ-31-01","REQ-31-02","REQ-35-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Observation, retrieval, memory, projections, import and evaluation transform material data across product boundaries. Bind source/target, schema, transform, time window, offsets, ordering, lateness, deduplication, idempotency, dependencies and reconciliation. Preserve quarantine, loss, partial failure and correction records; exercise replay, backpressure, malformed input and recovery. A completed pipeline, checksum or sample does not prove complete or semantically correct data. Backfill and replay retain exact authority.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/154_DATA_MODELING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/154_DATA_MODELING.txt","sha256":"d7937df109cb9957b3012fdebb7552c8ac5d163d0dddd934fc6ff6fce0b24f29","bytes":6313,"section":"154","original_title":"SECTION 154 — Data Modeling","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"Conceptual, logical, and physical models with controlled mappings, definitions, ownership, constraints, variants, lineage, quality rules, change impact, and acceptance boundaries.","original_applicability":"Apply when data entities, events, relationships, schemas, identifiers, classifications, or transformations materially affect behavior or decisions.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-06-01","REQ-06-02","REQ-07-01","REQ-07-04","REQ-11-02","REQ-12-01","REQ-12-03","REQ-14-02","REQ-31-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The supplied canonical objects, memory/graph and migration require explicit models rather than interchangeable record shapes. Keep conceptual, logical and physical models distinct. Define actual entity/key/relationship/cardinality/null/unknown/valid-time/recorded-time/classification/source/owner semantics and mappings. Enforce constraints, compatibility, provenance and consumer validation. A diagram or syntactically valid record cannot establish canonical truth or grant authority.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/155_DATA_GOVERNANCE.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/155_DATA_GOVERNANCE.txt","sha256":"879c4ac16abdb62a92468a79510fc8b3429c49eb681a1d49904cf660bf45710a","bytes":5898,"section":"155","original_title":"SECTION 155 — Data Governance","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A data-governance operating model with accountable owners, classifications, policies, decision rights, exceptions, evidence, review cadence, and enforcement paths.","original_applicability":"Apply whenever data affects rights, decisions, safety, privacy, security, compliance, service, finance, models, records, or material operations.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-07-01","REQ-11-02","REQ-12-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-23-04","REQ-24-05","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-29-03","REQ-35-03","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"CETA handles conversations, files, preferences, embeddings, claims and operational evidence under exact user scope. Record source rights, purpose, owner, classification, access/sharing, expiry, retention, correction, deletion, exception, review and supersession. Enforce current controls and audit scope changes at source and derived boundaries. Technical access is not permission; no consent, lawful basis, permanent preference or cross-project bridge is inferred.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/156_DATA_QUALITY_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/156_DATA_QUALITY_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"10c60c40df11aa570081ad91c2e7d43f662ea87842ef3970ed7bad847f4b1a31","bytes":5604,"section":"156","original_title":"SECTION 156 — Data Quality Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"Quality dimensions, rules, thresholds, sampling, monitoring, ownership, quarantine, correction, reconciliation, evidence, and impact handling for each material data product.","original_applicability":"Apply when data informs decisions, automation, reporting, models, records, compliance, safety, service, or material operations.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-10-01","REQ-11-04","REQ-12-01","REQ-12-03","REQ-24-01","REQ-24-02","REQ-24-03","REQ-31-02","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Grounded context, memory, observations, migration and model evaluation depend on actual quality beyond schema validity. Declare population, dimensions, rule/version, thresholds, sampling, missingness, drift, bias, false positives/negatives, owners and consumer impact. Test invalid and incomplete data, quarantine, correction and quality regressions. Preserve failures; do not silently impute, lower criteria or relabel data as clean. Quality is distinct from uptime, confidence and model competence.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/157_DATA_INTEGRATION.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/157_DATA_INTEGRATION.txt","sha256":"3803974bf5090e6f781aa5eec10308d50052cce0b62c597d6e0a29b0e26cf661","bytes":5259,"section":"157","original_title":"SECTION 157 — Data Integration","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"Integration contracts, mappings, transport, timing, ordering, error, retry, reconciliation, lineage, ownership, compatibility, and recovery are explicit.","original_applicability":"Apply when data crosses a system, trust, domain, supplier, jurisdiction, protocol, or lifecycle boundary.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-05-04","REQ-06-01","REQ-10-01","REQ-11-02","REQ-12-03","REQ-20-03","REQ-29-03","REQ-31-01","REQ-33-01","REQ-33-03","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Typed records, modality adapters, legacy import and model/context interfaces integrate material sources and consumers. Bind actual source/consumer identities, versions, time windows, meanings, mappings, permissions and trust assumptions. Test contract mismatch, ordering, retry, duplicates, partial delivery, replay and independent reconciliation/compensation. Delivery does not prove semantic equivalence or completed outcome. No unrelated project data is transferred by matching names or accessible paths.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/158_DATA_MIGRATION.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/158_DATA_MIGRATION.txt","sha256":"119588bb92559f17c25197a7b215e09f76848611bc0a472e3c687afb37223145","bytes":5672,"section":"158","original_title":"SECTION 158 — Data Migration","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A migration plan with inventory, mapping, reconciliation, controls, rehearsal, cutover, coexistence, rollback or compensation, validation, communications, and retirement.","original_applicability":"Apply to material movement, conversion, consolidation, separation, modernization, provider change, schema change, region change, or retention transition.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-07-01","REQ-07-04","REQ-29-02","REQ-29-03","REQ-30-03","REQ-31-01","REQ-31-02","REQ-31-03","REQ-31-04","REQ-31-05","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The required rebuild includes discovered-schema import, genesis and a coherent cutover with historical uncertainty preserved. Inventory actual source/target schemas, mappings, unknown categories, coexistence, writers, checkpoints and idempotency. Rehearse verified snapshots; validate IDs, bytes, counts, hashes, relations, meaning and consumers. Preserve source, target and concurrent user work, residual copies and failures. Cutover requires quiescence, real restore, compatible rollback and explicit normal-data replacement authority; no live migration occurs now.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/159_DATA_WAREHOUSING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/159_DATA_WAREHOUSING.txt","sha256":"242433dc44cbc148421ea7f66c7a32b2287f943fe3c22125f9ba19ce19dfa1ea","bytes":5536,"section":"159","original_title":"SECTION 159 — Data Warehousing","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A warehouse model with source contracts, grain, dimensions, facts, history, refresh, quality, lineage, security, ownership, recovery, and lifecycle controls.","original_applicability":"Apply when historical, integrated, subject-oriented, or decision-support data is consolidated for reporting, analysis, compliance, or operations.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-07-03","REQ-07-04","REQ-09-01","REQ-12-03","REQ-24-03","REQ-29-01","REQ-32-01","REQ-32-03","REQ-35-01","REQ-35-03","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"CETA's canonical histories and evidence/status projections support owner decisions; this allocation concerns those views within the product. Define each actual historical analytical view's source, grain, window, metrics, denominator, history corrections, late data, freshness, permission, retention and reproducible query. Reconcile results with authoritative records and consumers. No separate enterprise warehouse or analytical platform is introduced; a query or dashboard cannot prove trusted history, complete coverage or a decision outcome.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/160_DATA_LAKE_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/160_DATA_LAKE_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"91066ccab0056bd170ccf8a741b49f28bec5a6a526c35836b8b87ce8d26d838d","bytes":5546,"section":"160","original_title":"SECTION 160 — Data Lake Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A lake-zone and catalog design covering ingestion, formats, schemas, metadata, access, isolation, quality, lineage, retention, recovery, and consumer contracts.","original_applicability":"Apply when varied structured, semi-structured, unstructured, streaming, experimental, or historical data is collected for authorized reuse.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-10-01","REQ-11-02","REQ-12-01","REQ-12-03","REQ-22-04","REQ-23-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-29-03","REQ-31-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The product holds authorized attachments, observations, model assets, outputs, memory and evidence in distinguishable lifecycle states. Inventory only declared collections, formats, schema/version, partition/classification, purpose, ownership, source-to-derived lineage, access, quality, quarantine, archive/backup and retention. Test discovery, stale/poisoned input, derived-copy revocation and deletion. A catalog or object count proves neither trust nor completeness. No whole-drive collection, universal raw retention or cloud lake is authorized.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/161_ANALYTICS_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/161_ANALYTICS_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"c619584d5ecf90d4d813617ed27b251cf25db057d19002ba469ff586c994fe43","bytes":5174,"section":"161","original_title":"SECTION 161 — Analytics Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"Versioned analytical models with metric definitions, lineage, tests, owners, freshness, access, documentation, deployment, monitoring, and recovery.","original_applicability":"Apply when reusable transformations, metrics, analytical models, semantic layers, or decision datasets are built or changed.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-07-04","REQ-24-02","REQ-24-03","REQ-24-04","REQ-32-03","REQ-34-01","REQ-34-02","REQ-35-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Model-quality, performance, resource and evidence views transform observations into decision material. Version exact definitions, code, population, denominator, grain, filters, window, input revisions, lineage, freshness and privacy. Reproduce results and corrections; test missing, stale, duplicate and incompatible sources, and retain failed runs. Correlation is not causation; no metric or threshold is redefined silently to improve a reported status.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/162_BUSINESS_INTELLIGENCE.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/162_BUSINESS_INTELLIGENCE.txt","sha256":"16b3d053badd50f4b6cc51437a1158bb9f3de08ea4008aeb0810c09475f0c21b","bytes":5333,"section":"162","original_title":"SECTION 162 — Business Intelligence","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A BI model with audience, decision purpose, metrics, lineage, refresh, permissions, accessibility, explanation, alerts, owner, evidence, and correction paths.","original_applicability":"Apply when reports, dashboards, scorecards, alerts, self-service analytics, or executive views influence material decisions or operations.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-07-04","REQ-24-03","REQ-29-01","REQ-32-01","REQ-32-02","REQ-32-03","REQ-32-04","REQ-35-01","REQ-35-03","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The mandatory native memory/evidence, models/resources, approvals and recovery controls present decision-relevant material. Bind actual audience, purpose, source/version, metric/denominator, filters, freshness, permissions, uncertainty, alerts and correction paths. Test discrepancies, stale views, denied access, accessibility and decisions under degraded state. A green chart or screenshot is not accurate evidence or accepted outcome. This adds no separate business-intelligence product.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/163_DATA_ANALYSIS.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/163_DATA_ANALYSIS.txt","sha256":"43d060ad40bcbc631aa9d36274fe5785b0fb67d575f49400e4ec8b2a9a715a0b","bytes":7451,"section":"163","original_title":"SECTION 163 — Data Analysis","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A question, population, scope, time window, unit of analysis, and decision context.\n- Reproducible data preparation, measures, methods, assumptions, limitations, and findings.\n- Traceability from source data through transformations, calculations, visualizations, conclusions, and owner action.\n- Explicit uncertainty, quality, bias, privacy, security, accessibility, and non-applicability determinations.","original_applicability":"Applies when data is used to describe conditions, explain variation, compare groups, diagnose causes, monitor outcomes, support decisions, or assess a change. It applies more deeply when results affect rights, safety, finance, service, policy, models, or public claims.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-13-03","REQ-23-02","REQ-23-03","REQ-24-01","REQ-24-02","REQ-24-03","REQ-24-04","REQ-34-02","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"CETA capability, quality, performance, resource and failure analysis support material engineering and owner decisions. State actual question, population, window, unit, inclusion, denominator, measurement, quality, missingness, bias, uncertainty and sensitivity. Retain methods, versions, counterexamples and dissent; separate observation, calculation, interpretation, recommendation and decision. Samples or associations do not establish causality, generalized capability or safety; no post-hoc exclusion is concealed.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/164_DATA_SCIENCE.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/164_DATA_SCIENCE.txt","sha256":"40c4ebf4a06b700fc5d119f9e486666dff3b0dbad0e184dcbe47f0c8da7a03ea","bytes":6806,"section":"164","original_title":"SECTION 164 — Data Science","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A research question, hypothesis, population, data basis, method, evaluation plan, and decision boundary.\n- Reproducible experiments with traceable features, assumptions, uncertainty, limitations, and alternatives.\n- Explicit separation of exploration, selection, validation, recommendation, and deployment authority.","original_applicability":"Applies to predictive, explanatory, causal, simulation, optimization, experimentation, or decision-support work using data and models. Depth increases with human impact, automation, external publication, regulated use, or irreversibility.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-14-01","REQ-14-03","REQ-23-03","REQ-23-04","REQ-24-01","REQ-24-02","REQ-24-03","REQ-24-04","REQ-34-02","REQ-36-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The rebuild must compare model/configuration candidates and evaluate semantic, planning, drift and recovery behavior. Predeclare question, baseline, population, split, held-out data, leakage controls, representation, error costs, subgroup/uncertainty, sensitivity and decision criteria. Bind exact sources, code, seeds, hardware/resources and all failed attempts. Simulation and experiments remain bounded evidence; no new scientific domain, private-data study, training run or publication is implied.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/165_STATISTICS.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/165_STATISTICS.txt","sha256":"eb0f8bb03e9fecfc063a891ca2ced4356cb36b41aeda1f77692758dbcf1c7fe6","bytes":6542,"section":"165","original_title":"SECTION 165 — Statistics","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A defined estimand, population, sampling design, assumptions, method, uncertainty, and decision context.\n- Reproducible calculations and transparent treatment of missingness, dependence, multiplicity, confounding, and sensitivity.\n- An interpretation bounded by the design and accepted by the accountable human owner.","original_applicability":"Applies to estimation, inference, forecasting, experimentation, sampling, measurement, risk quantification, quality control, and statistical claims. Greater review is required for regulated, rights-affecting, safety, financial, or public decisions.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-06-02","REQ-24-02","REQ-24-03","REQ-24-04","REQ-34-01","REQ-34-02","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Semantic nondeterminism and measured latency/resource qualification require more than one success or an aggregate average. Specify estimand, target population, sample/design, denominator, dependency, missingness, exclusions, multiplicity, stopping, subgroups and sensitivity. Follow repeated-trial and latency sample-count requirements; retain failures, distribution and uncertainty. Deterministic inventory counts need no invented confidence interval. Do not manufacture p-values, probabilities, causal or safety claims from averages or self-reported model confidence.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/166_OPERATIONS_RESEARCH.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/166_OPERATIONS_RESEARCH.txt","sha256":"9f8b2d3bc6147be03411543711a98b1f0c9a0cc212cb9072ec3b0c18e45cce04","bytes":6783,"section":"166","original_title":"SECTION 166 — Operations Research","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A decision problem with objective, decision variables, constraints, scenarios, stakeholders, and authority.\n- A validated model with data lineage, assumptions, sensitivity, uncertainty, feasibility, and failure behavior.\n- A recommendation that is explicitly distinct from an authorized operational decision or execution.","original_applicability":"Applies to allocation, routing, scheduling, capacity, inventory, queues, reliability, staffing, pricing, logistics, simulation, resource planning, or multi-criteria decisions. Review depth rises with scarcity, human impact, automation, and irreversibility.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-08-01","REQ-14-03","REQ-18-01","REQ-18-02","REQ-18-03","REQ-19-01","REQ-23-03","REQ-30-01","REQ-34-01","REQ-34-04","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Admission, constrained planning and orchestration select work under actual budgets, deadlines, authority and reserved recovery capacity. Define actual objectives, weights/preferences, hard constraints, feasibility, alternatives, uncertainty, baseline and decision authority. Test infeasible states, sensitivity, resource pressure and constraint enforcement at execution. An optimized score does not prove a protected outcome or authority. No unselected solver, resource purchase or relaxation of a safety/consent boundary is invented.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/167_MACHINE_LEARNING_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/167_MACHINE_LEARNING_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"50fd95f9d72795248f01cf0203251fab6fab41dd1ca7b6eb42035b0014dc6f0e","bytes":6539,"section":"167","original_title":"SECTION 167 — Machine Learning Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A traceable ML system from objective and data to model, service, decision, monitoring, and retirement.\n- Reproducible builds, versioned artifacts, evaluation evidence, deployment controls, and rollback-by-compensation paths.\n- Clear separation between technical capability, authorized use, and observed outcome.","original_applicability":"Applies when learned parameters or learned representations affect software, hardware, decisions, automation, ranking, prediction, or control. Depth increases with external impact, autonomy, sensitive data, drift, or hard-to-reverse actions.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-11-03","REQ-12-03","REQ-22-01","REQ-22-02","REQ-22-03","REQ-22-04","REQ-23-02","REQ-24-01","REQ-24-02","REQ-24-03","REQ-24-05","REQ-35-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Owned GGUF inference and learned representations are required ML components even when no new training executes. Bind actual weights/model, authorized data/splits, code, tokenizer/template, runtime, configuration, dependencies, hardware, evaluation, prohibited uses and lifecycle. Test leakage, shift, robustness, subgroups, inference/training parity where claimed, monitored drift, fallback and revocation. Preserve failures. A benchmark or endpoint liveness cannot qualify the installed product; future training remains separately authorized.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/168_DEEP_LEARNING_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/168_DEEP_LEARNING_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"23129329138dfc75ebd222269950bc816c7c3bf19ff18d520fd094017516f19f","bytes":6187,"section":"168","original_title":"SECTION 168 — Deep Learning Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- An attributable neural-system design with architecture, data, objective, compute, artifacts, and operational contract.\n- Reproducible training and evaluation with robustness, calibration, subgroup, privacy, security, and resource evidence.\n- Controlled deployment, monitoring, fallback, and retirement.","original_applicability":"Applies to neural networks, representation learners, multimodal models, sequence models, foundation models, and neural components used in consequential systems. It applies to training, fine-tuning, distillation, compression, and serving.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-11-03","REQ-22-01","REQ-22-03","REQ-22-04","REQ-23-02","REQ-23-03","REQ-23-04","REQ-24-01","REQ-24-03","REQ-24-05","REQ-31-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"CETA consumes and qualifies neural GGUF artifacts in its owned local runtime; training is a distinct conditional lane. Record architecture/source, artifact identity, authorized data lineage, input representation, configuration, precision, hardware, framework/runtime, serving, evaluation, safety, resources and privacy. Test actual deployment behavior and artifact/configuration change invalidation. Preserve available training lineage separately; do not invent checkpoints, training metrics, interpretability, new training, providers or compute budgets.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/169_AI_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/169_AI_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"291ef89db6482e04e31f73a974db38cf400416e1e814c1216918bc62d3389a49","bytes":6530,"section":"169","original_title":"SECTION 169 — AI Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A complete AI system boundary and contract, including capability, authority, data, tools, users, providers, and failure behavior.\n- Reproducible implementation, evaluation, observability, security, privacy, safety, accessibility, and human-control evidence.\n- A governed path from prototype to operation and retirement.","original_applicability":"Applies to systems that use models, agents, classifiers, generators, recommenders, speech, vision, retrieval, or learned components to inform or act. Depth increases with autonomy, sensitive data, external effects, and long-running operation.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-04","REQ-04-01","REQ-11-01","REQ-13-02","REQ-16-01","REQ-17-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-20-01","REQ-22-01","REQ-24-01","REQ-32-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"CETA is an AI-enabled socio-technical product whose external effects cannot be qualified by model-only tests. Define actual purpose, affected parties, prohibited use, model/provider, prompt, policy, retrieval, tools, identity, data, interface, review and autonomy. Evaluate normal, adversarial, ambiguous and failed paths, privacy, security, safety, accessibility, resource use, stop, correction, fallback and retirement. Version the whole path; a response/demo/trace is bounded evidence and cannot confer permission or readiness.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/170_GENERATIVE_AI_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/170_GENERATIVE_AI_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"ae6b43cca97c900e6c6510ffb80242844e220ccc91a054312fb95abcef2c85fd","bytes":6491,"section":"170","original_title":"SECTION 170 — Generative AI Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A generation contract specifying purpose, audience, inputs, output limits, sources, authority, review, and prohibited uses.\n- Reproducible prompts, model, retrieval, tools, safety controls, evaluations, traces, and release conditions.\n- Safe handling of uncertainty, refusal, correction, disclosure, misuse, and recovery.","original_applicability":"Applies to generation, transformation, summarization, translation, code synthesis, multimodal creation, retrieval-augmented generation, and tool-using generation. Review depth increases with external publication, rights impact, autonomy, or sensitive data.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-11-01","REQ-11-02","REQ-11-03","REQ-11-04","REQ-13-02","REQ-13-03","REQ-13-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-22-03","REQ-24-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-33-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Local conversation, summarization, proposals and manifested modalities generate material text or structured outputs. Bind actual purpose/audience, rights, model, prompt, context, retrieval, tools, policy, output schema, refusal, disclosure and review. Evaluate hallucination, grounding/citations, malformed output, injection, leakage, bias, accessibility and correction/withdrawal. Keep output validation and effect authority outside the model; fluency or a citation proves neither truth, rights nor permission to publish or execute.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/171_NATURAL_LANGUAGE_PROCESSING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/171_NATURAL_LANGUAGE_PROCESSING.txt","sha256":"063585b40be24315bffc288154093fbe47e78d7c7aefbee8324b6e14c36e6eb3","bytes":6260,"section":"171","original_title":"SECTION 171 — Natural Language Processing","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A language task and contract with population, languages, context, source, output, error, and review boundaries.\n- Evaluation for meaning, robustness, subgroup and language coverage, privacy, security, and usability.\n- Traceable deployment, correction, refusal, fallback, and retirement paths.","original_applicability":"Applies to classification, extraction, search, translation, question answering, dialogue, summarization, sentiment, generation, moderation, and language interfaces. Depth increases with rights, safety, employment, health, legal, or public impact.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-11-01","REQ-11-02","REQ-11-03","REQ-11-04","REQ-13-01","REQ-13-02","REQ-13-05","REQ-22-03","REQ-24-01","REQ-24-03","REQ-32-04","REQ-33-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Request compilation, conversation, summarization, source recall and speech-derived text are semantic language functions. Declare actual supported languages/dialects/users, corpora/labels, tokenizer/model, meaning/output/error/review limits and rights. Test ambiguity, negation, code-switching, long context, paraphrase, exact quotations, injection, privacy, accessibility, correction and per-language regressions. Missing language/population evidence stays unknown; fluency and aggregate scores do not establish meaning or unsupported language support.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/172_COMPUTER_VISION.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/172_COMPUTER_VISION.txt","sha256":"a272557cb63e0744a3f8377c8581b5a9e753582afdd366d36facb08f6a97eaf2","bytes":6299,"section":"172","original_title":"SECTION 172 — Computer Vision","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A visual task contract covering sensor, scene, population, environment, output, uncertainty, and action boundary.\n- Evidence for accuracy, robustness, subgroup and condition coverage, privacy, security, safety, and accessibility.\n- Controlled deployment, human review, incident, fallback, and retirement paths.","original_applicability":"Applies to image or video analysis, biometric or object recognition, inspection, medical or industrial vision, autonomous perception, visual search, and image generation. Depth increases with surveillance, physical action, identity, safety, or rights impact.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-10-01","REQ-10-02","REQ-11-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-23-02","REQ-24-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-32-04","REQ-33-01","REQ-33-02","REQ-33-03","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"REQ-33 explicitly retains selected-screen interpretation; visual meaning has source, context, uncertainty and privacy consequences. Bind selected lawful image/source, capture scope/identity/time, actual model/preprocessing, conditions, data/labels, thresholds, uncertainty, retention and action boundary. Test ambiguous, obscured, altered, stale, spoofed and degraded imagery, accessibility, privacy, stop and correction on selected configurations. Screen interpretation grants no identity, surveillance, biometric or physical-action authority; actual capture and hardware qualification remain unperformed.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/173_SPEECH_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/173_SPEECH_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"379eb02ff0a9b16c05d2637f382d27e277564a4954a9f481a9a0fc5e66b29bea","bytes":6277,"section":"173","original_title":"SECTION 173 — Speech Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A speech task and audio contract covering speakers, languages, environment, consent, retention, output, and action.\n- Evidence for intelligibility, word or intent accuracy, subgroup and acoustic coverage, privacy, security, and safety.\n- Controlled capture, review, correction, fallback, and retirement.","original_applicability":"Applies to speech-to-text, text-to-speech, voice authentication, diarization, call analysis, spoken dialogue, audio event detection, and voice cloning. Depth increases with biometrics, transactions, surveillance, health, safety, or public communication.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-10-01","REQ-11-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-23-02","REQ-24-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-32-04","REQ-33-01","REQ-33-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"REQ-33 retains local voice with explicit activation, visible status and confirmation before consequential actions. Bind actual capture policy, audio device/source, time, consent, language/accent, acoustics, model/voice/runtime, transcript, synthetic disclosure, review and retention. Test noise, overlap, silence, impairments, misrecognition, replay/spoofing, stop, correction, deletion and text/non-AI fallback. A transcript, word score or voice confidence cannot establish identity, consent or effect authority; no recording or voice cloning is performed.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/174_REINFORCEMENT_LEARNING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/174_REINFORCEMENT_LEARNING.txt","sha256":"334332b83b0fc6a20b7e4745ef8c3c9aa52ba0056cd0b98956e256591b484284","bytes":6391,"section":"174","original_title":"SECTION 174 — Reinforcement Learning","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A formal task and environment contract with states, actions, observations, rewards, constraints, termination, and authority.\n- Evidence that behavior meets protected outcomes beyond reward optimization in simulation or training.\n- Controlled exploration, evaluation, deployment, monitoring, interruption, and recovery.","original_applicability":"Applies to reinforcement learning, preference optimization, online learning, planning agents, adaptive control, bandits, and systems that learn from actions or feedback. Depth increases with physical action, external users, autonomy, or live exploration.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-14-01","REQ-14-02","REQ-14-03","REQ-18-01","REQ-18-02","REQ-18-03","REQ-19-01","REQ-20-03","REQ-23-04","REQ-24-01","REQ-24-05","REQ-30-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The original explicitly includes planning agents; CETA has bounded planning and orchestration even without online reinforcement training. Define actual states, observations, allowed actions, objectives, hard constraints, termination, uncertainty, authority and compensation. Bind any simulation/reward/trajectory claims to their actual provenance; test constraint failures, simulator gaps, feedback poisoning, stop and revocation. No reward objective, live exploration, online weight change or RL algorithm is added. Feedback cannot silently alter policy; training/exploration require their own exact authorization.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/175_KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/175_KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"13a485745a2e479833b4a2d8beec19e119bfe78eaa3c55269dbb341de26aecc4","bytes":6284,"section":"175","original_title":"SECTION 175 — Knowledge Graph Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A graph scope, vocabulary, identity policy, relationship model, provenance model, and query contract.\n- Traceable ingestion, reconciliation, inference, access, quality, update, and retirement behavior.\n- Explicit distinction between sourced facts, derived relationships, hypotheses, and generated answers.","original_applicability":"Applies to entity graphs, semantic search, lineage graphs, recommendation, dependency maps, retrieval systems, reasoning systems, and graph-based agents. Depth increases with identity, sensitive data, automated inference, or external action.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-06-01","REQ-06-02","REQ-11-02","REQ-12-01","REQ-12-02","REQ-12-03","REQ-12-04","REQ-14-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-29-03","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The mandatory memory graph represents provenance, support, contradiction, dependency, supersession and outcomes. Define actual graph purpose, vocabulary, identifiers, relations, temporal/validity, source/inference classes, access, quality, conflict, update and deletion. Test identity collisions, poisoned/stale/conflicting/cyclic/deleted edges, permission-filtered traversal, derived links, correction and export. A connected path or edge named authorizes proves neither truth nor a kernel grant. Canonical identity and accepted meaning remain separately governed.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/176_ONTOLOGY_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/176_ONTOLOGY_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"918a7f495fa22097ebb24d12d07cb6337373d46e736b7367d739c3751db87016","bytes":6081,"section":"176","original_title":"SECTION 176 — Ontology Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- An ontology scope, competency questions, concepts, relationships, constraints, mappings, owners, and version policy.\n- Evidence that definitions fit domain usage, stakeholder needs, data, information, and system behavior.\n- Controlled change, translation, conflict, deprecation, and adoption paths.","original_applicability":"Applies when shared formal meaning, reasoning, mapping, semantic validation, cross-domain exchange, or ontology-based AI is required. Depth increases with legal, safety, identity, public, or automated decision impact.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-06-01","REQ-06-02","REQ-11-02","REQ-12-01","REQ-12-03","REQ-12-05","REQ-14-02","REQ-16-02","REQ-18-01","REQ-31-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Typed graph relations and semantic validation require shared formal meanings with scope, authority and lifecycle effects. State actual competency questions, namespaces, concepts, relations, constraints, mappings, sources, domain owners, versions and inference limits. Test ambiguity, unintended entailment, mapping collisions, multilingual terms and compatible deprecation/migration. Keep semantic definition distinct from storage shape; lexical similarity or a reasoner result cannot settle contested meaning, identity, access or policy. No universal ontology is invented.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/177_SEMANTIC_SYSTEMS_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/177_SEMANTIC_SYSTEMS_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"310ab92e49c846200b837450a46bdf392bb56c6747cd4311135f936e22fcfe7b","bytes":6043,"section":"177","original_title":"SECTION 177 — Semantic Systems Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A semantic contract connecting ontology, data, information, queries, inference, users, and decisions.\n- Verified mappings, reasoning boundaries, provenance, access, contradiction handling, and lifecycle controls.\n- A clear distinction between semantic consistency and domain correctness.","original_applicability":"Applies to semantic APIs, knowledge representations, reasoning engines, federated meaning, ontology services, semantic search, validation, and AI grounding. Depth increases with automated inference, cross-domain exchange, or external consequence.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-11-02","REQ-11-03","REQ-11-04","REQ-12-01","REQ-12-03","REQ-12-04","REQ-13-03","REQ-14-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-35-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Context compilation, memory retrieval, typed graphs and proposition promotion interpret and exchange meaning. Version actual semantics, mappings, ontologies, embeddings, indexes, queries, provenance, policies and outputs. Separate source, inference, generated proposal and verified claim; preserve temporal validity, contradictions and permission before retrieval/inference. Test stale/deleted indexes, mapping drift, identity collision, unintended/unauthorized inference and explanation. Consistency or embedding similarity is not domain truth or authorization.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/178_AGENT_SYSTEMS_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/178_AGENT_SYSTEMS_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"70458e618d777e1870a58c01790cd30dadad8398c2bde0d871eea16d63d25dab","bytes":6429,"section":"178","original_title":"SECTION 178 — Agent Systems Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A bounded agent contract for goal, capabilities, tools, data, permissions, state, planning, action, review, and termination.\n- Reproducible evaluation of planning, tool use, delegation, refusal, recovery, security, safety, and user control.\n- Immutable decisions and append-only evidence for consequential action.","original_applicability":"Applies to autonomous, semi-autonomous, tool-using, multi-agent, workflow, planning, and long-running agents. Depth increases with external mutation, delegation, sensitive data, autonomy, persistence, or multi-party impact.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-08-01","REQ-09-01","REQ-13-03","REQ-16-01","REQ-17-02","REQ-18-01","REQ-18-03","REQ-18-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-19-03","REQ-20-01","REQ-20-03","REQ-30-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The required supervised task and effect cycle is an agent system with persistent state, scoped tools and governed decisions. Bind actual goal, actor/capability, state, memory, plan, review, policy, tool invocation, trace, decision, mutation, observation and settlement. Reconcile the original's named bindings with the supplied CETA typed contracts rather than importing another API as authority. Test expiry/revocation, replay/concurrency, missing review, injection, hidden delegation, unbounded loops, terminal events and linked compensation. Goals, plans and tool responses alone confer neither permission nor success.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/179_MODEL_TRAINING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/179_MODEL_TRAINING.txt","sha256":"0cc7b0805cfb63a7fb9a410e7254de48b457df06b1ed8725be6333b971ebde46","bytes":6044,"section":"179","original_title":"SECTION 179 — Model Training","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"SUPPORTING","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A training plan connecting authorized purpose, data, objective, configuration, compute, artifacts, and evaluation.\n- Reproducible runs with lineage, resource, contamination, privacy, security, and failure evidence.\n- Controlled checkpoint selection and handoff; training is not deployment approval.","original_applicability":"Applies to pretraining, fine-tuning, transfer learning, reinforcement or preference optimization, distillation, quantization-aware training, and retraining. Depth increases with sensitive data, scale, autonomy, or external use.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-23-04","REQ-24-02","REQ-24-05","REQ-29-01","REQ-31-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Current desktop inference consumes externally obtained artifacts; REQ-24-05 requires a separately authorized and budgeted training pipeline, while REQ-31-01 preserves historical training artifacts. Retain the training pipeline contract, source/data rights, objective, splits/contamination, compute authority, configurations/seeds, run/checkpoint identities, failed runs, evaluation, selection and promotion requirements. Keep training dependencies outside the runtime closure when unnecessary. No model training, data reuse, checkpoint selection or deployment is authorized by this assessment. Reopen direct run obligations before any pretraining/fine-tuning/distillation/preference optimization/retraining or changed model artifact; lineage and authorization boundaries remain mandatory now.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/180_MODEL_EVALUATION.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/180_MODEL_EVALUATION.txt","sha256":"8f529e974a1d369e0600440babffc480d42d4fa49da3ebb47f749486dd0b4909","bytes":6036,"section":"180","original_title":"SECTION 180 — Model Evaluation","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- An evaluation charter with claims, datasets, scenarios, metrics, thresholds, uncertainty, and decision authority.\n- Evidence covering expected, boundary, adversarial, subgroup, safety, privacy, security, accessibility, robustness, and operational behavior.\n- A decision that states what the evidence supports and what remains unknown.","original_applicability":"Applies to model selection, training gates, release, monitoring, incident review, retraining, and claims about capability, safety, fairness, robustness, or alignment. Depth increases with consequence and autonomy.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-17-03","REQ-22-03","REQ-23-03","REQ-24-01","REQ-24-02","REQ-24-03","REQ-24-04","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-03","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"REQ-24 and the full acceptance matrix demand qualification of actual CETA behavior beyond endpoint liveness. Freeze claims, populations, scenarios, metrics, rubrics, thresholds, grader/evaluator identities, independence and uncertainty. Separate development/selection/held-out/monitoring data and source-family leakage; bind payload, runtime/model/template/settings/source/environment and repeated outcomes. Retain failures, abstentions, disagreement and counterexamples. Self-review or LLM-only grading cannot satisfy independent assurance; a result grants no release authority.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/181_MODEL_ALIGNMENT.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/181_MODEL_ALIGNMENT.txt","sha256":"cad01bcab95bbee192743b37c1533a8e30145b60dd5f42e967b4662c22ece337","bytes":6134,"section":"181","original_title":"SECTION 181 — Model Alignment","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- Explicit behavior objectives, prohibited behaviors, value conflicts, feedback sources, and decision authority.\n- Evidence of helpfulness, honesty, refusal, robustness, bias, manipulation resistance, and human-control behavior.\n- Transparent limitations and residual disagreement.","original_applicability":"Applies to instruction tuning, preference optimization, constitutional or policy training, refusal behavior, value shaping, reward modeling, and behavior modification. Depth increases with autonomy, power, user impact, or contested values.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-11-01","REQ-13-02","REQ-13-04","REQ-13-05","REQ-17-01","REQ-17-03","REQ-24-01","REQ-24-02","REQ-24-04","REQ-24-05","REQ-28-01","REQ-28-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The companion directive and prompt/request path shape helpfulness, uncertainty, refusal and user control; behavior qualification applies without new weight training. Declare actual behavior targets, policies, users, prohibited actions, rubrics, feedback provenance and disagreements. Test sycophancy, deception, manipulation, over/under-refusal, injection, ambiguity, correction and policy conflicts on exact configurations. Preserve residual uncertainty and independent review; reward, popularity or agreement is not legitimacy, universal alignment or effect authority. Training-based alignment remains separately authorized.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/182_AI_SAFETY.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/182_AI_SAFETY.txt","sha256":"b4fcbd9deae03b04d01797665d01cf6036f429ffa2f5fd4f9efe5d87a8400469","bytes":6171,"section":"182","original_title":"SECTION 182 — AI Safety","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A safety case with hazards, affected parties, severity, likelihood, controls, evidence, residual risk, and authority.\n- Tested safe states, refusal, interruption, fallback, incident, communication, and compensation paths.\n- No claim of safety beyond declared scope and evidence.","original_applicability":"Applies to any AI system with material user, public, physical, environmental, financial, privacy, security, rights, or autonomy consequence. Depth is proportional to hazard and reversibility.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-14-03","REQ-16-01","REQ-17-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-20-01","REQ-21-01","REQ-24-01","REQ-28-01","REQ-28-02","REQ-28-03","REQ-30-01","REQ-33-03","REQ-35-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Models, retrieval and tools can create material privacy, security, user and external-effect hazards. Build actual scoped hazard/control/requirement/test/evidence links, affected parties, severity/likelihood uncertainty, residual risk and decision authority. Exercise adversarial/degraded paths, lost monitors, authority expiry, injection, failed observations, independent stop, safe fallback, incidents, correction and compensation. Preserve near misses and findings. No model or same-actor test suite self-certifies safety; missing actual physical evidence leaves dependent lanes unavailable.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/183_AI_GOVERNANCE.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/183_AI_GOVERNANCE.txt","sha256":"c94ea530614d7adc337b874a9ec3f6bc0383a1f6f8a2509a7c80340cd7943d80","bytes":6514,"section":"183","original_title":"SECTION 183 — AI Governance","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A governed AI inventory with purpose, owner, impact, risk, capability, data, provider, lifecycle, and decision status.\n- Policy evaluation linked to immutable DecisionRecord and AuditDecision artifacts.\n- Complete mutation bindings for consequential model, prompt, tool, data, deployment, and policy changes.","original_applicability":"Applies to AI design, procurement, training, evaluation, deployment, operation, tool use, data use, prompt changes, policy changes, and retirement. It applies more deeply with regulated use, autonomy, sensitive data, external effect, or mutation.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-07-01","REQ-13-03","REQ-16-01","REQ-16-02","REQ-16-03","REQ-16-04","REQ-17-02","REQ-18-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-19-02","REQ-19-03","REQ-19-04","REQ-20-03","REQ-26-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"CETA's deterministic kernel alone owns effective policy, legal state, grants, admissions and effect settlement. Bind exact intent, actor, scope, resource/action, capability generation, policy evaluation, trace, reviews/quorum where required, decision, audit, effect and compensation. Map original governance-binding names to actual CETA schemas/contracts without conflating local shape validation with policy evaluation or importing another project's endpoints. Test incomplete/stale/conflicting bindings, replay, self-approval, missing quorum and alternate bypass paths. Preserve immutable evidence and owner policy-change authority.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/184_MLOPS.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/184_MLOPS.txt","sha256":"73017a5c74f0a44811d36a6d65c3d8357f5ed5a0dab640d8144b047f79081c59","bytes":5979,"section":"184","original_title":"SECTION 184 — MLOps","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- Reproducible, traceable promotion of ML artifacts through controlled environments.\n- Gates for data, evaluation, security, safety, policy, approval, observability, rollback, and compensation.\n- Continuous evidence that distinguishes pipeline health from model or outcome validity.","original_applicability":"Applies to ML build, registry, validation, release, serving, monitoring, retraining, promotion, rollback, incident, and retirement workflows. Depth increases with autonomy, continuous learning, sensitive data, or external effect.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-22-01","REQ-22-02","REQ-22-04","REQ-23-01","REQ-23-03","REQ-23-04","REQ-24-01","REQ-24-02","REQ-24-05","REQ-30-03","REQ-35-02","REQ-38-01","REQ-38-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The product acquires, qualifies, activates, replaces and retires local models and configurations under owned lifecycle controls. Version source/data/model/runtime/template/configuration/dependencies/environment/evaluator/approval and trace. Enforce artifact integrity, quality, safety, privacy, policy and promotion gates; test broken artifacts, evaluator loss, authority expiry, drift, failed monitors, interrupted activation, fallback and compatible rollback. Green automation is not model fitness. Retraining remains separately authorized; external effects recover by linked compensation.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/185_MODEL_OPERATIONS.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/185_MODEL_OPERATIONS.txt","sha256":"572a7e0d309ecc0cdff2fa6f0fb1c40ae0d1a64e75404c7969b651b3900135a4","bytes":5896,"section":"185","original_title":"SECTION 185 — Model Operations","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- An operational model inventory and serving contract with owner, version, scope, authority, dependencies, and lifecycle.\n- Reliable observability of model, service, data, policy, user, and outcome behavior.\n- Safe stop, fallback, incident, compensation, and retirement paths.","original_applicability":"Applies to deployed, hosted, embedded, batch, edge, shadow, or human-reviewed model use. Depth increases with live learning, external mutation, sensitive data, and high consequence.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-08-01","REQ-22-01","REQ-22-02","REQ-22-03","REQ-22-04","REQ-23-02","REQ-23-03","REQ-24-01","REQ-24-03","REQ-30-01","REQ-34-02","REQ-35-01","REQ-35-03","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"CETA operates local model workers with authoritative lifetime/generation, dispatch and configuration leases. Bind actual endpoint/worker identity, weights/runtime/template/tokenizer, configuration, device, traffic/load, quality and latency metrics, data/policy scope, current qualifications, traces, monitoring and lifecycle. Test mismatch, stale data, drift, load, malformed requests, provider/monitor loss, unauthorized access, cancellation, qualified fallback and retirement. Uptime, latency or a single output proves neither competence nor safety; material model/routing changes retain authority.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/186_PROMPT_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/186_PROMPT_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"91fc117189f832c88e123d1c19e4f9c7b6fa212935df23fdd50c8b793a6d61c7","bytes":5897,"section":"186","original_title":"SECTION 186 — Prompt Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A prompt contract with purpose, audience, model, context, tools, output, policy, failure, and review boundaries.\n- Reproducible prompt versions, evaluations, injection tests, provenance, and release decisions.\n- Explicit limits on what prompt changes can and cannot authorize.","original_applicability":"Applies to system instructions, templates, few-shot examples, routing prompts, tool instructions, evaluator prompts, retrieval context, and prompt optimization. Depth increases with tools, sensitive data, external action, or policy consequence.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-11-01","REQ-11-02","REQ-11-03","REQ-11-04","REQ-11-05","REQ-13-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-22-03","REQ-24-01","REQ-24-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"One inspectable request compiler handles chat, planning, review, probes, maintenance and modality inputs. Version actual instruction layers, prompt/template/tokenizer, examples, authorized context, roles, tools, policy, rendered payload, schemas, evaluator and deadline. Test injection, conflict, stale/poisoned context, exact token budget, long inputs, ambiguity, model replacement, leakage, malformed output and rollback. Prompts shape behavior but cannot authorize data/effects or replace kernel validation. Preserve latest user wording and context omissions.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/187_SYNTHETIC_DATA_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/187_SYNTHETIC_DATA_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"885ca3bf8e7706a0bd1841f72c2f1917c6ba3f8a81f43e98a45e1963dd255482","bytes":6443,"section":"187","original_title":"SECTION 187 — Synthetic Data Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A synthetic-data purpose, generator, source basis, population, privacy, quality, utility, and limitation record.\n- Evidence that synthetic data is labeled, fit for its bounded use, not mistaken for observed fact, and not a hidden disclosure channel.\n- Controlled generation, access, correction, deletion, and retirement.","original_applicability":"Applies to generated records, simulations, augmented samples, masked or perturbed data, test fixtures, synthetic images, text, audio, features, labels, and training or evaluation data. Depth increases with sensitive source data or consequential models.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-06-02","REQ-14-01","REQ-14-03","REQ-23-04","REQ-24-02","REQ-24-03","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-31-02","REQ-34-03","REQ-36-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"REQ-34 requires isolated 10,000/100,000-event synthetic stress profiles; exploratory propositions and model evaluation also need explicit generated-versus-observed status. Record actual generator, source basis/rights, versions, seeds/configuration, target use/population, labels, utility/coverage/bias/rare cases, privacy/linkage where sensitive inputs exist, downstream lineage, retention and deletion. Test label survival, schema, failures, reproducibility and downstream limits; do not claim real-world fidelity, privacy or independence from synthetic success. Handwritten constants carry no realism claim; no private-data generator or training run is added.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/188_HUMAN_IN_THE_LOOP_OPERATIONS.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/188_HUMAN_IN_THE_LOOP_OPERATIONS.txt","sha256":"66cd8bb9030562302a36b9431145562762a8b54f0b2b890fa3f68dd6f08d6dc6","bytes":6774,"section":"188","original_title":"SECTION 188 — Human-in-the-Loop Operations","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":6,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_06_Data_Intelligence_and_Human_Oversight.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A human-control model with role, authority, workload, timing, information, training, escalation, and decision boundaries.\n- Review that is meaningful, accessible, attributable, and able to change the result before consequence.\n- Durable records linking AI output, human action, policy evaluation, decision, trace, and outcome.","original_applicability":"Applies when humans review, approve, monitor, label, correct, appeal, override, supervise, or recover AI and automated outputs. Depth increases with consequence, scale, speed, vulnerability, autonomy, or irreversible action.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-13-05","REQ-17-01","REQ-17-02","REQ-17-03","REQ-19-01","REQ-19-02","REQ-19-03","REQ-20-01","REQ-20-03","REQ-30-01","REQ-32-03","REQ-32-04","REQ-36-04","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Approvals, independent review, stop, correction, recovery and owner control are mandatory product behavior. Bind actual human role/identity, authority, evidence/version, context, consequence, timing, review point, quorum/expiry where required, decision/rationale/dissent, trace and outcome. Test stale/missing context, overload, inaccessible controls, prefilled approval, policy mismatch, interruptions, appeal and compensation. Review must precede and be able to change a required mutation. Silence, a click or three correlated model passes proves neither consent nor independent oversight.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_12.md","handoff/volume_vi_reconciliation_20261007_12.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/189_CYBERSECURITY_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/189_CYBERSECURITY_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"e95b4f751730b15463f04db4b1f68bfe715e09c90eaf2067e23c3b130eaed244","bytes":8168,"section":"189","original_title":"SECTION 189 — Cybersecurity Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":7,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_07_Cybersecurity_through_Privacy_Engineering.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- A bounded cybersecurity scope, threat model, control architecture, owners, authorities, trust boundaries, and lifecycle states.\n - Security requirements allocated to people, processes, applications, platforms, infrastructure, data, interfaces, suppliers, and operations.\n - Tested prevention, detection, response, recovery, evidence, and continuous-improvement paths with explicit limitations.","original_applicability":"Applies when systems, data, identities, devices, facilities, suppliers, interfaces, models, or operations face unauthorized access, misuse, disruption, manipulation, disclosure, or loss. It applies proportionally to consequence, exposure, and recovery dependence.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-03","REQ-03-04","REQ-16-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-20-01","REQ-21-01","REQ-21-02","REQ-25-01","REQ-26-04","REQ-28-02","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-03","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"CETA holds private state and admits model-directed effects, so whole-system security directly governs the rebuild. Inventory actual assets, actors, trusted/untrusted domains and OS/admin/hardware assumptions; connect threats, protected outcomes, controls, implementation, telemetry, hostile tests, residual risks and recovery. Exercise unauthorized access, tamper, disclosure, denial, dependency/key loss and evidence replay. Preserve failures and dissent; no scan, unit suite or dashboard establishes total security.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_13.md","handoff/volume_vii_reconciliation_20261007_13.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/190_APPLICATION_SECURITY.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/190_APPLICATION_SECURITY.txt","sha256":"ef596a3add240475be73090055313c446490059cc0cdc9d6e5e241fd4d22f00a","bytes":6491,"section":"190","original_title":"SECTION 190 — Application Security","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":7,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_07_Cybersecurity_through_Privacy_Engineering.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- Application threat model, security requirements, secure design patterns, ownership, and trust boundaries.\n - Verified protections for input, output, identity, authorization, secrets, dependencies, data, sessions, errors, logging, and recovery.\n - Security evidence and remediation decisions linked to exact artifacts and runtime environments.","original_applicability":"Applies to web, mobile, desktop, service, API, batch, event, agent, plugin, and administrative applications, including code, configuration, libraries, pipelines, and runtime interfaces.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-05-04","REQ-06-01","REQ-07-01","REQ-11-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-19-02","REQ-21-03","REQ-21-04","REQ-22-04","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-04","REQ-38-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Native UI, canonical store, kernel, broker, context and model workers expose material code, data and dependency boundaries. Bind source/build/runtime versions, dependencies, configuration, entry points, identity, secrets and data flows. Test injection, malformed/oversized input, confused deputy, concurrency, denied/stale access, safe errors/logs, dependency failure, update and recovery. Verify fixes on actual public paths; client state, generated code and static scans are bounded evidence.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_13.md","handoff/volume_vii_reconciliation_20261007_13.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/191_PRODUCT_SECURITY.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/191_PRODUCT_SECURITY.txt","sha256":"11a8318c1c7e63b0c2a23b37ed134ccd8578639fbede9991961a8c4028690015","bytes":6967,"section":"191","original_title":"SECTION 191 — Product Security","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":7,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_07_Cybersecurity_through_Privacy_Engineering.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- Product security objectives, threat model, security requirements, accountable owners, release gates, support commitments, and retirement conditions.\n - Security controls and evidence spanning design, build, delivery, deployment, use, update, incident, and customer communication.\n - A risk and vulnerability process that protects users without concealing limitations or shifting unbounded burden to customers.","original_applicability":"Applies to products, services, devices, platforms sold or provided to users, internal products with material users, managed offerings, SDKs, APIs, models, and productized AI capabilities.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-01","REQ-03-02","REQ-24-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-31-04","REQ-32-01","REQ-32-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-37-02","REQ-38-01","REQ-38-02","REQ-38-03","REQ-38-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The goal is an installable usable CETA product whose lifecycle includes local data, models, updates, support and retirement. Trace actual user promises, defaults, abuse surface, supply chain, migration, supported versions, accessible reporting, update authenticity/rollback, privacy and recovery. Preserve customer responsibility and evidence limits; qualifying one component does not qualify the installed release. Actual support/disclosure commitments and public release need concrete owner decisions at their relevant gate.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_13.md","handoff/volume_vii_reconciliation_20261007_13.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/192_PLATFORM_SECURITY.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/192_PLATFORM_SECURITY.txt","sha256":"7415ecc052956c47e05f8e35a8083f1268696ca8f71fd0fde925ffe8d11e175e","bytes":6982,"section":"192","original_title":"SECTION 192 — Platform Security","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":7,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_07_Cybersecurity_through_Privacy_Engineering.pdf","original_required_outcome":"- Platform assets, tenants, trust zones, administrative roles, control objectives, dependencies, and operating modes.\n - Enforced isolation, identity, authorization, configuration, patching, secrets, monitoring, recovery, and supply-chain controls.\n - Evidence linking platform state to workload impact, exceptions, incident response, and safe change.","original_applicability":"Applies to runtime, container, orchestration, developer, CI/CD, data, identity, observability, integration, edge, hosting, and shared service platforms, including managed providers and control planes.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-03","REQ-03-04","REQ-05-01","REQ-07-01","REQ-18-03","REQ-19-01","REQ-21-01","REQ-21-02","REQ-21-03","REQ-29-03","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"One CETA application has isolated processes, shared contracts, scoped streams and a small trusted authority boundary. Inventory actual platform/control-plane owners, workloads, project isolation, privileges, configuration, dependencies and recovery assumptions. Test escape, cross-scope access, inherited handles, malicious artifacts, authority/control-plane loss, overload, drift, restore and evidence. Same-privilege processes and configuration templates cannot prove runtime isolation. No cloud/container platform or service-per-table redesign is introduced.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_13.md","handoff/volume_vii_reconciliation_20261007_13.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/193_INFRASTRUCTURE_SECURITY.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/193_INFRASTRUCTURE_SECURITY.txt","sha256":"5923085ce9d08ee83b8e0eaeeed49f4b8b4c9064087bb19b833a3c0d568a9167","bytes":5437,"section":"193","original_title":"SECTION 193 — Infrastructure Security","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":7,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_07_Cybersecurity_through_Privacy_Engineering.pdf","original_required_outcome":"Infrastructure assets, trust zones, owners, hardening baselines, privileged paths, patching, monitoring, isolation, backup, recovery, and evidence are explicit and tested.","original_applicability":"Applies to servers, hosts, hypervisors, storage, images, operating systems, facilities, provisioning, administrative tooling, and physical or virtual infrastructure.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-07-02","REQ-21-01","REQ-21-02","REQ-21-04","REQ-23-02","REQ-25-04","REQ-27-04","REQ-30-04","REQ-35-02","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Windows host, storage, resource controls, runtime/toolchain and hardware support are material infrastructure dependencies. Bind selected OS/library/binary/filesystem/device/driver versions, privileges, assets and required hardening/backup/recovery assumptions. Test actual host/service/store isolation, dependency/management loss, file tamper, load and restore. Preserve host defenses and narrow privileged installation scope; no boot, firmware, provisioning, host wipe or global security-settings change is authorized by a source assessment.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_13.md","handoff/volume_vii_reconciliation_20261007_13.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/194_CLOUD_SECURITY.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/194_CLOUD_SECURITY.txt","sha256":"c98fc259ded42060203dd8a19bbb659fd1e2a8bb87363081bda500ec47a1eb24","bytes":5430,"section":"194","original_title":"SECTION 194 — Cloud Security","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"SUPPORTING","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":7,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_07_Cybersecurity_through_Privacy_Engineering.pdf","original_required_outcome":"Cloud scope, account ownership, tenancy, identity, policy, network, data, logging, provider responsibility, resilience, recovery, and evidence are explicit.","original_applicability":"Applies to public, private, hybrid, multi-cloud, managed services, cloud-native applications, accounts, subscriptions, regions, and provider control planes.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-01","REQ-03-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-20-02","REQ-22-01","REQ-22-04","REQ-29-01","REQ-33-03","REQ-35-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The owner specification requires local owned inference and forbids a mandatory cloud account/hidden external fallback. No cloud account, deployment, region or control plane is selected in this build baseline. Retain exact provider/account/tenant/region, identity, data location, responsibility, terms, logging, limits, outage and recovery requirements for any selected external service or future cloud-hosted control. REQ-33 qualified network-service lanes remain open. Reopen direct cloud clauses before an actual provider/account/resource/data/control-plane change or cloud assurance claim. Do not create accounts, resources, egress or implicit fallback from this topic.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_13.md","handoff/volume_vii_reconciliation_20261007_13.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/195_NETWORK_SECURITY.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/195_NETWORK_SECURITY.txt","sha256":"4d0a6c5cf078dffe0df9f312d20dfc6515ab9c628e9c5e1a61312690abe11438","bytes":5154,"section":"195","original_title":"SECTION 195 — Network Security","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":7,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_07_Cybersecurity_through_Privacy_Engineering.pdf","original_required_outcome":"Network assets, zones, flows, owners, identities, policy, encryption, monitoring, availability, segmentation, incident, recovery, and evidence are explicit.","original_applicability":"Applies to enterprise, cloud, data center, wireless, edge, internet, operational, partner, service-mesh, and management networks and their protocols and providers.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-05-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-19-04","REQ-21-02","REQ-21-03","REQ-22-01","REQ-22-02","REQ-22-04","REQ-26-04","REQ-29-01","REQ-33-03","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Required IPC, owned local inference and qualified network-service/browser adapters carry authority and private information. Declare actual transport/topology/peer identity/names, allowed flows, egress, credentials, freshness, protocol/version and recovery. Authenticate peers and confine workers; test spoofing, replay, unauthorized routes/requests, lost/partitioned transport, stale credentials, load and evidence. A loopback address, matching port or process name is not trusted readiness. No broad firewall, route, remote capture or provider change is performed.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_13.md","handoff/volume_vii_reconciliation_20261007_13.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/196_ENDPOINT_SECURITY.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/196_ENDPOINT_SECURITY.txt","sha256":"25a72814a436f8025c80d1dab187e9608bc914245ff986dc271b0639058a3e19","bytes":5294,"section":"196","original_title":"SECTION 196 — Endpoint Security","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":7,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_07_Cybersecurity_through_Privacy_Engineering.pdf","original_required_outcome":"Endpoint inventory, ownership, posture, access, software, patching, encryption, isolation, monitoring, response, recovery, and disposal are explicit and verifiable.","original_applicability":"Applies to workstations, servers, mobile devices, virtual desktops, kiosks, field devices, privileged consoles, and endpoint management systems.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-01","REQ-21-01","REQ-21-02","REQ-21-04","REQ-23-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-04","REQ-32-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Native CETA runs on user-owned Windows hosts and must protect data, models and credentials while remaining usable offline. Bind actual supported endpoint/OS/user/principal/management boundary, software/patch/configuration, device resources, permissions and evidence. Test local privilege, hostile files, removable assets, stale policy, offline/host/management loss, restore and updates. Preserve user privacy and host defenses; no endpoint enrollment system, remote wipe, broad surveillance or blanket admin trust is inferred.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_13.md","handoff/volume_vii_reconciliation_20261007_13.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/197_MOBILE_SECURITY.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/197_MOBILE_SECURITY.txt","sha256":"e2765bfe8a7a5888e06f6122cce0e16f1f9bf9b928a573634e92697d85005ff3","bytes":12760,"section":"197","original_title":"SECTION 197 — Mobile Security","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"NOT_APPLICABLE","implementation_status":"NOT_APPLICABLE","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":7,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_07_Cybersecurity_through_Privacy_Engineering.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A mobile-security architecture and operating model that identifies assets, users, trust boundaries, threats, permissions, data handling, update paths, telemetry, response authority, recovery, and disposal for the exact platforms, versions, populations, and environments in scope.","original_applicability":"Apply when a mobile application, mobile device, mobile identity, mobile endpoint, app store, mobile API, device-management service, sensor, local cache, or mobile support workflow can access information, perform actions, or affect a person, organization, or connected system.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-01","REQ-04-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-33-03","REQ-36-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The supplied target is native Windows x64. Current component/work-package inventory selects no mobile app, mobile device/identity management, app-store release, mobile data or support workflow. This is a bounded engineering decision against the exact owner specification and recorded inventory, not a universal mobile exemption or owner security acceptance. Desktop/API/device/privacy/offline/recovery obligations remain mandatory. Reopen before any mobile client/device identity/API/store/SDK/sensor/cache/support lane or mobile use with data or authority effect; phone viewing does not itself remove such duties. Do not add a mobile product from the section title.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_13.md","handoff/volume_vii_reconciliation_20261007_13.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/198_EMBEDDED_SECURITY.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/198_EMBEDDED_SECURITY.txt","sha256":"91a2d8c3b9849d895fbb28e9fa2295193bfb60bdb65c643cf13d76d92e42d232","bytes":10792,"section":"198","original_title":"SECTION 198 — Embedded Security","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":7,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_07_Cybersecurity_through_Privacy_Engineering.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A bounded security design for the exact device, firmware, hardware, interface, environment, threat scope, population, and lifecycle, including trust boundaries, keys, data, update paths, debug controls, safe states, telemetry, response authority, recovery, and evidence.","original_applicability":"Apply when software, firmware, electronics, sensors, actuators, controllers, appliances, vehicles, industrial equipment, medical devices, or other physical systems contain computation, connectivity, stored data, update capability, or security-relevant identity.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-21-03","REQ-23-02","REQ-25-03","REQ-25-04","REQ-26-02","REQ-27-04","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-33-03","REQ-35-02","REQ-37-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"REQ-33 retains manifested devices/actuators and requires actual interlocks and hardware qualification before operation. For each selected device, bind actual hardware/firmware/build/source/interface/debug/update identity, trust roots, data, threats, safety constraints, owner and lifecycle. Test tamper, malicious peripheral, loss/clock/power/update interruption, safe halt, manual recovery and disposal on real representative hardware. No custom firmware, flashing, secret extraction, manufacturing credentials or device effects occur now; missing hardware keeps the lane open/unavailable.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_13.md","handoff/volume_vii_reconciliation_20261007_13.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/199_HARDWARE_SECURITY.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/199_HARDWARE_SECURITY.txt","sha256":"cb1cf26eed191956d494d900eabd2fcff6c674ab64af79ea186a270e6d5189ce","bytes":7122,"section":"199","original_title":"SECTION 199 — Hardware Security","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":7,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_07_Cybersecurity_through_Privacy_Engineering.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A hardware-security baseline covering assets, suppliers, provenance, tamper resistance, debug and service access, trust roots, physical exposure, secure provisioning, monitoring, replacement, and disposal for the declared product and environment.","original_applicability":"Apply when hardware, boards, chips, modules, peripherals, manufacturing, provisioning, service ports, physical enclosures, or component supply chains affect identity, confidentiality, integrity, availability, safety, or recovery.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-21-01","REQ-23-02","REQ-25-03","REQ-25-04","REQ-26-01","REQ-26-02","REQ-26-04","REQ-27-04","REQ-33-03","REQ-35-02","REQ-37-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Strong custody/distributed-authority profiles and selected physical adapters have required hardware identity, lifetime and compromise boundaries. Inventory actual consumed hardware/revisions/suppliers/interfaces/trust anchors, provisioning and physical threat assumptions. Verify selected possession-factor/cloning claims, hardware isolation/attestation, debug exposure, replacement and recovery on real technology. USB serials, launch hashes and one inspected unit do not prove protected possession or host-compromise resilience. No new chip/board/manufacturing design or physical intervention is introduced.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_13.md","handoff/volume_vii_reconciliation_20261007_13.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/200_IDENTITY_AND_ACCESS_MANAGEMENT.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/200_IDENTITY_AND_ACCESS_MANAGEMENT.txt","sha256":"1cd43fc3f6b366dfd90de94fd4def9bed6466b3026373f603399ebbf8951655d","bytes":6807,"section":"200","original_title":"SECTION 200 — Identity and Access Management","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":7,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_07_Cybersecurity_through_Privacy_Engineering.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An identity and access model with authoritative sources, identity proofing, authentication dependency, authorization relationship, provisioning, review, delegation, privileged access, logging, revocation, recovery, and owner accountability.","original_applicability":"Apply whenever a person, service, device, workload, agent, supplier, or organization can access information, invoke a capability, make a decision, or affect a protected resource.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-06-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-19-02","REQ-19-05","REQ-30-04"],"decision_reason":"Human and non-human identities access protected resources; full original inspected; access lifecycle, actual proof, delegation/review and recovery remain open.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261006_02.md"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/201_AUTHENTICATION_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/201_AUTHENTICATION_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"4385c48068e043ab960b81a7629c2429d5ab4452d57153d526dedb46182f2494","bytes":6810,"section":"201","original_title":"SECTION 201 — Authentication Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":7,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_07_Cybersecurity_through_Privacy_Engineering.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An authentication design covering assurance levels, authenticators, enrollment, recovery, phishing and replay resistance, federation, session management, step-up, failure handling, logging, user support, and retirement.","original_applicability":"Apply whenever an identity must be established before access, transaction, administration, delegation, account recovery, or other consequential action.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-05-03","REQ-06-01","REQ-19-05","REQ-21-01","REQ-21-05"],"decision_reason":"IPC peers and trusted approval need actual authenticated session binding; full original inspected; no authenticator, assurance target, provider or recovery proof has been invented.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261006_02.md"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/202_AUTHORIZATION_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/202_AUTHORIZATION_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"abfe7af1174c7d18817f141cc91f1dd17b3570c8a6841d0cc2c3d94bd3980743","bytes":6553,"section":"202","original_title":"SECTION 202 — Authorization Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":7,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_07_Cybersecurity_through_Privacy_Engineering.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An authorization model with resource ownership, actions, subjects, policy rules, context, delegation, separation of duties, enforcement points, denial behavior, decision evidence, review, and change control.","original_applicability":"Apply whenever an identity, service, device, workload, agent, or user can read, create, change, execute, approve, share, delete, administer, or otherwise affect a resource or decision.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-16-01","REQ-16-02","REQ-16-03","REQ-16-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-19-02","REQ-19-03","REQ-19-04","REQ-19-05"],"decision_reason":"Protected effects require exact current authority and real enforcement; truncated display was reread completely; kernel, policy, races and consume-once remain open.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261006_02.md"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/203_CRYPTOGRAPHY.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/203_CRYPTOGRAPHY.txt","sha256":"ada575b4efcbbf9b6fdcc7e07a6eabf0fa74cc950d3db0eeea94021423e83132","bytes":6934,"section":"203","original_title":"SECTION 203 — Cryptography","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":7,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_07_Cybersecurity_through_Privacy_Engineering.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A cryptographic architecture with protection goals, algorithms and protocols, randomness, parameters, key dependencies, trust boundaries, data states, implementation constraints, crypto-agility, verification, migration, and failure handling.","original_applicability":"Apply when information, identity, communication, software, hardware, transactions, or evidence requires confidentiality, integrity, authenticity, origin binding, controlled disclosure, or tamper detection.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-06-03","REQ-07-03","REQ-07-05","REQ-27-01","REQ-27-02","REQ-27-03","REQ-27-04"],"decision_reason":"Commitments, signatures, custody and distributed authority require distinct crypto properties; full original inspected; deterministic preimages do not establish signature/custody/protocol qualification.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261006_02.md"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/204_KEY_MANAGEMENT.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/204_KEY_MANAGEMENT.txt","sha256":"060113c43066455a5e5a9d6bf2a4be5dc548b40a1451168febf50dc7e1b34cd6","bytes":6594,"section":"204","original_title":"SECTION 204 — Key Management","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":7,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_07_Cybersecurity_through_Privacy_Engineering.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A key lifecycle and trust model identifying key classes, owners, purpose, algorithms, custody, access, state transitions, separation of duties, hardware or service protection, evidence, recovery, and destruction authority.","original_applicability":"Apply when cryptographic keys, certificates, signing identities, tokens, trust anchors, hardware roots, or derived secrets protect data, identity, software, devices, communications, or decisions.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-06-01","REQ-25-01","REQ-25-02","REQ-27-01","REQ-27-02","REQ-27-03","REQ-27-04","REQ-30-04"],"decision_reason":"Installation, signer, custody, publisher and distributed key roles affect trust and recovery; full original inspected; key lifecycle remains open and no production key material was accessed.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261006_02.md"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/205_SECRETS_MANAGEMENT.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/205_SECRETS_MANAGEMENT.txt","sha256":"9b3bb8c17bea07ff8cfb203332481ed3224e18bc1134af56bb6ac8098a704af3","bytes":6860,"section":"205","original_title":"SECTION 205 — Secrets Management","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":7,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_07_Cybersecurity_through_Privacy_Engineering.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A secrets lifecycle with inventory, classification, ownership, approved storage, retrieval, least privilege, injection, rotation, detection, redaction, incident response, recovery, and destruction for every declared environment and consumer.","original_applicability":"Apply whenever a non-public value can authenticate, authorize, decrypt, sign, connect, identify, configure, or otherwise grant access to a system, service, device, data store, provider, or person.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-06-02","REQ-25-01","REQ-29-01"],"decision_reason":"Final runtime secrets and credentials require controlled storage, use and exposure handling; full original inspected; current pure code neither retrieves nor logs secret values, broader controls remain open.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261006_02.md"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/206_SECURITY_OPERATIONS.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/206_SECURITY_OPERATIONS.txt","sha256":"d2876b9a692e67276f709fe180c75efa279b30a9a861e1dc06f002e58288f7d9","bytes":6833,"section":"206","original_title":"SECTION 206 — Security Operations","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":7,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_07_Cybersecurity_through_Privacy_Engineering.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A security-operations model with monitored assets, signal sources, coverage, detection logic, ownership, triage, response authority, escalation, privacy, evidence preservation, continuity, recovery, and measurable gaps.","original_applicability":"Apply when systems, data, identities, devices, applications, networks, providers, or physical assets require ongoing security monitoring, detection, response, assurance, or evidence.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-21-01","REQ-24-03","REQ-28-01","REQ-28-02","REQ-28-03","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-35-03","REQ-36-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Required NIRL monitoring and assumption/evidence propagation govern technical violations and dependent effects. Define actual protected assets, telemetry coverage, source/time/clock basis, normalization, rule/version, missingness, false positives/negatives, operator/review/response authority, privacy and retention. Exercise poisoned/tampered/missing/duplicate/high-volume signals, monitor loss, escalation, stop, containment and recovery. Signal generation grants no containment authority; no alert or absence of alerts proves incident or safety.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_13.md","handoff/volume_vii_reconciliation_20261007_13.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/207_THREAT_INTELLIGENCE.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/207_THREAT_INTELLIGENCE.txt","sha256":"52158f0df7a53e1ff5476f28a9eb1e2eab1e43858512ed3183caf70c00e87176","bytes":6626,"section":"207","original_title":"SECTION 207 — Threat Intelligence","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":7,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_07_Cybersecurity_through_Privacy_Engineering.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A threat-intelligence process with source governance, collection requirements, confidence and provenance, relevance, analysis, dissemination, privacy, handling, action mapping, feedback, and explicit uncertainty.","original_applicability":"Apply when security decisions depend on external or internal information about threats, adversaries, techniques, vulnerabilities, campaigns, abuse, fraud, geopolitical or sector conditions, or emerging risk.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-21-01","REQ-22-04","REQ-24-04","REQ-28-01","REQ-28-02","REQ-35-02","REQ-35-03","REQ-38-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Actual runtime/dependency advisories and technical threat evidence must inform selected assets and release qualification. Define bounded questions/consumers, authorized sources, handling, version/time, confidence/corroboration/contradictions, asset relevance, expiry and action owners. Verify source identity, poisoned/stale/duplicate indicators and correction propagation. A headline/feed/vendor claim/model narrative does not establish attribution, exposure or permission to block. No external intelligence feed, sensitive collection or broad sharing is added; actual advisories must be rechecked before dependent packaging claims.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_13.md","handoff/volume_vii_reconciliation_20261007_13.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/208_THREAT_MODELING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/208_THREAT_MODELING.txt","sha256":"54fce8242c72755d9f609dd400bc8c96fb0ce00089e6dcf99911f35bf01b36ae","bytes":6687,"section":"208","original_title":"SECTION 208 — Threat Modeling","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":7,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_07_Cybersecurity_through_Privacy_Engineering.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A versioned threat model with assets, actors, trust boundaries, entry points, assumptions, threats, abuse cases, impacts, likelihood or uncertainty, mitigations, residual risk, owners, evidence, and reopening conditions.","original_applicability":"Apply when a system, product, process, device, data set, organization, AI capability, or change can create security, safety, privacy, financial, social, operational, or abuse consequences.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-03","REQ-03-04","REQ-16-04","REQ-19-05","REQ-21-01","REQ-21-02","REQ-21-03","REQ-21-04","REQ-22-04","REQ-25-04","REQ-26-04","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-03","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The supplied specification explicitly declares malicious model outputs, hostile data/code, compromised workers and forged IPC. Version actual assets/people/flows/principals/trust domains, attacker/OS/admin/driver/hardware assumptions, threats, impact/uncertainty, controls, owners, hostile tests, residual risk and invalidation triggers. Challenge escape, confused deputy, unauthorized reads/effects, consent forgery, model leakage, custody and failed recovery. Generic checklists, risk scores and threat counts do not prove mitigation or complete coverage.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_13.md","handoff/volume_vii_reconciliation_20261007_13.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/209_VULNERABILITY_MANAGEMENT.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/209_VULNERABILITY_MANAGEMENT.txt","sha256":"70dc340fa0a9277ff606c0f2bd71103186c3de0618eeefc60a2108537ac750d2","bytes":6529,"section":"209","original_title":"SECTION 209 — Vulnerability Management","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":7,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_07_Cybersecurity_through_Privacy_Engineering.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A vulnerability lifecycle with asset coverage, source and finding provenance, severity and exploitability context, owner, deadline, remediation or mitigation, exception, verification, disclosure, evidence, and reopening rules.","original_applicability":"Apply when a system, product, device, dependency, provider, configuration, process, or supplier can contain a weakness that affects security, privacy, safety, availability, or trust.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-07-02","REQ-21-01","REQ-22-04","REQ-23-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-02","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-38-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The product consumes model parsers, Windows/native/Python libraries, packaging tools and update artifacts that can contain material weaknesses. Inventory actual source/loaded/frozen dependencies/configurations/support; retain advisory/finding identity, provenance, exposure/exploitability/impact, owner, remediation/mitigation, exception/expiry and retest. Verify actual changed versions and hostile regression rather than closing on install alone. Clean scans have bounded coverage; no finding is hidden or ignored as existing. Current source assessment supplies no new vulnerability-free or production-ready claim.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_13.md","handoff/volume_vii_reconciliation_20261007_13.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/210_PENETRATION_TESTING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/210_PENETRATION_TESTING.txt","sha256":"568aa0c3ed76d8e53f0ea97573bb126f1755a1be76c087e72785e3723cd2a226","bytes":6516,"section":"210","original_title":"SECTION 210 — Penetration Testing","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":7,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_07_Cybersecurity_through_Privacy_Engineering.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A scoped penetration-test plan and evidence package with authorization, targets, exclusions, safety limits, methods, observations, findings, impact, reproducibility, remediation, retest, and owner acceptance.","original_applicability":"Apply when authorized adversarial testing can materially validate security of applications, networks, devices, APIs, identities, cloud resources, facilities, or operational controls.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-19-01","REQ-19-05","REQ-21-01","REQ-21-02","REQ-21-03","REQ-21-04","REQ-25-04","REQ-27-04","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-03","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The mandatory hostile matrix requires real-boundary testing in isolated candidate environments after implementation. Bind actual owner authorization, targets/versions/accounts, exclusions, methods/rates/data/safety/stop/contact/evidence and environment before execution. Test actual IPC, worker/resource, key/custody, consent and recovery boundaries; safely reproduce material findings and verify remediation. Synthetic contract tests and an isolated clean result remain bounded evidence. No production/external target, persistence, data extraction or offensive exercise is initiated by reconciliation.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_13.md","handoff/volume_vii_reconciliation_20261007_13.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/211_RED_TEAMING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/211_RED_TEAMING.txt","sha256":"6766840e6e0af8cb22a7a503b32ae1eae65d33764c2327f6be1c706453a3db91","bytes":6781,"section":"211","original_title":"SECTION 211 — Red Teaming","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":7,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_07_Cybersecurity_through_Privacy_Engineering.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A governed red-team exercise with objective, threat scenario, authorization, scope, safety boundaries, independent control, rules, evidence, defender interaction, findings, impact, remediation, lessons, and owner decisions.","original_applicability":"Apply when an authorized adversary-emulation exercise can reveal material weaknesses in prevention, detection, response, decision-making, physical security, social process, or recovery.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-17-03","REQ-21-01","REQ-21-03","REQ-24-01","REQ-24-02","REQ-25-04","REQ-27-04","REQ-28-01","REQ-28-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-03","REQ-36-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The product's model/tool/authority/privacy hazards require adversarial system review beyond independent parser cases. Define actual scoped scenario, targets/exclusions, authorized test identity/controller, safeguards, immediate stop, privacy/evidence and defender deconfliction. Evaluate prevention, detection, independent interruption, response and recovery, then retain findings/cleanup/retest/limits. Same-actor checks are labeled self-review. No social/physical deception, intrusion, external-party test or production exercise is authorized or executed by these allocations.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_13.md","handoff/volume_vii_reconciliation_20261007_13.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/212_BLUE_TEAMING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/212_BLUE_TEAMING.txt","sha256":"52c53edc0ed8f6c502316ddd78369dc5b5a1d5362660925bae7579adaa3251b6","bytes":6708,"section":"212","original_title":"SECTION 212 — Blue Teaming","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":7,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_07_Cybersecurity_through_Privacy_Engineering.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A defensive operating model with asset and telemetry coverage, baselines, detections, analyst workflows, response playbooks, hardening, threat-informed validation, evidence, authority, recovery, and measurable improvement.","original_applicability":"Apply when a team or capability is responsible for security monitoring, detection, investigation, hardening, response, resilience, or defensive learning for systems, people, data, devices, or facilities.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-21-01","REQ-28-01","REQ-28-02","REQ-28-03","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-30-03","REQ-35-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-35-03","REQ-36-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"CETA requires technical violation detection, fail-closed dependent effects, explicit containment and owner-controlled restoration. Bind actual coverage, signals, rules/playbooks, operator roles, authority, privacy, evidence, load and assumptions. Test missing/poisoned logs, false positives/negatives, monitor failure, harmful controls, stop, rollback configuration, response, handoff and recovery. No dashboard or installed tool alone establishes defensive capability; failed required monitors block dependent effects while unrelated safe work continues.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_13.md","handoff/volume_vii_reconciliation_20261007_13.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/213_DIGITAL_FORENSICS.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/213_DIGITAL_FORENSICS.txt","sha256":"f586f07357bcc51c4a4a5ad4d318cb718fd1d5ca5786cf5e0a2e7363b9a4759d","bytes":6264,"section":"213","original_title":"SECTION 213 — Digital Forensics","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":7,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_07_Cybersecurity_through_Privacy_Engineering.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A forensic plan and evidence package with authority, scope, preservation, acquisition, integrity, chain of custody, analysis, reporting, access control, retention, disclosure, and limitation records.","original_applicability":"Apply when system, device, cloud, application, network, identity, log, communication, or data artifacts may support incident response, legal action, safety review, fraud investigation, compliance, or learning.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-06-02","REQ-07-03","REQ-13-03","REQ-20-03","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-29-03","REQ-31-01","REQ-31-02","REQ-35-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-03","REQ-19-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Canonical evidence, forensic incident handling, migration provenance and independent history verification support consequential review. Bind actual question, source/snapshot/copy/IDs/hashes, acquisition authority/method/time/tool, custody/access/privacy/retention and observation-versus-inference. Preserve original evidence and alternatives; test corrupted copies, missing metadata, conflicting clocks, reproducibility and report lineage. No broad host/profile acquisition, raw sensitive upload or legal authenticity determination is performed. Ordinary engineering records do not imply forensic certification.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_13.md","handoff/volume_vii_reconciliation_20261007_13.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/214_INCIDENT_RESPONSE.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/214_INCIDENT_RESPONSE.txt","sha256":"4252f568efa7cdadda2508f87a8810e5ff35a18902db34e5d04f6190cc13064e","bytes":6266,"section":"214","original_title":"SECTION 214 — Incident Response","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":7,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_07_Cybersecurity_through_Privacy_Engineering.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An incident-response model with classification, authority, roles, intake, triage, evidence, containment, communication, recovery, legal and privacy coordination, closure, and lessons-learned paths.","original_applicability":"Apply when an actual or suspected event may violate security, privacy, safety, availability, policy, law, contract, user trust, or organizational control.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-07-03","REQ-20-01","REQ-20-04","REQ-25-01","REQ-27-03","REQ-28-01","REQ-28-02","REQ-28-03","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-30-03","REQ-30-04","REQ-35-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Loss of authority, custody, monitor, privacy, worker integrity or trusted history requires preserved containment and recovery. Bind actual suspected/confirmed/disproved/unknown state, case/time/source, severity rationale, affected scope/people, responders/authority, evidence, actions, communications and restoration/closure. Exercise degraded telemetry, intake/escalation, independent stop, key/history/worker failure, protected evidence and reconciliation. Preserve drafts/uncertain effects and meaningful owner decisions. No external notification, allegation or real incident declaration occurs now.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_13.md","handoff/volume_vii_reconciliation_20261007_13.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/215_FRAUD_PREVENTION.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/215_FRAUD_PREVENTION.txt","sha256":"50f699a34f1127be432c3ee17c9c0da362e4e1d9be61666455e71606b6dd2670","bytes":6269,"section":"215","original_title":"SECTION 215 — Fraud Prevention","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":7,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_07_Cybersecurity_through_Privacy_Engineering.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A fraud-prevention model with protected outcomes, threat and abuse scenarios, signals, decision thresholds, human review, user communication, appeal, evidence, privacy, model monitoring, recovery, and accountability.","original_applicability":"Apply when systems detect, prevent, investigate, or respond to fraud involving accounts, payments, identity, transactions, content, suppliers, benefits, or organizational resources.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-13-05","REQ-19-01","REQ-19-05","REQ-21-01","REQ-21-03","REQ-24-05","REQ-28-01","REQ-28-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-32-03","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The required attacker model includes forged approvals/receipts and unauthorized identity/transaction attempts affecting CETA resources. Declare actual technical deception scenarios, protected outcomes, source/rule versions, uncertainty, false positives/negatives, action owner, review, explanation/correction and recovery. Validate counterfeit capabilities/receipts/approval channels at actual boundaries. Do not create a payment-fraud product, infer sensitive traits, accuse the user or equate anger/disagreement/anomalies with fraud. Weak signals cannot become final denial authority or covert feedback training.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_13.md","handoff/volume_vii_reconciliation_20261007_13.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/216_ABUSE_PREVENTION.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/216_ABUSE_PREVENTION.txt","sha256":"a5e51839232900dedb74d13e91797cc2dded60bdd85cd0d25725ecb7073f67fb","bytes":6104,"section":"216","original_title":"SECTION 216 — Abuse Prevention","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":7,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_07_Cybersecurity_through_Privacy_Engineering.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An abuse-prevention model with abuse taxonomy, affected parties, signals, reporting, triage, user protection, enforcement, appeal, escalation, privacy, evidence, recovery, and continuous review.","original_applicability":"Apply when users, operators, suppliers, agents, or external actors can misuse a product, platform, process, facility, data set, or organizational capability to harm people, property, systems, or trust.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-13-02","REQ-13-05","REQ-17-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-21-01","REQ-24-05","REQ-28-01","REQ-28-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-32-03","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Untrusted model/workers/tools can misuse product capabilities, while owner intent and legitimate conversation must remain distinguishable from technical violations. Define actual capability misuse/harm taxonomy, affected parties, evidence/source/context, technical controls, report/review/correction/appeal where consequential and required support. Test injection, forged signals, ambiguity, false positives/negatives, access revocation and restoration. Profanity, unusual questions, criticism or one feedback event imply neither compromise nor hostile intent. No new community moderation, surveillance, user accusation or irreversible semantic enforcement is introduced.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_13.md","handoff/volume_vii_reconciliation_20261007_13.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/217_TRUST_AND_SAFETY.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/217_TRUST_AND_SAFETY.txt","sha256":"1233209e0245727436a14f081a06165f473af8beaedcce1d608f4ad16c85339d","bytes":6158,"section":"217","original_title":"SECTION 217 — Trust and Safety","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":7,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_07_Cybersecurity_through_Privacy_Engineering.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A trust-and-safety model with harms, affected parties, policies, controls, reporting, review, escalation, transparency, appeal, measurement, incident response, recovery, and accountable ownership.","original_applicability":"Apply when a product, service, platform, organization, AI capability, or decision process can affect people, public trust, rights, safety, dignity, access, or community conditions.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-13-02","REQ-13-03","REQ-13-04","REQ-13-05","REQ-17-02","REQ-19-05","REQ-24-01","REQ-28-01","REQ-28-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-32-03","REQ-32-04","REQ-35-03","REQ-19-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Companion reasoning, personalization, model-directed actions and user controls affect trust, privacy, access and safety. Map actual affected users/non-users, foreseeable harms, policies, evidence, review, accessible explanations/reporting/correction, appeal/reconsideration, support, incidents and recovery. Test emotional pressure, sycophancy, unsupported surveillance/protection/qualification claims, false-positive restrictions, stale evidence and effective stop. Reports/ratings/policy presence cannot establish safety; actual controls and retained uncertainty govern status.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_13.md","handoff/volume_vii_reconciliation_20261007_13.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/218_PRIVACY_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/218_PRIVACY_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"212cd89ed1b534fd1d5821f02f75f4898c2514d8ffc17c020f3147718fa1a99c","bytes":6409,"section":"218","original_title":"SECTION 218 — Privacy Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":7,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_07_Cybersecurity_through_Privacy_Engineering.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A privacy-engineering model with purpose, data inventory, lawful or authorized basis, minimization, notice, choice, access, correction, retention, deletion, security, sharing, automation, incident, and evidence controls.","original_applicability":"Apply whenever information can identify, describe, infer about, locate, affect, or be linked to a person, household, device, organization, or protected group.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-07-01","REQ-11-02","REQ-12-03","REQ-12-04","REQ-16-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-25-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-29-03","REQ-33-01","REQ-33-02","REQ-35-03","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"CETA processes linkable conversations, preferences, files, embeddings, outputs, observations and evidence under user control. Inventory actual source/class/purpose/subject/processor/flows and authority without inferring lawful basis or consent. Enforce minimization, authorized retrieval, project/user/session isolation, notice/choice, correction, scoped non-overwriting export, revocation, retention and deletion including indexes/caches/backups. Test stale grants, identity mismatch, changed purpose, inference leakage, model reuse and restore. Notices, deletion events and valid shapes do not prove actual rights handling or forgetting.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261007_13.md","handoff/volume_vii_reconciliation_20261007_13.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/219_LEGAL.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/219_LEGAL.txt","sha256":"5df11cbecb68d5de4a24273f005f8885633d4365ac09fb4ffca71d86004b473e","bytes":6205,"section":"219","original_title":"SECTION 219 — Legal","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A legal-obligation map with jurisdictions, parties, claims, contracts, notices, approvals, privacy, safety, IP, records, regulatory, dispute, and escalation requirements, clearly marked as legal advice or unresolved counsel questions.","original_applicability":"Apply when law, regulation, contract, rights, litigation, investigation, licensing, intellectual property, employment, safety, privacy, public communication, or jurisdiction affects the scope or consequences.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-23-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-31-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-38-04","REQ-40-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The desktop product uses third-party material, protected user information, approvals and distribution paths; legal applicability must remain attributable to an exact activity and reviewer. Maintain scoped obligation/source/version/owner/jurisdiction/party/fact/contract/notice/deadline/hold/dispute/exception records and qualified interpretation boundaries. Do not invent applicable law, privilege, counsel, permission or legal sufficiency. Engineering checks and factual inventories remain distinct from legal determination, external communication and release approval.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/220_REGULATORY_COMPLIANCE.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/220_REGULATORY_COMPLIANCE.txt","sha256":"d9dc9c36bf8af83273926c89d8eff5f767b5692684bdb876ca800dc9c9288d95","bytes":5869,"section":"220","original_title":"SECTION 220 — Regulatory Compliance","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A regulatory register mapping jurisdiction, authority, obligation, scope, control, owner, evidence, cadence, reporting, exception, remediation, and change trigger.","original_applicability":"Apply when a regulator, statute, rule, license, order, standard adopted by contract, or public obligation affects the system, organization, product, data, or process.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-16-03","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-04","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01"],"decision_reason":"Obligation and compliance claims require scope, jurisdiction, entity, activity, population, time and current evidence; no sector-specific regime is presumed. Bind applicable criteria to source versions, owner, exact control, cadence, population, period, sample, report, exception/expiry and remediation. Separate design from operation and require qualified interpretation/attestation. Reopen after changed rules, entity, activity, data or claims; do not make blanket compliance or certification assertions.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/221_POLICY.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/221_POLICY.txt","sha256":"81363be7ec3341f3089590257037128c911a45a1aab6811504a3d0fd0fd5c11d","bytes":5725,"section":"221","original_title":"SECTION 221 — Policy","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A policy lifecycle with purpose, scope, authority, definitions, obligations, exceptions, enforcement, implementation owners, communication, evidence, review, appeal, change, and retirement.","original_applicability":"Apply when a rule, standard, principle, commitment, restriction, or decision framework governs people, systems, data, products, operations, suppliers, or agents.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-16-01","REQ-16-02","REQ-16-03","REQ-16-04","REQ-17-02","REQ-19-05","REQ-32-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The deterministic kernel and owner controls operate binding policy; drafts and model interpretations need separate status. Map purpose/scope/authority/definitions/source/version/effective time, constraints, ambiguity/conflict/dissent, exceptions, communication, accessibility, appeal, review and retirement to current policy records. Pin evaluated IR/rules and invalidate affected evidence on amendments. Model drafting cannot self-approve binding rules or turn temporary exceptions permanent.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/222_ETHICS.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/222_ETHICS.txt","sha256":"57196a9783708f55daed659dcd984c72de0524c0f2abfd8ee9af698af04ee97e","bytes":5956,"section":"222","original_title":"SECTION 222 — Ethics","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An ethics assessment with human purpose, affected parties, values, options, harms, benefits, uncertainty, dissent, safeguards, decision authority, monitoring, appeal, and reconsideration.","original_applicability":"Apply when choices affect people, rights, dignity, safety, opportunity, privacy, communities, environment, future users, or power relationships, especially when automation or AI influences outcomes.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-13-02","REQ-17-01","REQ-17-03","REQ-28-01","REQ-28-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-32-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"CETA's interpretations, memory, recommendations and actions affect users and potentially others; benefit, harm and agency need contextual evidence. Record actual purpose, affected people/non-users, alternatives, values, power, harms, benefits, uncertainty, dissent, safeguards, monitoring, recourse and accountable tradeoff. Preserve accessible stop/correction/appeal controls and human impact review. Do not fabricate consultation, consensus, ethical certification or psychological motives, or infer acceptability from a technical score or legal permission.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/223_INTELLECTUAL_PROPERTY.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/223_INTELLECTUAL_PROPERTY.txt","sha256":"7ed651b23827d90d0390d77c407e05d74a85ea568ee115ad999f8f0f0a827fe5","bytes":5970,"section":"223","original_title":"SECTION 223 — Intellectual Property","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An IP register with works, inventions, marks, data, model or training material, owners, contributors, provenance, rights, restrictions, licenses, approvals, confidentiality, publication, enforcement, and evidence.","original_applicability":"Apply when the work creates, uses, modifies, distributes, trains on, embeds, names, publishes, or derives value from potentially protected works, inventions, data, marks, or confidential material.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-23-01","REQ-23-04","REQ-29-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-38-02","REQ-38-04","REQ-40-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Supplied sources, dependencies, model assets and generated/shipped work have provenance and possible rights restrictions. Link actual assets/versions/authors/contributors/source, rights/restrictions/licenses/contracts, confidentiality, notices, approvals and distribution. Preserve attribution and source boundary authority in builds and exports; hold uncertain use/publication for the required decision. Record downstream withdrawal and reopening on contributor, source, license or claim changes; no ownership/originality inference from URLs or generated output.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/224_LICENSING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/224_LICENSING.txt","sha256":"4ea7ea16632553d7967248b54cd46209ef5aa408f4ec8bc0e4a3f2a53a0b3d26","bytes":5663,"section":"224","original_title":"SECTION 224 — Licensing","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A license inventory and compliance model with asset, version, licensor, rights, restrictions, notices, obligations, consumers, distribution, approval, renewal, exception, and evidence.","original_applicability":"Apply when the work consumes, modifies, embeds, distributes, trains on, publishes, or operates licensed software, data, content, models, APIs, hardware, or services.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-23-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-38-02","REQ-38-04","REQ-38-05","REQ-40-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Runtime, tools, models and delivered source companions consume and may distribute licensed material. Inventory direct/transitive asset identities, captured license text/licensor/version/source/contract, permitted consumers, distribution, obligations/notices/restrictions, renewal/termination and approved exceptions. Bind compatibility review and notice package to actual built bytes; resolve ambiguous terms through qualified review. Preserve termination/withdrawal/remediation and do not assume licensing from package names.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/225_RECORDS_MANAGEMENT.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/225_RECORDS_MANAGEMENT.txt","sha256":"d1071dcb82f9b8a0eeb1d7e1ce051ee0d30c6baca68f57e1e6da587cec1776fc","bytes":5746,"section":"225","original_title":"SECTION 225 — Records Management","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A records model with record classes, owners, authoritative copies, metadata, retention, legal hold, access, integrity, disposition, audit, continuity, and exception rules.","original_applicability":"Apply when information documents business, legal, regulatory, financial, safety, security, product, user, operational, or governance activity or must be preserved for accountability.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-07-01","REQ-07-03","REQ-12-03","REQ-29-02","REQ-29-03","REQ-31-01","REQ-31-02","REQ-30-03","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Canonical evidence, history, exports, backups, migration and user payload retention need distinct authoritative records and disposition rules. Record classes/source/authority/owner/metadata/access/integrity, schedules/retention/holds/jurisdiction/transfer/disposition, exceptions and retrieval. Preserve hold checks and explicit authority before reclassification, disclosure or destruction. Separate operational data, records, protected payloads, indexes, backup and archive; explain remaining retained copies and recover failed/partial disposition without silent loss.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/226_AUDIT.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/226_AUDIT.txt","sha256":"a3c18d6701fc3bd1dd71844f84ec40e46e44ad0f5008d7a539579133d1391b3f","bytes":5567,"section":"226","original_title":"SECTION 226 — Audit","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An audit scope, criteria, independence statement, evidence plan, sampling method, procedures, findings, management response, remediation, follow-up, and residual-risk record.","original_applicability":"Apply when independent assurance is needed for material controls, obligations, risks, financial or operational claims, safety, security, privacy, quality, or governance.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-17-03","REQ-27-04","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-03","REQ-36-04","REQ-39-01","REQ-40-03","REQ-41-02","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Material governance, security, privacy, quality and release claims require independent evidence examination rather than self-certification. Bind criteria/scope/period/population/sample/source/method/reviewer/independence/confidentiality to workpapers, reproducible sampling, findings, management response, due owner, remediation and follow-up. Preserve contradictions and late evidence through amendments/reopened conclusions. Current executor review remains self-review; no audit opinion, external attestation or independent closure is fabricated.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/227_INTERNAL_CONTROLS.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/227_INTERNAL_CONTROLS.txt","sha256":"caaa5d5091b8023abc0e940395141491c4a46e8a51e6f41305237363065d3d66","bytes":5766,"section":"227","original_title":"SECTION 227 — Internal Controls","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A control framework with objectives, risks, control owners, preventive and detective activities, segregation of duties, evidence, frequency, exceptions, testing, remediation, and management review.","original_applicability":"Apply when governance, financial, operational, security, privacy, safety, quality, compliance, or trust outcomes require repeatable control.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-16-03","REQ-19-02","REQ-20-01","REQ-21-01","REQ-25-03","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-03","REQ-41-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Current authority, identity, privacy, custody, recovery and quality depend on repeatable preventive/detective controls. Link objective/risk/obligation/process/system/control/owner/operator, segregation, frequency/evidence/test population and period, exceptions/expiry/compensating controls and remediation. Test design and actual operation, overrides/failure/recovery/change impact. Preserve independent challenge and management decisions; activity completion or configuration presence cannot self-attest operation.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/228_QUALITY_MANAGEMENT.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/228_QUALITY_MANAGEMENT.txt","sha256":"9048dbe3249f6184fda6f86a08fbcfe56a07e0ee0bbdcfdee8aa41e6a05b16e6","bytes":5585,"section":"228","original_title":"SECTION 228 — Quality Management","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A quality-management system with quality characteristics, owners, criteria, measures, reviews, nonconformance, corrective action, escalation, records, and continuous-improvement decisions.","original_applicability":"Apply when a product, service, process, system, artifact, or decision has quality expectations, acceptance risk, repeatable work, or consequences from defect or variation.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-24-01","REQ-24-03","REQ-32-04","REQ-34-01","REQ-36-02","REQ-39-04","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01"],"decision_reason":"The whole product has user, semantic, security, accessibility, reliability, maintainability and lifecycle quality obligations. Use existing requirement/evidence/issue ledgers for characteristics, definitions/populations/periods/thresholds, review, nonconformance, defects/causes, corrective/preventive actions, escalation, owner tradeoffs and reopening. Preserve conflicting signals and failed runs; no metric, checklist or schedule decides release. Actual owner/independent review remains separately recorded.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/229_QUALITY_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/229_QUALITY_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"24cd9779c4f19b472365c92671de6fc701e60aaf9d5be418e666bdbd3add5c7c","bytes":5544,"section":"229","original_title":"SECTION 229 — Quality Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A quality-engineering approach that links risks and quality characteristics to design choices, controls, tests, observability, defect prevention, maintainability, and measurable outcomes.","original_applicability":"Apply when quality must be designed into software, hardware, data, processes, services, AI, or operations rather than inspected only after production.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-04-03","REQ-20-02","REQ-32-04","REQ-34-04","REQ-35-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-02","REQ-39-02","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Quality must be built into interfaces, state, observability and failure handling before wider runtime integration. Link characteristic/risk to architecture/control/test/environment, defect causes and safe experiments. Expose stable contracts, bounded fault seams, state/errors, telemetry and rollback while preserving production authority/privacy. Require representative scenarios, specialist/user judgment and independent reproduction for material claims; generated checks cannot define quality by themselves.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/230_QUALITY_ASSURANCE.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/230_QUALITY_ASSURANCE.txt","sha256":"614de3a03e7bbb35ed76469e47480f84e8c8c6151ad1fd5903a402e2192835b9","bytes":5185,"section":"230","original_title":"SECTION 230 — Quality Assurance","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A quality-assurance plan with independence, criteria, reviews, test oversight, evidence, nonconformance, escalation, release or acceptance input, and follow-up.","original_applicability":"Apply when independent review or assurance is needed for quality, safety, security, privacy, compliance, user impact, release, or material operational claims.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-17-03","REQ-36-03","REQ-36-04","REQ-39-01","REQ-40-03","REQ-41-02","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"A finished product requires challenge of criteria, tests, observations and evidence by the applicable reviewers. Preserve criteria/scope/independence/access/confidentiality/sample/reviewer/findings, corrective follow-up, release recommendation and accountable acceptance. Separate automated verification, sequential self-review, independent assurance and human release decision. Unsupported assurance is withdrawn or amended and reopened on changed evidence/baseline; do not sign for the owner.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/231_SOFTWARE_TESTING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/231_SOFTWARE_TESTING.txt","sha256":"061f7ad3b6ce050a73e542cb2c27ae7ad35d7b0c7316b5b28f7965718fd60091","bytes":5295,"section":"231","original_title":"SECTION 231 — Software Testing","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A software test strategy with scope, risks, levels, environments, data, oracles, automation, manual judgment, evidence, defects, coverage, exit criteria, and limitations.","original_applicability":"Apply when software behavior, change, dependency, configuration, interface, model, or operational path can affect a declared outcome.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-36-01","REQ-36-02","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-02","REQ-40-02","REQ-40-03","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"All executable components and behavior changes require truthful risk, oracle, fixture and environment coverage. Cover functional/boundary/invalid/state/error/security/accessibility/performance/recovery behavior with explicit authority/data handling. Bind actual execution to source/version/case/oracle/environment/actor/output, failures/flakiness/defects/retests/coverage/exclusions and exit criteria. Keep representative manual/domain judgment alongside automation; generated cases and counts are not execution or acceptance.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/232_HARDWARE_TESTING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/232_HARDWARE_TESTING.txt","sha256":"c370adfe98e5a0d8b36995baef4073b710cacb41258767028addaaadf60d9ac6","bytes":5480,"section":"232","original_title":"SECTION 232 — Hardware Testing","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A hardware-test strategy with representative units, fixtures, instrumentation, conditions, limits, safety controls, data integrity, failures, coverage, acceptance, and lifecycle limitations.","original_applicability":"Apply when physical components, boards, devices, sensors, actuators, enclosures, interfaces, or manufacturing variation affect a requirement or operational outcome.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-23-02","REQ-25-03","REQ-25-04","REQ-26-02","REQ-27-04","REQ-33-03","REQ-37-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Selected devices, hardware custody/anchoring, CPU/GPU placement and physical adapters have actual physical and interface claims. Bind units/revisions/lots/BOM/conditions/environment/load/fixture/instrument/calibration/operator/hazards, safe limits/stop/recovery, sample variation and acceptance. Use qualified authority for hazardous/destructive tests and actual supported hardware evidence; simulations remain labeled fixtures. Required unavailable hardware keeps its lane and promotion obligations open, with no substitution of bench or mock evidence for field claims.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/233_UNIT_TESTING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/233_UNIT_TESTING.txt","sha256":"2a7714994b5c13231d5625ad258cda68aa769a8fe2aff508c9697d954f5eb7f1","bytes":4732,"section":"233","original_title":"SECTION 233 — Unit Testing","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"Fast, deterministic unit tests with clear subject, fixture, oracle, boundary cases, failure evidence, ownership, maintenance, and known limits.","original_applicability":"Apply when an isolated unit has meaningful behavior, contract, risk, or defect history that can be tested independently.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-06-03","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-02","REQ-40-03","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Pure contracts and isolated components have behavior suitable for precise unit validation. Bind unit/version/contract/oracle/fixture/framework/environment/substitutions, normal/boundary/invalid/error/state cases, execution/failure/flakiness and limitations. Maintain stable contract-focused tests without unsafe test-only paths or over-mocking. Existing 123 contract tests are historical bounded foundation evidence; they do not establish integration, security, human acceptance or complete source conformance.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/234_INTEGRATION_TESTING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/234_INTEGRATION_TESTING.txt","sha256":"c6a1ad27c9946ea2693d03bc81dd39c4679c2158a1af54e9985542efced86bae","bytes":4997,"section":"234","original_title":"SECTION 234 — Integration Testing","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An integration-test model with participating versions, interfaces, fixtures, environments, data, dependency behavior, observability, failure paths, results, and limitations.","original_applicability":"Apply when two or more components, services, devices, teams, providers, data stores, or processes interact through a contract.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-04-04","REQ-07-01","REQ-19-02","REQ-20-04","REQ-21-03","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-02","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The store, kernel, authenticated IPC, supervisor, workers, adapters and UI must exchange state and identity correctly. Record participating identities/versions/contracts/schema/semantics/data/environment, ordering/duplicates/timeouts/retries/version skew/provider loss/rollback, traces and recovery. Declare substitute fidelity and use real public paths for integration claims. Preserve current permissions and no-reexecution semantics under failure; syntax/serializer agreement alone is insufficient.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/235_SYSTEM_TESTING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/235_SYSTEM_TESTING.txt","sha256":"fc27e1fe440390bda5f7c39b701f5696e43b72105f8a8d3856a78e01e220db92","bytes":5045,"section":"235","original_title":"SECTION 235 — System Testing","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A system-test baseline with versioned system, configuration, interfaces, data, users, scenarios, environment, results, defects, coverage, acceptance, and limitations.","original_applicability":"Apply when an assembled system or service has meaningful functional, quality, safety, security, operational, or user outcomes.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-04-04","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-37-02","REQ-41-03","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The assembled native application must meet functional, security, privacy, accessibility, performance and lifecycle outcomes together. Bind system/configuration/versions/users/scenarios/data/interfaces/dependencies/environment/oracles/exit criteria to actual execution and observed defects. Exercise normal/boundary/failure/operator/security/safety/accessibility/recovery paths, trace coverage/exclusions, reset and reproducibility; source/unit/integration passes cannot replace whole-system evidence.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/236_END_TO_END_TESTING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/236_END_TO_END_TESTING.txt","sha256":"9da0c68fca5c32a63fca5719f3fd18d77fcbfeb3a5286746902204a5decdc59c","bytes":4972,"section":"236","original_title":"SECTION 236 — End-to-End Testing","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An end-to-end test model with journey, actors, versions, dependencies, data, environment, expected outcome, evidence, failure and recovery behavior, and user acceptance limits.","original_applicability":"Apply when a material outcome crosses multiple components, teams, providers, roles, or lifecycle states and must be validated as experienced.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-32-01","REQ-32-04","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-02","REQ-41-03","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Users need the whole path from scope selection and observation through approval/effect/readback and later explanation. Record journey/actors/roles/steps/data/versions/dependencies/environment/expected and observed outcomes, actual user-visible errors, accessibility/support/cancellation/recovery and cleanup. Use realistic scope and declared substitute fidelity. Automation completion does not prove user meaning, comprehension or full end-to-end acceptance.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/237_ACCEPTANCE_TESTING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/237_ACCEPTANCE_TESTING.txt","sha256":"6d92eb5e997dd2f5fbff251b3e5cb806a8b65fe66c78f4154be9b1d9569dfea9","bytes":5268,"section":"237","original_title":"SECTION 237 — Acceptance Testing","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An acceptance model with decision owner, user or stakeholder scenarios, criteria, evidence, exceptions, unresolved issues, accessibility, operational readiness, and explicit accept, reject, or conditional decision.","original_applicability":"Apply before a product, service, process, system, or change is accepted for use, release, transition, funding, or operational ownership.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-19-05","REQ-32-04","REQ-37-02","REQ-40-03","REQ-41-02","REQ-41-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01"],"decision_reason":"Adoption/release needs accountable users/owners to assess the declared outcomes and limitations. Confirm authority/criteria/representative users and contexts, scenarios/evidence, comprehension/accessibility, defects/dissent, operational readiness/training/support/recovery, explicit accept/reject/conditional decision, exception owner/expiry and reopening. Technical execution cannot simulate consent or sign off on behalf of participants or the owner.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/238_REGRESSION_TESTING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/238_REGRESSION_TESTING.txt","sha256":"5657e2055c644e3f9fade43fa0e363f72b19ead31fca27b8df1da5ff995b087a","bytes":4874,"section":"238","original_title":"SECTION 238 — Regression Testing","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A risk-based regression suite and review process tied to change impact, versions, environments, defects, coverage, exclusions, results, and owner decision.","original_applicability":"Apply when code, hardware, data, configuration, dependency, policy, model, provider, environment, or operational change may affect existing behavior.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-16-01","REQ-24-01","REQ-24-04","REQ-36-02","REQ-40-03","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Code, model, data, configuration, policy, dependencies and environment can affect prior behavior. Map actual diffs/dependencies/critical journeys/previous defects to selected cases and any justified full suite, with baseline/versions/fixtures/environment/exclusions/quarantine/flakiness/owner/exit criteria. Preserve historical small-model failures and repaired deny conditions, changed semantics/version/migration and differential evidence; do not remove failed cases to qualify.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/239_PERFORMANCE_TESTING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/239_PERFORMANCE_TESTING.txt","sha256":"3ac21f6bb4edede592f7571040666dd8f69e60619f402a88d0b9edb4573bb06a","bytes":5076,"section":"239","original_title":"SECTION 239 — Performance Testing","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A performance-test model with workload, scenarios, service levels, environment, instrumentation, baselines, variability, bottleneck analysis, evidence, and limits.","original_applicability":"Apply when response time, throughput, resource use, capacity, cost, or user experience is material to the capability.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-23-02","REQ-23-03","REQ-34-01","REQ-34-02","REQ-34-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Responsiveness, local inference, resource use and stop/recovery responsiveness are material product qualities. Freeze machine/profile/workload/metric/targets before tuning and retain ratification state. Measure actual stages, cold/warm/cache states, relevant histories, at least30 samples for p95 and adequate explicit samples for p99, failures/timeouts/resource pressure, variability/user impact and limits. Fast incorrect outputs cannot qualify; no paid/shared/production load is launched by this assessment.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/240_LOAD_TESTING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/240_LOAD_TESTING.txt","sha256":"ae58a38c65bcf76fe6d1db90a0bedaed4f59772945ca1415d1f6a7eee66a1a6c","bytes":4829,"section":"240","original_title":"SECTION 240 — Load Testing","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A load-test plan with workload model, ramp and duration, environment, data, service objectives, instrumentation, safety controls, results, bottlenecks, and capacity decision.","original_applicability":"Apply when concurrent users, requests, jobs, devices, events, or transactions can affect capacity, latency, cost, or reliability.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-08-02","REQ-19-03","REQ-34-02","REQ-34-03","REQ-34-04","REQ-36-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Concurrent tasks, events, model work and UI actions can exhaust queues and shared recovery reserves. Define local workload arrival/ramp/concurrency/duration/data mix/limits/generator validation, isolated target/dependencies, authority/stop/safety/resource/cost and service outcomes. Measure queues, latency, errors and recovery under sustained realistic load. Protect external/shared resources and retain limits; no capacity conclusion extends beyond tested profiles.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/241_STRESS_TESTING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/241_STRESS_TESTING.txt","sha256":"ccffcf883b92f1481cdb5987ac4968e1fde83f9a81e942b66566a0d57717896b","bytes":5143,"section":"241","original_title":"SECTION 241 — Stress Testing","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A stress-test model with overload or adverse condition, safety boundaries, observable thresholds, degradation expectations, recovery, resource exhaustion behavior, evidence, and owner decision.","original_applicability":"Apply when overload, dependency loss, resource exhaustion, failure combination, extreme input, or environmental boundary can affect safety, continuity, integrity, or service.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-07-04","REQ-19-03","REQ-20-04","REQ-30-01","REQ-30-03","REQ-34-04","REQ-36-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Overload, missing dependencies, malformed inputs and resource loss can undermine authority and durable outcomes. Plan isolated stress scenario/trigger/limit/data/dependencies, stop/restore/safety/communication authority and expected degradation. Observe integrity, queue/retry/resource behavior, halt/reconcile/restore and return-to-service; preserve traces and adverse findings. Never inject host-wide or production destruction or call a simulation full resilience.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/242_SCALABILITY_TESTING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/242_SCALABILITY_TESTING.txt","sha256":"9e6148fa9838450c4eb5609da406d84eadcf6095a1378385afbfa54e03267f21","bytes":5509,"section":"242","original_title":"SECTION 242 — Scalability Testing","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A scalability model with growth dimensions, workload projection, architecture assumptions, scale mechanism, limits, service objectives, cost, data behavior, operational burden, and evidence.","original_applicability":"Apply when expected or strategic growth can affect performance, reliability, cost, privacy, security, data lifecycle, operations, or user experience.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-07-04","REQ-12-03","REQ-29-02","REQ-34-02","REQ-34-03","REQ-34-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"History, memory/index volume, task/event counts and local workload grow over the product lifetime. Record actual growth dimensions/horizon/projections/assumptions, representative scale steps, 10k/100k labeled synthetic histories, resources/latency/cost/operator burden/security/privacy/data integrity and recovery. Measure nonlinear limits and capacity choices rather than extrapolating universal traffic/tenant/geography support. Resource changes and customer commitments need the applicable decision.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/243_RELIABILITY_TESTING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/243_RELIABILITY_TESTING.txt","sha256":"15fa66a9b977cc02b809cbdc213f13335dae1de26aec1aa2aee6aa6565b5336b","bytes":5275,"section":"243","original_title":"SECTION 243 — Reliability Testing","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A reliability-test model with failure definition, workload, duration, environment, fault assumptions, service objectives, data integrity, repair or recovery behavior, evidence, and limits.","original_applicability":"Apply when continuity, failure frequency, durability, correctness over time, maintenance, or recovery is material to people, service, equipment, data, or trust.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-07-02","REQ-08-03","REQ-30-03","REQ-34-04","REQ-37-03","REQ-40-03","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Correct operation over time, durable history, restart/recovery and the required seven-day campaign are product obligations. Define failure/workload/duration/exposure/sample/fault/environment/maintenance/service objective, monitor intermittent and semantic failures, integrity/repair/recovery, uncertainty and field limits. Run the exact installed seven-day controlled campaign only after prerequisite gates; accelerated clocks and uptime alone are not elapsed endurance or reliability proof.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/244_RESILIENCE_TESTING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/244_RESILIENCE_TESTING.txt","sha256":"e2f7fc6bdd3a391472824a0ba6debbd1d1dbaaf8b54215f223f8c27d66447dcc","bytes":5209,"section":"244","original_title":"SECTION 244 — Resilience Testing","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A resilience-test model with disruption scenarios, protected outcomes, dependencies, degradation, continuity, recovery, communications, evidence, owners, and residual-risk decision.","original_applicability":"Apply when disruption, dependency loss, resource failure, human absence, attack, environmental change, or organizational shock can affect essential outcomes.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-07-04","REQ-19-02","REQ-25-03","REQ-26-04","REQ-30-03","REQ-35-02","REQ-37-02","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Required disruption handling must preserve authority, integrity, privacy, user agency and recovery in addition to availability. Map essential outcomes/modes/dependencies/common failure, scenario/environment/authority/stop, staffing/communication/runbooks, degradation/failover/backup/restore/reconciliation and residual impact. Exercise control-plane independence and user-visible recovery under bounded candidate faults. Reopen correlated failure assumptions and do not hide data loss behind uptime.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/245_CHAOS_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/245_CHAOS_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"46036afcc3f127bb208491d2e792014a9a754b47b22b3d3deed2f2d410eb52e2","bytes":5178,"section":"245","original_title":"SECTION 245 — Chaos Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A governed chaos experiment with steady-state hypothesis, scope, authorization, blast radius, safety, abort, observability, result, learning, remediation, and repeatability.","original_applicability":"Apply when controlled disruption can safely answer a material resilience or operational question that ordinary testing cannot.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-20-04","REQ-28-03","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-40-03","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Controlled candidate disruption can test material resilience hypotheses not answered by ordinary checks. Record steady-state hypothesis/target/version/conditions, exact authority/blast radius/data/environment, live observability/controller/abort/restore/communication/incident conversion, timeline/observed impact/learning/remediation/repeatability. Begin with the smallest isolated experiment; no live/shared target, privilege escalation or adverse experiment is initiated by reconciliation.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/246_SECURITY_TESTING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/246_SECURITY_TESTING.txt","sha256":"62e408e8397e0ec670ddd762c3da4b6cf745287d94c3020af5d5fdf0824e7c6f","bytes":5115,"section":"246","original_title":"SECTION 246 — Security Testing","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A risk-based security-test plan and evidence package with scope, threat basis, authorization, methods, findings, severity, remediation, retest, limitations, and owner decision.","original_applicability":"Apply when a material security property, trust boundary, identity, data, interface, dependency, configuration, or defensive control changes or requires assurance.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-19-05","REQ-21-01","REQ-21-03","REQ-21-04","REQ-27-02","REQ-27-04","REQ-36-03","REQ-36-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Authority, Windows principals, authenticated IPC, storage, crypto/custody and data boundaries need actual adversarial control evidence. Bind threat/asset/version/configuration/identity/method/authorization/environment/data/exclusions/stop/sensitive evidence to findings/severity/remediation/retest/cleanup and independent review. Exercise forged/replayed/cross-scope/stale messages, hostile input, path races, monitor loss and recovery on bounded candidate targets. No scanner, parser or self-review proves full security.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/247_ACCESSIBILITY_TESTING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/247_ACCESSIBILITY_TESTING.txt","sha256":"6e95737b19e1362de5c77101bd90e017be9bd57b86d0c9fa16f1f1e94f15c0e2","bytes":5709,"section":"247","original_title":"SECTION 247 — Accessibility Testing","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An accessibility-test model with users, standards, journeys, assistive technology, environments, criteria, defects, accommodations, evidence, and owner decision.","original_applicability":"Apply to user interfaces, documentation, devices, services, communication, support, physical environments, data presentations, and AI interactions intended for or affecting people.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-19-05","REQ-30-01","REQ-32-02","REQ-32-03","REQ-32-04","REQ-33-01","REQ-37-02","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Conversation, setup, approvals, models, memory/evidence, stop and recovery are person-facing control surfaces. Record declared users/platform/assistive technology/version/criteria/journeys/method, keyboard/focus/non-visual/scaling/contrast/timing/language/errors/authentication and alternatives, real findings/severity/accommodations/expiry. Use actual assistive technology and appropriate qualified/user input; static inspection and simulated participants cannot establish accessibility acceptance.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/248_COMPATIBILITY_TESTING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/248_COMPATIBILITY_TESTING.txt","sha256":"97a06a58922d74ab3e5244da7f34c8524deaf0ba9ca87a3d29ac1a92c9f1c0ca","bytes":5059,"section":"248","original_title":"SECTION 248 — Compatibility Testing","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A compatibility matrix with supported combinations, assumptions, contracts, prioritized coverage, results, known incompatibilities, migration or fallback, and owner decision.","original_applicability":"Apply when users, systems, devices, providers, formats, environments, or versions must interoperate or remain supported across change.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-01","REQ-22-01","REQ-23-02","REQ-31-04","REQ-32-04","REQ-38-04","REQ-38-05","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Windows, Python/PySide6, model/tokenizer/backend, hardware, schemas and update paths need explicit support boundaries. Inventory supported/version/configuration/interface/data/device/provider combinations, risk priorities/actual test environments, performance/security/accessibility/migration/results/known incompatibilities/fallback/deprecation and communication. Do not infer another platform/provider/locale is supported from a single successful combination or silently drop old users.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/249_USABILITY_TESTING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/249_USABILITY_TESTING.txt","sha256":"fe826de1fa7bd0fcc66f2e3e4c8aad6cd188af87ee223bb5ad561e0191478de7","bytes":5099,"section":"249","original_title":"SECTION 249 — Usability Testing","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A usability-test model with users, tasks, context, prototype or product, observation method, consent, accessibility, findings, severity, design response, and limitations.","original_applicability":"Apply when a person must understand, decide, operate, recover, learn, or trust a user-facing or operator-facing capability.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-13-01","REQ-19-05","REQ-29-01","REQ-32-01","REQ-32-03","REQ-32-04","REQ-37-02","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Owner controls and conversational/workspace flows must be understandable and preserve agency in actual use. Record real users/tasks/context/hypotheses/criteria/consent/privacy/observer, observations versus interpretations, errors/confidence/comprehension/support/accessibility, findings/severity/design responses/retests and limitations. Preserve participant withdrawal and care; polish/analytics/synthetic personas cannot supply participation or acceptance.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/250_LOCALIZATION_TESTING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/250_LOCALIZATION_TESTING.txt","sha256":"ceab88aac0d2442881ee6af0027af6a0d78ae46698bb0652ec6eb6fab460c50a","bytes":5272,"section":"250","original_title":"SECTION 250 — Localization Testing","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A localization-test model with locales, content, translators, formats, layout, input, data, legal or cultural constraints, accessibility, defects, evidence, and owner decision.","original_applicability":"Apply when users, content, data, interfaces, communications, support, or obligations vary by language, locale, script, region, calendar, currency, or cultural context.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-06-03","REQ-21-04","REQ-24-01","REQ-32-04","REQ-38-05","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Native content, user input, long paths, dates/numbers/time and model formats can vary with locale even within the Windows scope. Inventory the actual declared locales/content/terminology/platform/input/formats/legal/safety/accessibility/support/fallback, reviewer/translation provenance and version. Test long/missing/malformed/mixed-script text, directionality and formatting without assuming unsupported languages or inventing regional law. Actual locale support and sensitive translations need qualified contextual review, with safe fallback and reopening.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/251_COMPLIANCE_TESTING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/251_COMPLIANCE_TESTING.txt","sha256":"8b3c3f77da96a1beb16fee228191c151b4c257ce9d6849a1c638b748260cbd05","bytes":5149,"section":"251","original_title":"SECTION 251 — Compliance Testing","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A compliance-test plan with authority, criteria, scope, sample, evidence, test method, exceptions, findings, remediation, attestation boundaries, and qualified owner decision.","original_applicability":"Apply when a claim of compliance, conformity, certification, attestation, contractual adherence, or regulatory control is required or material.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-16-03","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-03","REQ-36-04","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-03","REQ-41-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01"],"decision_reason":"Source conformance, governance controls, licensing, privacy and release claims need exact criteria and operation evidence. Bind authority/jurisdiction/entity/activity/scope/period/criterion/source currency, population/sample/control/workpapers/method/reviewer/results/exceptions/remediation/attestation authority and expiry. Separate engineering checks from qualified legal/regulatory conclusions; missing actual evidence remains open. Do not sign compliance or make external reports through this assessment.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/252_SAFETY_TESTING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/252_SAFETY_TESTING.txt","sha256":"548fa4cc8f062193eff2ecd7ba453f8914fc1af50902006688e9511eb6391482","bytes":5478,"section":"252","original_title":"SECTION 252 — Safety Testing","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A safety-test model with hazards, protected people, assumptions, operating modes, controls, test authority, safe limits, evidence, failures, recovery, and qualified acceptance.","original_applicability":"Apply when failure, misuse, automation, environment, or operation can cause injury, illness, unsafe condition, environmental harm, property damage, or loss of critical control.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-19-05","REQ-20-02","REQ-25-04","REQ-30-01","REQ-33-03","REQ-37-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Consequential file/command/device/physical actions and protected-object handling can affect property, privacy and critical control. Record qualified hazards/protected people/environment/modes/assumptions/limits/authority, normal/misuse/degraded/emergency/maintenance/recovery scenarios, independent safety functions/interlocks/alarms/accessible stop/exposure/residual risk and review. Hardware/physical tests require actual equipment and supervision; simulation cannot certify safety or authorize hazardous execution.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/253_MODEL_TESTING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/253_MODEL_TESTING.txt","sha256":"8995c53721c963b067bb7aa76b1833e7817407ed459e36fec8f1ced928fdf409","bytes":5586,"section":"253","original_title":"SECTION 253 — Model Testing","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A model-test model with purpose, population, data, labels, baseline, metrics, slices, thresholds, adversarial cases, human review, monitoring, deployment gates, and recovery.","original_applicability":"Apply when a statistical, machine-learning, generative, rules-based, simulation, or decision model influences output, ranking, prediction, classification, recommendation, or action.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-11-03","REQ-22-01","REQ-24-01","REQ-24-02","REQ-24-03","REQ-24-04","REQ-24-05","REQ-37-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Owned local inference and bounded planning/classification/generation influence user outputs and action proposals. Bind intended/prohibited use/model-data-template-tokenizer-prompt-policy-tool/backend/configuration versions, populations/slices/metrics/thresholds/baselines/frozen sets/labels/repeated samples/uncertainty/robustness/privacy/security/safety/human review. Preserve historical failures, contamination and counterexamples; assess shift/drift/rollback. No self-judge-only pipeline, raw endpoint score, or weight identity qualifies the installed path.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/254_DATA_TESTING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/254_DATA_TESTING.txt","sha256":"b7b42e973786373d28ffae41bad2b0d70af02fa4484b30327d0871da573399a9","bytes":5434,"section":"254","original_title":"SECTION 254 — Data Testing","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A data-test model with contracts, schema, grain, quality dimensions, samples, lineage, privacy, reconciliation, freshness, failure handling, evidence, and owner acceptance.","original_applicability":"Apply when data is collected, transformed, stored, exchanged, reported, modeled, archived, deleted, or used to make or support a decision.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-07-04","REQ-11-02","REQ-12-03","REQ-29-02","REQ-29-03","REQ-31-01","REQ-31-02","REQ-36-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Events, migration, memory/graphs/indexes, context, model data and exports need more than syntax and row counts. Bind source/schema/grain/definitions/population/time/transforms/lineage, semantic quality rules/thresholds/samples/access/privacy/freshness/reconciliation/consumers and authority. Test duplicates/misjoins/staleness/unauthorized data, quarantine/correction/backfill/deletion/restore and downstream interpretation. Preserve original records and correction provenance; no invented sensitive attributes or silent canonical changes.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/255_TEST_AUTOMATION.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/255_TEST_AUTOMATION.txt","sha256":"4d7ff1c5e5b88ed6a5cd7e8e89301bd7bb125ba2cbf89fcc11afdd0709da6f02","bytes":5043,"section":"255","original_title":"SECTION 255 — Test Automation","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An automation model with target tests, framework, fixtures, environments, triggers, ownership, flakiness, artifacts, security, observability, maintenance, quarantine, and human exit decision.","original_applicability":"Apply when tests, checks, simulations, scans, or verification steps are executed automatically or are candidates for automation.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-36-01","REQ-36-02","REQ-36-04","REQ-40-02","REQ-40-03","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Existing source/test runners and later integration/security/installed campaigns need trustworthy automation. Declare suite/assertions/fixtures/target/runner/framework/environment/dependencies/trigger/identity/credential scope, isolated data/reset/cleanup/rate limits/retries/artifacts/retention/hash binding, failures/flakiness/quarantine ownership and maintenance. Human/domain interpretation and gate decisions stay explicit. Never hide skipped critical cases, retry failures into success or leak secrets through evidence.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/256_VERIFICATION.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/256_VERIFICATION.txt","sha256":"3eb7321c5f1a50afc5552183399f146564cd94b5f3d39790510545b3366e6c70","bytes":4920,"section":"256","original_title":"SECTION 256 — Verification","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A verification record linking requirement or constraint to method, artifact, configuration, test or inspection, result, reviewer, exception, and conclusion within a bounded scope.","original_applicability":"Apply whenever conformance to requirements, design, contract, standard, configuration, or implementation claim matters.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-35-02","REQ-36-03","REQ-36-04","REQ-40-01","REQ-40-03","REQ-41-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Conformance claims throughout the build require exact requirements, versions, artifacts and methods. Maintain requirement/constraint/source-version/artifact/configuration/environment/method/execution/inspection/result/deviation/waiver/reviewer/independence/limitations and change impact. Independently validate bundle/history using an actual distinct verifier where required. Separate verified facts from owner adoption and human usefulness; no similarity, intended design or unsupported waiver closes conformance.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/257_VALIDATION.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/257_VALIDATION.txt","sha256":"98102f63d04270e3128eb0688bc3718db1f9463f9a716430ce94956493069d51","bytes":5403,"section":"257","original_title":"SECTION 257 — Validation","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":8,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_08_Law_Assurance_and_Validation.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A validation record connecting human objective, users, context, scenarios, outcomes, evidence, alternatives, harms, acceptance, and unresolved mismatch to a decision owner.","original_applicability":"Apply when a capability, product, service, policy, model, process, or decision must be shown useful, safe, acceptable, or fit for its intended purpose.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-13-01","REQ-17-03","REQ-29-01","REQ-32-04","REQ-37-02","REQ-40-03","REQ-41-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01"],"decision_reason":"A finished CETA must solve the owner's actual work and fit representative users and contexts, not only conform to tests. Bind human objective/users/affected non-users/context/scenarios/artifact, real outcomes/benefits/harms/comprehension/accessibility/privacy/support/recovery, alternatives/dissent/uncertainty/owner decision and post-use monitoring. Preserve mismatch and remedy/reopen when context changes; no synthetic participation, proxy metric, launch or usage creates acceptance.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_14.md","handoff/volume_viii_reconciliation_20261008_14.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/258_CONFIGURATION_MANAGEMENT.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/258_CONFIGURATION_MANAGEMENT.txt","sha256":"5688d7d3a5e33c35a3971c2790c021fd6c5191d9a5ab27ef33dddcdfe1fbe3e6","bytes":5120,"section":"258","original_title":"SECTION 258 — Configuration Management","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":9,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_09_Configuration_through_Delivery_Infrastructure.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A configuration model with items, owners, source of truth, versions, dependencies, environments, secrets boundary, approval, change history, drift detection, rollback, and evidence.","original_applicability":"Apply when settings, flags, policies, infrastructure, runtime values, schemas, device parameters, or environment-specific behavior can affect an outcome.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-01","REQ-03-02","REQ-03-03","REQ-03-04","REQ-06-03","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-02","REQ-36-03","REQ-36-04"],"decision_reason":"Schemas, canonical profile, Unicode tables, toolchains, locks and runtime configuration affect behavior; complete original section read; production drift/rollback enforcement remains open.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261006.md"],"implementation_refs":["T:/00-Active/CETA-desktop-delivery-20260906/rebuild_ios/src/ceta/contracts/wire.py","T:/00-Active/CETA-desktop-delivery-20260906/rebuild_ios/src/ceta/contracts/provenance.py"],"test_refs":["T:/00-Active/CETA-desktop-delivery-20260906/rebuild_ios/tests/contract"],"bounded_evidence_refs":["evidence/runtime/desktop-contract-source-bound-01.json","evidence/runtime/canonical-comparison-run-03.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/259_SOURCE_CONTROL_MANAGEMENT.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/259_SOURCE_CONTROL_MANAGEMENT.txt","sha256":"11e43d5a8484283d5107cded3e4c763cf2a4b427f3e47e6bdf7a6a1daa422d45","bytes":5338,"section":"259","original_title":"SECTION 259 — Source Control Management","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":9,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_09_Configuration_through_Delivery_Infrastructure.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A source-control model with repositories, ownership, branches, commits, review, access, signing, protection, provenance, retention, release linkage, recovery, and retirement.","original_applicability":"Apply when versioned files, code, configuration, documentation, infrastructure, tests, models, data definitions, or artifacts are collaboratively changed or released.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-05-04","REQ-38-01","REQ-39-01","REQ-39-04","REQ-40-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared local Windows build and its required capability/delivery lifecycle have these bounded responsibilities. Bind the three authorized CETA roots and development namespace to actual refs/commits/authorship/dirty work/review/access/provenance, secret/IP handling, retained baselines and release links. Preserve ignored/untracked work, history and unknown files; no force push, merge/protection bypass or deletion is implied.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_15.md","handoff/volume_ix_reconciliation_20261008_15.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/260_DEPENDENCY_MANAGEMENT.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/260_DEPENDENCY_MANAGEMENT.txt","sha256":"0a9bb3c294732536a408244be70161cd23c2930e2757285b6dc5cbd0606c874c","bytes":5179,"section":"260","original_title":"SECTION 260 — Dependency Management","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":9,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_09_Configuration_through_Delivery_Infrastructure.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A dependency inventory and lifecycle with owner, purpose, version, provenance, license, vulnerability, support, compatibility, update policy, fallback, evidence, and retirement.","original_applicability":"Apply when software, hardware, data, service, provider, model, tool, package, API, or process relies on an external or separately owned component.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-05-04","REQ-23-04","REQ-38-01","REQ-38-02","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared local Windows build and its required capability/delivery lifecycle have these bounded responsibilities. Inventory actual versions/provenance/owners/purpose/licenses/support/advisories/compatibility/data access, pinned closure/update policy, findings/exception expiry, fallback/rollback and retirement. Verify loaded frozen libraries. Actual installed tools remain available; no unrelated personal environment or hidden provider becomes a dependency.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_15.md","handoff/volume_ix_reconciliation_20261008_15.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/261_PACKAGE_MANAGEMENT.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/261_PACKAGE_MANAGEMENT.txt","sha256":"7971b85253bcb4b730abd65b6989ddd6cae17c8ef2233082064735c3d0022b70","bytes":5113,"section":"261","original_title":"SECTION 261 — Package Management","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":9,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_09_Configuration_through_Delivery_Infrastructure.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A package-management model with registries, repositories, provenance, resolution, lock or pin policy, access, signing, scanning, retention, promotion, rollback, and owners.","original_applicability":"Apply when packages, modules, libraries, plugins, containers, firmware bundles, datasets, models, or provider components are fetched, built, cached, promoted, or consumed.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-23-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-38-02","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared local Windows build and its required capability/delivery lifecycle have these bounded responsibilities. Declare approved registries/namespaces/version/digest/source/build/license/scan and access, resolution/pinning/cache/quarantine/promotion/retention/withdrawal. Reject substituted or malformed packages and dependency confusion; no publication, trusting unknown inputs or credential access is implied by a package inventory.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_15.md","handoff/volume_ix_reconciliation_20261008_15.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/262_ARTIFACT_MANAGEMENT.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/262_ARTIFACT_MANAGEMENT.txt","sha256":"52e67e5dc4d2b47eb09c784340f65e900dd668baa8586ee27414817688b0d7e6","bytes":5077,"section":"262","original_title":"SECTION 262 — Artifact Management","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":9,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_09_Configuration_through_Delivery_Infrastructure.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An artifact model with type, version, digest, source, build, dependencies, environment, owner, status, approval, consumers, retention, evidence, rollback, and disposal.","original_applicability":"Apply to binaries, packages, containers, firmware, models, datasets, reports, documentation, infrastructure plans, test evidence, and other lifecycle outputs.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-06-03","REQ-35-02","REQ-38-01","REQ-38-02","REQ-40-03","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared local Windows build and its required capability/delivery lifecycle have these bounded responsibilities. Bind type/version/digest/source/build/dependencies/environment/owner/status/approval/consumers/retention/distribution to stored binaries, models, reports and verification bundles. Labels and filenames cannot prove identity. Preserve quarantine, corruption/substitution detection, independent checks, restore/rollback and withdrawal.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_15.md","handoff/volume_ix_reconciliation_20261008_15.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/263_ENVIRONMENT_MANAGEMENT.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/263_ENVIRONMENT_MANAGEMENT.txt","sha256":"d2c466e7ed5e19a6940799ec5f975b758029eb21e3bdfbe5b298e69018ded235","bytes":5247,"sectio