ion","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":9,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_09_Configuration_through_Delivery_Infrastructure.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A build-automation model with triggers, inputs, runners, steps, credentials, caches, outputs, logs, retries, cancellation, ownership, provenance, and maintenance.","original_applicability":"Apply when build or artifact creation is scripted, scheduled, event-driven, or run by CI, a platform, or an agent.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-19-03","REQ-30-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-40-02","REQ-40-03","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared local Windows build and its required capability/delivery lifecycle have these bounded responsibilities. Define owner/workflow/trigger/source/runner/steps/identity/credential scope/cache/outputs/logs/gates, bounded retries/concurrency and cancellation/failure recovery. Ordinary authorized local builds do not activate privileged or externally visible automation. Preserve first failures and versioned maintenance/retirement.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_15.md","handoff/volume_ix_reconciliation_20261008_15.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/266_CONTINUOUS_INTEGRATION.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/266_CONTINUOUS_INTEGRATION.txt","sha256":"26777ddb699e70edcacf312450f8589da15b68760cd6a4a3590ae8a7f4400421","bytes":4742,"section":"266","original_title":"SECTION 266 — Continuous Integration","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_stat