ites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":9,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_09_Configuration_through_Delivery_Infrastructure.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A delivery model with artifact identity, readiness gates, environments, approvals, configuration, data migration, communication, release strategy, rollback, and owner decision.","original_applicability":"Apply when artifacts are promoted or prepared for release across environments, customers, operators, devices, or services.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-31-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-02","REQ-38-04","REQ-41-02","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared local Windows build and its required capability/delivery lifecycle have these bounded responsibilities. Bind candidate bytes/readiness criteria/tests/findings/compatibility/environments/configuration, support/migration/communication/approval, staged promotion/health/rollback and outcome. A ready artifact cannot claim installation or adoption; normal-data migration and release communication need applicable current authority.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_15.md","handoff/volume_ix_reconciliation_20261008_15.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/268_CONTINUOUS_DEPLOYMENT.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/268_CONTINUOUS_DEPLOYMENT.txt","sha256":"64d4829b31872a3c7f3121c181b627039f72ae8726f3c1b969cfa11cb2006fb5","bytes":5066,"section":"268","original_title":"SECTION 268 — Continuous Deployment","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":9,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_09_Configuration_through_Delivery_Infrastructure.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A deployment model with trigger, artifact, target, identity, policy gates, strategy, configuration, migration, monitoring, rollback, communication, approval, and incident behavior.","original_applicability":"Apply when artifacts are automatically or repeatedly deployed to an environment, device population, customer, service, or infrastructure target.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-19-01","REQ-31-04","REQ-38-04","REQ-41-02","REQ-04-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared local Windows build and its required capability/delivery lifecycle have these bounded responsibilities. Apply deployment trigger/target/identity/exact artifact/configuration/gates, staged activation/health/pause/kill switch/migration/checkpoint/rollback/audit and incident handling to qualified candidate installations and later governed updates. No automatic public/cloud rollout or production permission is introduced.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_15.md","handoff/volume_ix_reconciliation_20261008_15.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/269_DEVOPS.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/269_DEVOPS.txt","sha256":"0a306e9ecf3ed03fdeb332b5f5c6842b89457201453119a3f488d6e79138eac8","bytes":5254,"section":"269","original_title":"SECTION 269 — DevOps","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":9,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_09_Configuration_through_Delivery_Infrastructure.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A DevOps operating model with shared ownership, flow, feedback, automation, environments, observability, incident learning, quality, security, and measurable improvement.","original_applicability":"Apply when development and operations jointly create, release, operate, secure, support, or improve a product or service.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-35-01","REQ-36-02","REQ-39-01","REQ-39-04","REQ-40-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared local Windows build and its required capability/delivery lifecycle have these bounded responsibilities. Use current integrator, component owners, work/evidence/issue ledgers and support/runbooks to link actual user outcomes/change flow/security/quality/operating/recovery/learning and sustainable workload. Do not invent teams or on-call participation, or optimize delivery count at the expense of protected outcomes.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_15.md","handoff/volume_ix_reconciliation_20261008_15.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/270_DEVSECOPS.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/270_DEVSECOPS.txt","sha256":"7ce24b6f97e0972f04e5cf16e8fc8b8b025402ed3cc3d676c911090e8e193e38","bytes":5256,"section":"270","original_title":"SECTION 270 — DevSecOps","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":9,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_09_Configuration_through_Delivery_Infrastructure.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A DevSecOps model with threat and vulnerability input, secure source and build, identity, secrets, testing, policy gates, remediation, monitoring, incident response, and exception lifecycle.","original_applicability":"Apply when software, infrastructure, data, hardware, models, or delivery workflows create material security, privacy, safety, or supply-chain risk.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-21-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-03","REQ-38-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared local Windows build and its required capability/delivery lifecycle have these bounded responsibilities. Link threats/assets/versions/code/configuration/dependencies/runners/artifacts/privacy and actual tests to findings/severity/owners/gates/exceptions/expiry/remediation/retests/incident evidence. Retain scanner coverage/false positives/outage and independent boundaries. Do not suppress findings, claim total security or weaken gates for convenience.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_15.md","handoff/volume_ix_reconciliation_20261008_15.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/271_GITOPS.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/271_GITOPS.txt","sha256":"70d40490aa3433b4e1af86c89f70aeaea178d259492f53d407afb25bc2d0e2c7","bytes":5173,"section":"271","original_title":"SECTION 271 — GitOps","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"SUPPORTING","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":9,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_09_Configuration_through_Delivery_Infrastructure.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A GitOps model with desired state, repository, controller, identity, policy, environment, reconciliation, drift, secrets, promotion, rollback, audit, and recovery.","original_applicability":"Apply when versioned source drives infrastructure, platform, application, policy, configuration, or environment reconciliation.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-16-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-38-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"No current gitops reconciliation control-plane deployment is selected. Relevant design principles support the declared local Windows product; selecting such a target reopens direct technology-specific duties. Versioned configuration and drift principles remain allocated to local controlled delivery. A commit is desired state, never observed state or approval. No GitOps controller is selected; selecting one requires repository/controller/target/identity/permissions/secret/drift/pause/health/rollback and recovery qualification before reconciling live targets.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_15.md","handoff/volume_ix_reconciliation_20261008_15.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/272_PLATFORM_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/272_PLATFORM_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"2e69bcd495dc6468d4047ea4357b4db7a845f7fc01440714e33a42e88646934e","bytes":5563,"section":"272","original_title":"SECTION 272 — Platform Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":9,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_09_Configuration_through_Delivery_Infrastructure.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A platform model with users, products, paved paths, interfaces, guardrails, tenancy, identity, self-service, reliability, support, cost, change, feedback, and retirement.","original_applicability":"Apply when a team provides reusable infrastructure, tooling, workflows, environments, services, templates, or developer-facing capabilities to other teams or users.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-05-01","REQ-05-02","REQ-21-01","REQ-32-01","REQ-40-02","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared local Windows build and its required capability/delivery lifecycle have these bounded responsibilities. Scope stable interfaces, setup/tooling, consumers/owners, guardrails/least authority, user isolation, reliability/resources/cost/support/feedback/portability/migration/escape/recovery to the native application and developer tooling. No enterprise platform or fleet is created from role names; shared capability failures remain visible and bounded.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_15.md","handoff/volume_ix_reconciliation_20261008_15.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/273_DEVELOPER_EXPERIENCE.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/273_DEVELOPER_EXPERIENCE.txt","sha256":"d542cfaa632befb971ff9274de840fea5de9fef00584c0bbd038ab4728747feb","bytes":5064,"section":"273","original_title":"SECTION 273 — Developer Experience","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":9,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_09_Configuration_through_Delivery_Infrastructure.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A developer-experience model with user goals, journeys, setup, tooling, access, feedback, failure recovery, security, accessibility, support, measures, ownership, and retirement.","original_applicability":"Apply when contributors use a shared development workflow, platform, toolchain, repository, environment, documentation, or support path.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-05-04","REQ-32-04","REQ-38-02","REQ-40-02","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared local Windows build and its required capability/delivery lifecycle have these bounded responsibilities. Provide versioned actual commands, setup/tools/access/docs/examples/errors/diagnostics, isolated environments, accessibility/security/support/recovery and contributor feedback. Test clean setup and failure paths; no hidden account, unrelated repository environment, invented participants or polished-but-unexecuted instructions.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_15.md","handoff/volume_ix_reconciliation_20261008_15.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/274_TOOLING_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/274_TOOLING_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"226ba0a2691c510abc907661ba075e79bbe084e18c48ee4bd76a80bb28e3c2c4","bytes":4728,"section":"274","original_title":"SECTION 274 — Tooling Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":9,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_09_Configuration_through_Delivery_Infrastructure.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A tooling model with users, purpose, interfaces, dependencies, permissions, data, versions, installation, support, telemetry, quality, lifecycle, and fallback.","original_applicability":"Apply when a custom or shared tool materially affects engineering, testing, delivery, operations, governance, or user control.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-05-01","REQ-20-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-40-02","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared local Windows build and its required capability/delivery lifecycle have these bounded responsibilities. Record actual tool/source/version/purpose/users/interfaces/dependencies/permission/data/installation/telemetry/owner, behavior/security/accessibility/upgrade/degraded/rollback and retirement. Successful invocation does not prove safety or usefulness; tools retain explicit authority and offline/fallback paths.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_15.md","handoff/volume_ix_reconciliation_20261008_15.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/275_INFRASTRUCTURE_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/275_INFRASTRUCTURE_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"dda0706ad5d1a4adc3e457acea029d2143a7cfd26378d296767b6f7cf8498eab","bytes":5039,"section":"275","original_title":"SECTION 275 — Infrastructure Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":9,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_09_Configuration_through_Delivery_Infrastructure.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An infrastructure model with resources, dependencies, topology, identity, configuration, capacity, availability, security, cost, observability, recovery, and lifecycle ownership.","original_applicability":"Apply when physical, virtual, cloud, edge, network, storage, database, facility, or shared platform resources affect a system or service.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-21-01","REQ-23-02","REQ-25-03","REQ-26-04","REQ-34-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared local Windows build and its required capability/delivery lifecycle have these bounded responsibilities. Inventory the actual host/process/principal/network/storage/key/runtime and distributed authority resources, topology/dependencies/configuration/capacity/security/availability/cost/observation/backups/recovery/retirement. Test actual boundaries and common failures; multiple local processes cannot claim independent distributed domains.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_15.md","handoff/volume_ix_reconciliation_20261008_15.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/276_INFRASTRUCTURE_AS_CODE.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/276_INFRASTRUCTURE_AS_CODE.txt","sha256":"a45f05a198f25320465b65089b427b02edfaeec6e57a48a7ad6f227bace97cab","bytes":4778,"section":"276","original_title":"SECTION 276 — Infrastructure as Code","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":9,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_09_Configuration_through_Delivery_Infrastructure.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An IaC model with modules, inputs, state, providers, secrets boundary, policy, plan, approval, apply, drift, rollback, import, destruction, and evidence.","original_applicability":"Apply when code or declarative configuration provisions, changes, observes, or retires infrastructure, platform, network, storage, identity, or environment resources.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-19-01","REQ-21-02","REQ-31-04","REQ-38-01","REQ-38-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared local Windows build and its required capability/delivery lifecycle have these bounded responsibilities. Apply versioned setup/installer/resource definitions to the local selected environment, with modules/inputs/provider/tool identity/secret references/protected state/locking, reviewed plan versus actual apply, current scope/blast radius/drift/idempotence/rollback/recovery. No Terraform or cloud infrastructure is imposed; destructive host operations remain distinct.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_15.md","handoff/volume_ix_reconciliation_20261008_15.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/277_CLOUD_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/277_CLOUD_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"4d0086f26537454f3936f3940e06524b8429fd5d144308ed18e8b185723c4110","bytes":5140,"section":"277","original_title":"SECTION 277 — Cloud Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"SUPPORTING","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":9,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_09_Configuration_through_Delivery_Infrastructure.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A cloud model with provider, account or tenant, region, resources, identity, network, data, service limits, availability, cost, observability, governance, recovery, and exit.","original_applicability":"Apply when a public, private, hybrid, or managed cloud provides computing, storage, network, data, identity, platform, AI, or operations capability.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-03-02","REQ-23-04","REQ-29-01","REQ-33-03","REQ-38-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"No current cloud provider administration control-plane deployment is selected. Relevant design principles support the declared local Windows product; selecting such a target reopens direct technology-specific duties. No cloud account, region, managed provider or mandatory cloud inference is selected. Keep shared-responsibility/data-location/provider-limit/cost/identity/backup/exit controls as conditional obligations; selecting a cloud adapter reopens exact account/region/resources/data/network/availability/security/recovery and actual service evidence. Preserve offline local ownership.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_15.md","handoff/volume_ix_reconciliation_20261008_15.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/278_EDGE_COMPUTING_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/278_EDGE_COMPUTING_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"6d96d83916d07edab3f91a97090448ba0508565974195476fd22818ab476a308","bytes":5189,"section":"278","original_title":"SECTION 278 — Edge Computing Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":9,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_09_Configuration_through_Delivery_Infrastructure.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An edge model with site and node inventory, autonomy, synchronization, security, update, telemetry, resource limits, safety, offline behavior, recovery, and fleet ownership.","original_applicability":"Apply when computation or data processing occurs outside a central facility or cloud, including devices, sites, gateways, field systems, and distributed nodes.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-19-04","REQ-23-02","REQ-26-04","REQ-30-03","REQ-33-03","REQ-37-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared local Windows build and its required capability/delivery lifecycle have these bounded responsibilities. Bind actual node/site/device/hardware/software/identity/connectivity/data/autonomy/freshness/resources/local stop and safe state. Retain qualified device/physical/distributed lanes, synchronization conflict/update/rollback/buffered telemetry/recovery where selected. A central heartbeat cannot prove local/offline safety; no fleet-wide commands or field deployments are implied.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_15.md","handoff/volume_ix_reconciliation_20261008_15.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/279_CONTAINER_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/279_CONTAINER_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"53a9495efd0e2114cf8403b7fed102ab7886385f090293609aba31c65994cb26","bytes":4769,"section":"279","original_title":"SECTION 279 — Container Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"SUPPORTING","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":9,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_09_Configuration_through_Delivery_Infrastructure.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A container model with image sourc