ry_Infrastructure.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An orchestration model with cluster, control plane, nodes, workloads, identity, network, storage, scheduling, health, policy, upgrades, capacity, and recovery ownership.","original_applicability":"Apply when a control plane schedules or manages containerized workloads across nodes or environments.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-08-02","REQ-08-03","REQ-21-01","REQ-34-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"No current container cluster orchestration control-plane deployment is selected. Relevant design principles support the declared local Windows product; selecting such a target reopens direct technology-specific duties. No cluster, orchestrator or container node tenancy is selected. Scheduling/quotas/control-plane/identity/isolation/health/rollout/disruption/storage recovery concepts support the existing supervisor; a selected cluster requires real workload/node/control-plane/permission/failure-domain/upgrade/recovery evidence. Do not treat local supervisor processes as a cluster.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_15.md","handoff/volume_ix_reconciliation_20261008_15.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/281_VIRTUALIZATION_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/281_VIRTUALIZATION_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"7db58b315248504d2a568f1a6c663415926b852e94672b13cd54b7eae401fa8f","bytes":4703,"section":"281","original_title":"SECTION 281 — Virtualization Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"SUPPORTING","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":9,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_09_Configuration_through_Delivery_Infrastructure.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A virtualization model with host, guest, hypervisor, image, identity, resource, network, storage, tenancy, migration, monitoring, security, and lifecycle ownership.","original_applicability":"Apply when virtual machines, hypervisors, images, virtual networks, or virtual storage support a workload or service.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-21-01","REQ-21-05","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-03","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"No current vm and hypervisor administration control-plane deployment is selected. Relevant design principles support the declared local Windows product; selecting such a target reopens direct technology-specific duties. No hypervisor/guest deployment is established for this rebuild. Preserve host/guest/image identity, management/isolation/resource/network/storage/tenancy/migration/snapshot/backup/recovery duties for any selected qualification guest. Clean Windows and OS network-isolated qualification remain mandatory; prior legacy VM results do not transfer.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_15.md","handoff/volume_ix_reconciliation_20261008_15.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/282_SERVER_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/282_SERVER_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"feb7670cd6508e384256574fc36b2c90da9659397563b025c66a8e8fccb5eab1","bytes":4907,"section":"282","original_title":"SECTION 282 — Server Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":9,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_09_Configuration_through_Delivery_Infrastructure.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A server model with hardware or virtual host, operating system, services, identity, configuration, resource, network, storage, patch, monitoring, backup, and retirement ownership.","original_applicability":"Apply when a server hosts services, data, agents, workloads, control planes, or infrastructure that affects an outcome.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-08-01","REQ-21-01","REQ-21-02","REQ-26-04","REQ-38-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared local Windows build and its required capability/delivery lifecycle have these bounded responsibilities. Scope host/OS/service/principal/configuration/resources/network/storage/packages/patch/telemetry/backup/out-of-band recovery and retirement to actual local trusted services and future independent authority endpoints. Service liveness is not correctness; no server fleet, host reboot, admin account or patch operation is created by the assessment.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_15.md","handoff/volume_ix_reconciliation_20261008_15.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/283_SYSTEMS_ADMINISTRATION.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/283_SYSTEMS_ADMINISTRATION.txt","sha256":"35a20f299edd822a0607d7909248f6be2170c38197958de87247f6d1e3f538a6","bytes":4896,"section":"283","original_title":"SECTION 283 — Systems Administration","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":9,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_09_Configuration_through_Delivery_Infrastructure.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A systems-administration model with inventory, ownership, access, routine work, change, patch, monitoring, support, incident, backup, recovery, and retirement procedures.","original_applicability":"Apply when people or automation administer servers, endpoints, services, accounts, configurations, jobs, or infrastructure.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-08-04","REQ-16-04","REQ-19-05","REQ-21-02","REQ-38-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared local Windows build and its required capability/delivery lifecycle have these bounded responsibilities. Bind assets/accounts/services/jobs/runbooks/privileges/changes/commands/patches/alerts/support/backups/recovery to the actual application use case and operator authority. Maintenance is not a superuser exception; preserve auditable actions and separate administration from approval. No autostart, disabling host defenses or broad privileged commands are implied.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_15.md","handoff/volume_ix_reconciliation_20261008_15.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/284_NETWORK_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/284_NETWORK_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"3bde12048eed4dda424b53da73bb90d43bdb0c5c946c2c083b751054457fd606","bytes":5011,"section":"284","original_title":"SECTION 284 — Network Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":9,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_09_Configuration_through_Delivery_Infrastructure.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A network model with topology, addressing, identity, segmentation, routes, protocols, trust boundaries, performance, availability, monitoring, change, and recovery ownership.","original_applicability":"Apply when network, communication, routing, connectivity, name resolution, load balancing, firewall, wireless, or physical link affects a system or service.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-05-03","REQ-21-03","REQ-26-04","REQ-29-01","REQ-33-03","REQ-37-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared local Windows build and its required capability/delivery lifecycle have these bounded responsibilities. Scope topology/protocols/identities/routes/DNS/segmentation/encryption/limits/performance/observations/provider loss and recovery to authenticated IPC, offline qualification and selected network/device/distributed lanes. No universal traffic capture, firewall/DNS/routing change or reachability-as-security claim. Observe actual boundary enforcement.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_15.md","handoff/volume_ix_reconciliation_20261008_15.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/285_DATABASE_ADMINISTRATION.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/285_DATABASE_ADMINISTRATION.txt","sha256":"f80fd3e4b4434edbbcabdfc6fed7a4046281680fb5b2a90ab617c3c93bb2984b","bytes":5069,"section":"285","original_title":"SECTION 285 — Database Administration","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":9,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_09_Configuration_through_Delivery_Infrastructure.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A database-administration model with instances, schemas, owners, access, changes, capacity, performance, quality, backup, restore, replication, monitoring, retention, and retirement.","original_applicability":"Apply when a database or data service is provisioned, configured, queried, migrated, backed up, restored, replicated, secured, or retired.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-07-01","REQ-07-02","REQ-07-04","REQ-29-02","REQ-31-01","REQ-31-02","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared local Windows build and its required capability/delivery lifecycle have these bounded responsibilities. Scope actual local transactional store/engine/schema/grain/owners/principals/queries/indexes/migrations/durability/loaded settings/workload/backup/restore/retention/holds to the rebuild. Restrict raw data/DDL/writes, observe corruption/locks/lag where relevant, reconcile by category and test actual recovery rather than counts or successful queries.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_15.md","handoff/volume_ix_reconciliation_20261008_15.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/286_STORAGE_ADMINISTRATION.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/286_STORAGE_ADMINISTRATION.txt","sha256":"8737e1c7f9bd18d18bc20f317bbf0ebad8cbd39835f8519fc49709de00dba08d","bytes":5122,"section":"286","original_title":"SECTION 286 — Storage Administration","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":9,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_09_Configuration_through_Delivery_Infrastructure.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A storage model with classes, owners, location, capacity, performance, access, encryption, replication, backup, retention, deletion, monitoring, recovery, and lifecycle.","original_applicability":"Apply when data, artifacts, backups, logs, evidence, databases, files, objects, or physical or virtual volumes are stored, moved, recovered, retained, or deleted.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-07-02","REQ-25-02","REQ-29-02","REQ-29-03","REQ-31-04","REQ-34-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared local Windows build and its required capability/delivery lifecycle have these bounded responsibilities. Separate operational/profile/payload/model/artifact/log/evidence/quarantine/backup/archive/disposal stores, exact classes/owners/locations/permissions/encryption/integrity/capacity/performance/retention/holds/deletion and recovery. Test full volume/corruption/failed restore and replica/cache retention; preserve contents during authorized metadata diagnosis.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_15.md","handoff/volume_ix_reconciliation_20261008_15.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/287_RELEASE_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/287_RELEASE_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"e265bf3d36364ce766e1da0d1b19dac4f6201154de14f87b25f93450eeb90adb","bytes":5311,"section":"287","original_title":"SECTION 287 — Release Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":9,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_09_Configuration_through_Delivery_Infrastructure.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A release model with version, artifact, scope, readiness, notes, dependencies, approvals, packaging, communication, rollout, rollback, support, evidence, and retirement.","original_applicability":"Apply when a product, service, model, firmware, data, documentation, policy, infrastructure, or configuration version is made available to users, operators, or downstream systems.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-31-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-38-02","REQ-38-03","REQ-38-04","REQ-38-05","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared local Windows build and its required capability/delivery lifecycle have these bounded responsibilities. Bind source/new version/artifact/dependencies/tests/findings/compatibility/notices/security/notes/audience, readiness/support/migration/approvals/packaging/distribution/monitoring/rollback/withdrawal. Preserve separate identities for source, app, schema, policy, model and installer. Public notes/signing/release remain later actual authorized operations.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_15.md","handoff/volume_ix_reconciliation_20261008_15.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/288_RELEASE_MANAGEMENT.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/288_RELEASE_MANAGEMENT.txt","sha256":"134b5a6b5a5afab4aee84e4136ccf295fa337563e2806b6e62e9f24f78dd1145","bytes":4909,"section":"288","original_title":"SECTION 288 — Release Management","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":9,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_09_Configuration_through_Delivery_Infrastructure.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A release governance model with candidate, scope, readiness, decision rights, dependencies, communication, support, rollout, rollback, metrics, incident handling, and closure.","original_applicability":"Apply when a version, capability, policy, model, data, configuration, or infrastructure change is made available beyond its authoring context.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-17-03","REQ-38-04","REQ-39-01","REQ-41-02","REQ-41-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01"],"decision_reason":"The declared local Windows build and its required capability/delivery lifecycle have these bounded responsibilities. Use actual candidate/scope/audience/decision authority/evidence/readiness/risk/dependencies/support/communication/staged rollout/health/rollback/closure and reopening. Contributors cannot approve on behalf of owners; timely support, unresolved risks and partial outcomes stay visible. No public commitment is sent by preparation.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_15.md","handoff/volume_ix_reconciliation_20261008_15.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/289_CHANGE_MANAGEMENT.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/289_CHANGE_MANAGEMENT.txt","sha256":"9aebe55d562b083335ee425aad7b2f9f5ff21c5f8dc6758cc135f37d6ccda85f","bytes":4920,"section":"289","original_title":"SECTION 289 — Change Management","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":9,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_09_Configuration_through_Delivery_Infrastructure.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A change model with request, scope, reason, impact, risk, dependencies, approval, implementation, validation, communication, rollback, closure, and learning.","original_applicability":"Apply when a change can affect behavior, users, data, security, safety, cost, service, architecture, obligations, or continuity.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-16-04","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-02","REQ-39-04","REQ-40-03","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared local Windows build and its required capability/delivery lifecycle have these bounded responsibilities. Record request/current authority/owner/reason/baseline/scope/diffs/dependencies/impact/risk/tests/plan/communication/implementation/validation/rollback/closure and emergency follow-up. Apply existing user authorization to ordinary reversible work; preserve failed or partial changes and invalidate affected evidence rather than impose new approval rituals.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_15.md","handoff/volume_ix_reconciliation_20261008_15.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/290_DEPLOYMENT_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/290_DEPLOYMENT_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"bb9fc86131bd7a8d1b45d97a5f640f2aebafa01e8123bf8ccdf1782959919c73","bytes":4463,"section":"290","original_title":"SECTION 290 — Deployment Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":9,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_09_Configuration_th