ailability, performance, resilience, incident response, capacity, or operational improvement.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-08-01","REQ-34-01","REQ-34-02","REQ-34-04","REQ-35-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-37-03","REQ-40-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared persistent native Windows product and its required capability, delivery and recovery lifecycle have these bounded operational responsibilities. Bind actual services, critical user journeys, owners, SLI/SLO versions, error budgets, alerts, runbooks, capacity, incidents, recovery, toil and staffing limits. Qualify correctness, latency, safety, privacy and operator impact separately from uptime. Record authority to pause change or spend budgets, uncertainty and reopening; do not invent on-call staff or accepted objectives.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-16/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/302_PRODUCTION_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/302_PRODUCTION_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"8ff5855addcde5606aae776dc4fc8b9010318316c9b254a6c4dc3b68e5d221d0","bytes":5259,"section":"302","original_title":"SECTION 302 — Production Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":10,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_10_Production_Operations_and_Command.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A production-engineering model with service boundaries, environments, ownership, deployment, configuration, data, observability, performance, reliability, security, support, and recovery.","original_applicability":"Apply when building, changing, operating, or improving a production or production-like service, system, environment, or workflow.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-19-01","REQ-20-01","REQ-21-01","REQ-30-04","REQ-31-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-38-04","REQ-40-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared persistent native Windows product and its required capability, delivery and recovery lifecycle have these bounded operational responsibilities. Prepare exact native candidate/version/environment/configuration/data/service ownership, least privilege, progressive change, signals, support, capacity and recovery. Preserve real user outcome and consequence evidence. Production changes, communications, data replacement and return to service require their actual authority; present assessment does not authorize cutover or production execution.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-16/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/303_RUNTIME_OPERATIONS.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/303_RUNTIME_OPERATIONS.txt","sha256":"380f1722f87cefe9f6f1847d1e49c03c7bdc0aebbcedd4cfb5159a245b53a87b","bytes":4904,"section":"303","original_title":"SECTION 303 — Runtime Operations","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":10,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_10_Production_Operations_and_Command.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A runtime-operations model with process ownership, modes, health, configuration, dependencies, resource, scheduling, access, signals, change, incident, restart, recovery, and retirement.","original_applicability":"Apply when a live service, job, process, workload, device, agent, or control plane is executed, scheduled, restarted, paused, or recovered.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-08-01","REQ-08-02","REQ-08-03","REQ-08-04","REQ-22-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-30-03","REQ-35-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared persistent native Windows product and its required capability, delivery and recovery lifecycle have these bounded operational responsibilities. Inventory actual processes/services/jobs and lifetime identities, schedules, dependencies, modes, configurations, resource limits, health plus user outcomes, runbooks and owner authority. Use durable generation fencing, idempotency, bounded retries, graceful stop, state-preserving restart and independent control. Hung, duplicate or stale workers require reconciliation rather than assumed completion.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-16/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/304_CLOUD_OPERATIONS.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/304_CLOUD_OPERATIONS.txt","sha256":"8516e2a37efdbc343a698a3e94b9f3d618691b2d3dbac4ec6a877b73a922c541","bytes":4828,"section":"304","original_title":"SECTION 304 — Cloud Operations","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"SUPPORTING","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":10,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_10_Production_Operations_and_Command.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A cloud-operations model with inventory, ownership, health, access, change, cost, quota, security, compliance, observability, incident, backup, recovery, and exit.","original_applicability":"Apply when cloud resources or managed services are provisioned, changed, monitored, secured, billed, recovered, or retired.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-19-01","REQ-20-02","REQ-23-04","REQ-26-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-35-03","REQ-38-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Owned cloud accounts, resource fleets, provider administration, regions, billing and managed-service control are not selected by the declared local-first native build; approved external adapters remain independently scoped. Keep account/provider/resource/region/IAM/shared-responsibility/data/cost/quota/telemetry/incident/backup/recovery/exit duties as conditional obligations. Reopen DIRECT before any actual owned cloud service is provisioned or operated. No provider account, paid resource, implicit remote inference or region choice is adopted. Required distributed authority remains mandatory and cannot be relabeled a cloud dependency.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-16/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/305_NETWORK_OPERATIONS.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/305_NETWORK_OPERATIONS.txt","sha256":"c7902fbab9d2bb7a7794f4cae0eaa4fb98d10f8bf0b8d253002074069705a112","bytes":4670,"section":"305","original_title":"SECTION 305 — Network Operations","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":10,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_10_Production_Operations_and_Command.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A network-operations model with inventory, health, configuration, change, access, capacity, incidents, provider, monitoring, failover, and runbook ownership.","original_applicability":"Apply when networks, links, devices, routes, policies, DNS, load balancers, wireless, or providers are monitored, changed, repaired, or recovered.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-05-03","REQ-19-01","REQ-20-02","REQ-21-02","REQ-21-03","REQ-26-04","REQ-29-01","REQ-35-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared persistent native Windows product and its required capability, delivery and recovery lifecycle have these bounded operational responsibilities. Bind actual local IPC and any separately authorized network/distributed/device paths to endpoint identity, topology, permitted flows, routes/policies, DNS/certificate dependencies, capacity, signals, incident, rollback and out-of-band recovery. Restrict captures and high-impact network changes to exact permission. Unselected fleet/DNS/CDN/cloud administration does not weaken actual authentication, egress and recovery duties.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-16/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/306_SECURITY_OPERATIONS.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/306_SECURITY_OPERATIONS.txt","sha256":"3931435506156fa39edd946a2ac2a336175e3b1b03a96830b255c08a0bbddf79","bytes":5066,"section":"306"