d recovery lifecycle have these bounded operational responsibilities. Define the persistent product's actual service catalog, owners/consumers/outcomes, support and accessible status, internal expectations, requests/incidents/problems/changes, dependency/supplier boundaries, knowledge, continuity and improvement. Preserve unresolved consumer impact, evidence and reopening; ticket closure or SLA percentage cannot prove resolution. No service promise, external commitment or communication is created by assessment.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-16/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/312_IT_OPERATIONS.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/312_IT_OPERATIONS.txt","sha256":"dea33b9ea7d8e3d731d3ba00fcd3eb0cec6cab34d6b5a0f3e7a4ccdb4272abe9","bytes":4878,"section":"312","original_title":"SECTION 312 — IT Operations","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":10,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_10_Production_Operations_and_Command.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An IT-operations model with service catalog, users, assets, support, identity, devices, applications, network, incidents, changes, suppliers, continuity, and retirement.","original_applicability":"Apply when organizational IT services, devices, applications, accounts, support, or infrastructure are operated or changed.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-19-01","REQ-21-02","REQ-21-03","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-32-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-37-02","REQ-04-02","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared persistent native Windows product and its required capability, delivery and recovery lifecycle have these bounded operational responsibilities. Inventory CETA-owned installed services/endpoints/principals/assets, application/network/dependency configuration, access, support, incidents/changes, supplier constraints, backup and deliberate retention/retirement. Preserve user's other assets and content. Device changes, wipes, revocation and sensitive ticket closure need exact authority; no organizational fleet or employment decision is presumed.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-16/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/313_OBSERVABILITY_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/313_OBSERVABILITY_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"739f62aaaf99b94378a8f0cfa1fecfecee1c90f938669fdb2162c4e5cec76e3f","bytes":4941,"section":"313","original_title":"SECTION 313 — Observability Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":10,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_10_Production_Operations_and_Command.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An observability model with questions, signals, sources, context, cardinality, privacy, retention, correlation, dashboards, alerts, ownership, cost, and known blind spots.","original_applicability":"Apply when operators, owners, users, auditors, or automated systems need evidence about runtime, user, data, security, performance, or recovery behavior.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["R