y, quality, compliance, or user outcomes.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-08-01","REQ-28-01","REQ-28-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-35-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-35-03","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared persistent native Windows product and its required capability, delivery and recovery lifecycle have these bounded operational responsibilities. Inventory actual monitored targets/outcomes/sources/frequency/thresholds/context, owners, alert routes/actions/escalation, retention/privacy/cost and blind spots. Validate collector health separately from target health, false positives/misses and detection latency. Authority governs thresholds, expiring mutes and responses; no new monitoring/capture/egress scope is created.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-16/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/315_LOGGING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/315_LOGGING.txt","sha256":"1046b49c2ed6faa11823d8386dab7100e435b3a569581816a69864fa1c44c717","bytes":4802,"section":"315","original_title":"SECTION 315 — Logging","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":10,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_10_Production_Operations_and_Command.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A logging model with event taxonomy, fields, identity, time, correlation, severity, redaction, access, retention, integrity, transport, cost, and use.","original_applicability":"Apply when event records support operation, security, audit, debugging, compliance, safety, user support, or forensic evidence.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-07-03","REQ-25-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-29-03","REQ-35-01","REQ-35-03","REQ-40-03","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared persistent native Windows product and its required capability, delivery and recovery lifecycle have these bounded operational responsibilities. Define event taxonomy/schema/source/severity, stable identity/time/correlation, source health, resilient bounded transport, integrity/access and redaction; keep sensitive payloads and keys outside routine logs. Govern queries/export/disclosure, sampling/cardinality/cost/retention/holds/deletion and blind periods. A log line supports only its exact integrity context; absence is unknown rather than no event.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-16/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/316_TRACING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/316_TRACING.txt","sha256":"84f18d3b7f73bc74e078ae74c1bd41a5e9b4124266239a70709872bd529f4f58","bytes":4808,"section":"316","original_title":"SECTION 316 — Tracing","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":10,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_10_Production_Operations_and_Command.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A tracing model with trace and span identity, propagation, boundaries, timing, attributes, sampling, privacy, storage, correlation, access, cost, and diagnostic use.","original_applicability":"Apply when distributed requests, jobs, events, workflows, tool calls, or decisions cross components and timing or causality matters.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-05-03","REQ-19-04","REQ-20-01","REQ-26-03","REQ-29-01","REQ-35-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared persistent native Windows product and its required capability, delivery and recovery lifecycle have these bounded operational responsibilities. Bind request/task/operation/trace/span/parent identities through actual UI/usecase/kernel/worker/observation/settlement and required distributed paths. Record boot/time uncertainty, timing, allowed attributes, sampling, access/privacy/retention/cost and dropped-span gaps; correlate logs/metrics without claiming unseen causal paths. Sampling or collector changes require authority and re-evaluation.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-16/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/317_METRICS_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/317_METRICS_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"139febc739409ce3a38745869a17c54d24c1530b9c10288263095099602f61ef","bytes":4878,"section":"317","original_title":"SECTION 317 — Metrics Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":10,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_10_Production_Operations_and_Command.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A metric model with definition, owner, unit, population, dimension, source, calculation, window, freshness, quality, threshold, action, lineage, and limitation.","original_applicability":"Apply when a measure informs operation, quality, performance, service level, governance, product, security, safety, cost, or human decision.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-24-03","REQ-34-01","REQ-34-02","REQ-35-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-35-03","REQ-40-03","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared persistent native Windows product and its required capability, delivery and recovery lifecycle have these bounded operational responsibilities. Version metric questions/outcomes/units/populations/grain/dimensions/windows/denominators, source lineage/calculation/freshness/quality, owner/consumer, thresholds and action. Preserve missing/contrary data, exclusions, uncertainty/incentives, privacy and corrections with consumer notice. Never turn a chart, aggregate, score or proxy into fact or acceptance outside its measured slice.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-16/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/318_ALERTING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/318_ALERTING.txt","sha256":"f992ecff185b21835171b51f5c05ad10ecc25b5d5a525fc833a1f5fc0f801fc3","bytes":4595,"section":"318","original_title":"SECTION 318 — Alerting","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":10,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_10_Production_Operations_and_Command.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An alerting model with signal, condition, threshold, owner, severity, deduplication, routing, escalation, suppression, expiry, action, privacy, evidence, and feedback.","original_applicability":"Apply when a signal should prompt a human or controlled automation to investigate, decide, communicate, or act.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-16-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-32-03","REQ-35-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-35-03","REQ-04-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared persistent native Windows product and its required capability, delivery and recovery lifecycle have these bounded operational responsibilities. Bind protected conditions/signals/thresholds/context to current owner/severity, deduplication, rate limits, routes/escalation, privacy and runbooks. Record actual delivery, acknowledgement, diagnosis and response separately. Authorized suppression must expire and retain blind-period/noise/miss evidence; notification failure needs a usable alternate route without unapproved external messaging.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-16/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/319_INCIDENT_MANAGEMENT.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/319_INCIDENT_MANAGEMENT.txt","sha256":"361929396a10ce61fd3cb0924e80ac8760e40d1a2ec5a50b0ef61579039fb7d3","bytes":4862,"section":"319","original_title":"SECTION 319 — Incident Management","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":10,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_10_Production_Operations_and_Command.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An incident-management model with classification, commander, roles, timeline, evidence, impact, communications, actions, dependencies, recovery, closure, and review.","original_applicability":"Apply when an event disrupts or threatens service, safety, security, privacy, data, operations, users, property, or commitments.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-19-01","REQ-20-01","REQ-28-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-30-03","REQ-35-02","REQ-40-03","REQ-04-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared persistent native Windows product and its required capability, delivery and recovery lifecycle have these bounded operational responsibilities. Prepare actual incident intake/severity/scope/user impact, accountable command/action owners, immutable timeline/evidence, dependency visibility, safe containment and independent recovery. Preserve confirmed/suspected/disproved/unknown hypotheses, authorized communications and qualified legal/privacy escalation; record closure criteria/residual risk/post-incident actions and reopening. Parallel conflicting action must stop safely.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-16/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/320_PROBLEM_MANAGEMENT.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/320_PROBLEM_MANAGEMENT.txt","sha256":"24482a2e9b7aa254776cc7d05b4f944b4354a2518ccb431be4622df41f306e7c","bytes":4746,"section":"320","original_title":"SECTION 320 — Problem Management","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":10,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_10_Production_Operations_and_Command.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A problem model with symptoms, incidents, cause hypotheses, evidence, known error, workaround, corrective action, owner, risk, verification, and prevention.","original_applicability":"Apply when incidents, defects, vulnerabilities, recurring workarounds, or systemic risk warrant investigation beyond immediate restoration.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-24-04","REQ-30-03","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-02","REQ-36-04","REQ-39-01","REQ-40-03","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared persistent native Windows product and its required capability, delivery and recovery lifecycle have these bounded operational responsibilities. Link actual incidents/symptoms/changes/configurations/dependencies, impact, reproducible evidence, causal hypotheses/uncertainty, known-error/workaround, owner/risk/due date and corrective action. Use bounded safe experiments and independent challenge for material causality; verify regression and recurrence over declared exposure. Do not promote plausible narrative, blame or incident closure to solved cause.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-16/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/321_CAPACITY_MANAGEMENT.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/321_CAPACITY_MANAGEMENT.txt","sha256":"7ea1220b0bae6c4d84d1e7368340836fecbc08b868a15756aa2d436d56598d99","bytes":4605,"section":"321","original_title":"SECTION 321 — Capacity Management","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_s