T.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/324_RELIABILITY_MANAGEMENT.txt","sha256":"1b59d7210068883f8e1ab6055eb27858e56ecd3b96666c54a4b5172d81fc63b8","bytes":4670,"section":"324","original_title":"SECTION 324 — Reliability Management","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":10,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_10_Production_Operations_and_Command.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A reliability model with user and service outcomes, failure modes, indicators, objectives, error budget, dependencies, maintenance, incident, recovery, and improvement.","original_applicability":"Apply when service or system reliability, durability, correctness, continuity, or recovery is material.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-08-03","REQ-30-03","REQ-34-04","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-03","REQ-40-03","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared persistent native Windows product and its required capability, delivery and recovery lifecycle have these bounded operational responsibilities. Track actual service/user outcomes/failure modes/dependencies, objectives/error budgets, workload/duration/exposure, maintenance, toil/staffing, incidents, tests and recovery. Exercise degraded modes, dependency loss and learning with sustainable operators and independent control/evidence. A clean interval or estimated reliability cannot prove durable correctness or tested recovery.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-16/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/325_SERVICE_LEVEL_MANAGEMENT.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/325_SERVICE_LEVEL_MANAGEMENT.txt","sha256":"decdddfbc8ca0190c8cf75b9fa9ec246139f8601964ee294e0d5e6f9582165ba","bytes":4644,"section":"325","original_title":"SECTION 325 — Service Level Management","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":10,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_10_Production_Operations_and_Command.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A service-level model with service, consumer, outcome, indicator, objective, window, exclusions, measurement, commitment, escalation, remedy, and review.","original_applicability":"Apply when a service commitment, internal objective, contract, support expectation, or measurable outcome is declared or changed.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-19-01","REQ-32-03","REQ-35-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-35-03","REQ-40-03","REQ-41-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01"],"decision_reason":"The declared persistent native Windows product and its required capability, delivery and recovery lifecycle have these bounded operational responsibilities. Version actual consumers/services/outcomes/indicators/windows/denominators/exclusions, objective/commitment distinction, source/calculation, owners/review, breaches/escalation/remedies and evidence validity. Preserve disputed results and accessible user outcomes; metric outage does not imply compliance. Contractual/public commitments and remedies require qualified actual decision, not generated prose.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-16/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/326_BUSINESS_CONTINUITY.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/326_BUSINESS_CONTINUITY.txt","sha256":"c80f29fec3e4943d11bd84866e31e7307b44ceef8643a4bec34dfe22354ab505","bytes":5070,"section":"326","original_title":"SECTION 326 — Business Continuity","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":10,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_10_Production_Operations_and_Command.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A continuity model with essential functions, priorities, people, facilities, dependencies, minimum service, alternate process, communication, recovery objective, exercise, and decision authority.","original_applicability":"Apply when disruption could materially affect essential operations, obligations, people, customers, safety, finance, data, or public trust.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-08-04","REQ-29-03","REQ-30-04","REQ-32-04","REQ-37-02","REQ-37-04","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01"],"decision_reason":"The declared persistent native Windows product and its required capability, delivery and recovery lifecycle have these bounded operational responsibilities. Identify actual essential owner/user workflows, priority/minimum service, people/resources/device/facility/supplier dependencies where present, accessible manual/alternate channels and communications, authority and exercise gaps. Preserve physical/device/distributed/custody requirements rather than system-only continuity. Plans/tabletops do not prove actual staffing or alternative operation; return-to-normal remains observed and authorized.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-16/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/327_DISASTER_RECOVERY.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/327_DISASTER_RECOVERY.txt","sha256":"84a989f775dd9219141e01ab4f277c8985b7f2bba63a0d03958f86244f02da5d","bytes":5034,"section":"327","original_title":"SECTION 327 — Disaster Recovery","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":10,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_10_Production_Operations_and_Command.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A disaster-recovery model with scenarios, priorities, recovery time and data objectives, dependencies, runbooks, authority, alternate environment, evidence, testing, and return to service.","original_applicability":"Apply when loss or unavailability of a system, facility, region, provider, data, identity, or operational capability could materially affect essential outcomes.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-07-03","REQ-25-03","REQ-26-02","REQ-27-03","REQ-30-04","REQ-31-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-03","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared persistent native Windows product and its required capability, delivery and recovery lifecycle have these bounded operational responsibilities. Bind actual host/storage/identity/credential/dependency/trust-loss scenarios to essential services/priorities/RTO/RPO, offline assets, alternate isolated environment, independent access/control, staffing, runbooks and communication. Rehearse restore/reconciliation/staged return and record real measured gaps. Never reconstruct missing keys/authority from guesses or substitute a backup inventory for disaster capability.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-16/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/328_BACKUP_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/328_BACKUP_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"4e9791acf73ad244a10d2f09b763075d3a613b81bca90a75d688b7194bf38eb0","bytes":4827,"section":"328","original_title":"SECTION 328 — Backup Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":10,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_10_Production_Operations_and_Command.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A backup model with scope, source, frequency, consistency, retention, encryption, isolation, immutability, ownership, integrity, monitoring, restore test, and destruction.","original_applicability":"Apply when data or state must be recovered after deletion, corruption, outage, disaster, ransomware, error, or migration.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-07-02","REQ-07-03","REQ-25-01","REQ-25-03","REQ-27-03","REQ-29-02","REQ-31-04","REQ-40-03","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared persistent native Windows product and its required capability, delivery and recovery lifecycle have these bounded operational responsibilities. Inventory actual events/payloads/configuration/artifacts/state, consistency point/RPO/schedule/destination/owners, encryption/key references/independent access/immutability or isolation where warranted, integrity and monitoring. Qualify representative/critical restore, retained backups/legal holds/deletion and incident limits. No sensitive content, key export, retention expansion or real-profile backup change is authorized by assessment.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-16/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/329_RESTORE_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/329_RESTORE_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"952ddc5b602cd96315dcdf0ed39180778c7afc66eba45e34a67c6bc5b64a35d8","bytes":4804,"section":"329","original_title":"SECTION 329 — Restore Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":10,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_10_Production_Operations_and_Command.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A restore model with source, point in time, target, authority, integrity, dependency, sequencing, validation, reconciliation, rollback, communication, and evidence.","original_applicability":"Apply when backup, archive, snapshot, replica, prior artifact, or known-good state is used to return a system, data, or service to operation.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-07-03","REQ-20-04","REQ-29-03","REQ-30-03","REQ-30-04","REQ-31-02","REQ-31-03","REQ-31-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared persistent native Windows product and its required capability, delivery and recovery lifecycle have these bounded operational responsibilities. Bind exact immutable source/version/point-in-time, target/current-state preservation, authority/key access/dependency order/checkpoints, compatibility/integrity/permissions and data semantics. Validate and reconcile unknown material, deleted payloads, unresolved effects and authority before return to service. Preserve both states on failure; copying bytes cannot prove usability, and older executables cannot open incompatible data.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-16/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/330_FAILOVER_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/330_FAILOVER_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"34361c681c4f75be7a141059d261209463dc4865c71035a6e0097ce48d403232","bytes":4730,"section":"330","original_title":"SECTION 330 — Failover Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":10,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_10_Production_Operations_and_Command.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A failover model with trigger, authority, primary and alternate, data state, synchronization, health, sequencing, split-brain control, return, rollback, and evidence.","original_applicability":"Apply when a service, network, data store, region, provider, device, or control plane has an alternate path or instance.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-08-03","REQ-19-02","REQ-22-02","REQ-26-01","REQ-26-04","REQ-27-03","REQ-30-03","REQ-35-02","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared persistent native Windows product and its required capability, delivery and recovery lifecycle have these bounded operational responsibilities. Specify actual primary/alternate/control/dependency domains and authority, health/sync/data point, trigger, promotion/routing sequence, fencing/quorum, split-brain prevention, rollback/reconciliation and return. Required distributed-authority outage must retain genuine separation and quorum; local fixtures are not resilient domains. A standby label or fallback process cannot create safe promotion or missing permission.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-16/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/331_OPERATIONAL_READINESS.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/331_OPERATIONAL_READINESS.txt","sha256":"c7082267c77e3727b7f4959008819a0525c590790a70e26b1a7125494fa0622f","bytes":5005,"section":"331","original_title":"SECTION 331 — Operational Readiness","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":10,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_10_Production_Operations_and_Command.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An operational-readiness record with owner, scope, modes, runbooks, staffing, access, observability, support, security, capacity, continuity, recovery, evidence, gaps, and explicit decision.","original_applicability":"Apply before entering a new operational mode, production, field use, support commitment, or material transition.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-32-02","REQ-32-03","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-37-02","REQ-37-03","REQ-37-04","REQ-40-03","REQ-41-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-40-01"],"decision_reason":"The declared persistent native Windows product and its required capability, delivery and recovery lifecycle have these bounded operational responsibilities. Bind exact candidate/environment/modes/users/owners/access, runbooks/support/training/staffing, signals/security/privacy/accessibility/capacity, backups/restore/failover and real exercise evidence. Preserve READY/CONDITIONAL/HOLD/REJECT scope, gaps/risk/expiry/reviewer and reopening after changed evidence. Assessment, checklist, deployment and tests alone do not establish operational effectiveness or owner acceptance; all mandatory lanes stay open until actual proof.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-16/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/332_COMMAND_AND_CONTROL.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/332_COMMAND_AND_CONTROL.txt","sha256":"04d66b65994d66c85a0d514c245797b8245786a05df8e16aa1860addcd973a16","bytes":5199,"section":"332","original_title":"SECTION 332 — Command and Control","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":10,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_10_Production_Operations_and_Command.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A command-and-control model with authority, identity, scope, mode, decision rights, delegation, communication, status, override, evidence, audit, safety, and recovery.","original_applicability":"Apply when people, automation, AI, services, devices, or organizations can direct consequential operation, resource, safety, security, user, or recovery action.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-05-02","REQ-05-03","REQ-16-03","REQ-16-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-19-02","REQ-19-04","REQ-19-05","REQ-26-04","REQ-30-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared persistent native Windows product and its required capability, delivery and recovery lifecycle have these bounded operational responsibilities. Bind actors/principals/lifetimes to current authority/scope/mode/resources/decisions, delegation expiry/revocation, conflict/escalation and resilient command/evidence channels. Separate observe/advise/decide/authorize/execute/audit/recover; qualify stop/override, quorum/dual control where required and unavailable commander behavior. Model, role labels, shared credentials and quoted chat consent cannot create authority or permanent emergency exceptions.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-16/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/333_TECHNICAL_SUPPORT.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/333_TECHNICAL_SUPPORT.txt","sha256":"ab26546fe5553f6601b9a84b2ba48673183d995cc15d461c6f5e2518e775c641","bytes":4917,"section":"333","original_title":"SECTION 333 — Technical Support","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":11,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_11_Support_Enterprise_and_Roadmaps.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A support model with intake, identity, severity, context, troubleshooting, escalation, communication, workaround, resolution, knowledge, privacy, and feedback ownership.","original_applicability":"Apply when a person or team needs technical assistance to use, operate, integrate, recover, or understand a capability.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-29-01","REQ-29-03","REQ-30-04","REQ-32-03","REQ-32-04","REQ-35-01","REQ-36-02","REQ-40-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared local Windows CETA product and its mandatory lifecycle carry these bounded responsibilities; this allocates duties without asserting implementation, qualification, or owner acceptance. Implement native diagnostic intake with user/project/version/environment identity, severity, redaction, current evidence, approved troubleshooting, limitations, escalation, accessible communication, workaround, recovery, reopen and verified user outcome. Do not request secrets, silently mutate accounts/data/devices, equate ticket closure with success, or invent staffing, SLAs, support channels or user confirmation. Link recurring defects to tests and knowledge; retain consent and incident history.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-17/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/334_CUSTOMER_SUPPORT.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/334_CUSTOMER_SUPPORT.txt","sha256":"d0d4104e2d67ce4cec54920a287c17c0636929c27384062f0465ced32673d2ab","bytes":4901,"section":"334","original_title":"SECTION 334 — Customer Support","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":11,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_11_Support_Enterprise_and_Roadmaps.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A customer-support model with customer identity, entitlement, channel, issue, priority, communication, resolution, escalation, privacy, accessibility, service level, and feedback.","original_applicability":"Apply when customers need help using, integrating, billing, securing, recovering, or understanding a product or service.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-19-05","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-04","REQ-32-03","REQ-32-04","REQ-35-03","REQ-37-02","REQ-40-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared local Windows CETA product and its mandatory lifecycle carry these bounded responsibilities; this allocates duties without asserting implementation, qualification, or owner acceptance. Preserve user identity/entitlement, chosen local support channel, issue context, priority, status/history, accessible routing, current knowledge, incident escalation, response, appeal and feedback. Account/data/security/billing or compensation actions require exact authority if present; no refunds, promises, accounts or customer contracts are invented. Distinguish customer ratings, sentiment, closure and verified outcomes, and permit reopened disputes.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-17/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/335_HELP_DESK.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/335_HELP_DESK.txt","sha256":"ca3c373ea5109e0bfe7c4205f92c31d590e4dda91526003baebc4ea6a1cbbb2d","bytes":4559,"section":"335","original_title":"SECTION 335 — Help Desk","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":11,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_11_Support_Enterprise_and_Roadmaps.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A help-desk model with intake, identity, categorization, priority, knowledge, communication, escalation, service level, privacy, accessibility, and closure verification.","original_applicability":"Apply when users need a central channel for IT, service, access, device, application, or operational assistance.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-19-01","REQ-19-05","REQ-29-01","REQ-32-01","REQ-32-03","REQ-32-04","REQ-37-02","REQ-40-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared local Windows CETA product and its mandatory lifecycle carry these bounded responsibilities; this allocates duties without asserting implementation, qualification, or owner acceptance. Provide the product's first-contact help/recovery path with authenticated scoped intake, request/asset identity, category/severity, versioned knowledge, owner/routing, accessible status and escalation. Access grants, device operations, wipes and sensitive closure remain governed effects with actual confirmation. Do not introduce an enterprise help-desk service or assert staff/SLA availability. Retain recurring-problem, resolution and user-confirmation evidence.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","ha