, contamination, guardrails/stop, analysis/reproducibility and decision. Separate synthetic fixtures and trials from real participants; no live-user exposure, training, production change or ethical/qualified approval is fabricated. Preserve failures and adverse cases; significance is not safety or value.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-17/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/370_A_OR_B_TESTING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/370_A_OR_B_TESTING.txt","sha256":"2d8f8603d3d5fc35be1acaaed6fef77e6cebf97d2e6d37692d0e41718652d161","bytes":4615,"section":"370","original_title":"SECTION 370 — A/B Testing","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":11,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_11_Support_Enterprise_and_Roadmaps.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An A/B-test model with variant, population, randomization, exposure, control, metric, sample, duration, guardrails, statistical method, stop rule, and rollout decision.","original_applicability":"Apply when variants of a product, interface, process, message, policy, or system are compared experimentally.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-24-02","REQ-24-03","REQ-24-04","REQ-29-01","REQ-34-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-40-03","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared local Windows CETA product and its mandatory lifecycle carry these bounded responsibilities; this allocates duties without asserting implementation, qualification, or owner acceptance. Apply to required controlled candidate/baseline comparisons of model/request/configuration/system variants with exact hypothesis, stable assignment or declared alternative, exposure, exclusion/control, metrics/sample/time/guardrails/privacy/accessibility, analysis method and stop/rollback. Do not silently randomize real users or treat an offline comparison as a live randomized study. A statistical winner is not product value, qualification or rollout authority; retain contamination and missing-event failures.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-17/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/371_OPTIMIZATION.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/371_OPTIMIZATION.txt","sha256":"0721ec5362fedb11155bf6e17ec0e4b3fb4ce96c4e0bc5ec4b153c86a3ed72a6","bytes":4773,"section":"371","original_title":"SECTION 371 — Optimization","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":11,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_11_Support_Enterprise_and_Roadmaps.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An optimization model with objective, constraints, baseline, variables, method, tradeoffs, guardrails, evidence, experiment, decision, rollback, and monitoring.","original_applicability":"Apply when a system, process, product, resource, model, or operation is deliberately tuned to improve performance, cost, quality, growth, reliability, or another outcome.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-24-03","REQ-34-01","REQ-34-02","REQ-34-04","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-02","REQ-40-03","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared local Windows CETA product and its mandatory lifecycle carry these bounded responsibilities; this allocates duties without asserting implementation, qualification, or owner acceptance. Freeze measurable quality/performance/resource objectives and protected invariants, baseline, candidates/variables/methods/alternatives/guardrails/uncertainty/tradeoffs, actual profile, independent monitoring and rollback before tuning. Preserve all failed samples and no-harm limitations; throughput or memory gains cannot drop context, verification, privacy, stop or recovery reserves. No hidden provider, production change, goal drift or weakened acceptance is allowed without recorded requirement change.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-17/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/372_FEEDBACK_MANAGEMENT.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/372_FEEDBACK_MANAGEMENT.txt","sha256":"33d9ee8e987ffa0f14f41a7d5f72547a4d5c35b949270679de7ed82313f986c2","bytes":4786,"section":"372","original_title":"SECTION 372 — Feedback Management","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":11,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_11_Support_Enterprise_and_Roadmaps.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A feedback model with source, participant, context, consent, topic, severity, triage, owner, response, action, evidence, privacy, and closure or reopening.","original_applicability":"Apply when feedback from users, customers, operators, communities, staff, suppliers, tests, incidents, or stakeholders informs decisions or improvement.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-24-05","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-32-03","REQ-35-03","REQ-39-04","REQ-40-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The declared local Windows CETA product and its mandatory lifecycle carry these bounded responsibilities; this allocates duties without asserting implementation, qualification, or owner acceptance. Capture exact user/operator/test/incident feedback, corrections, negations, provenance, participant anonymity/consent, context/severity/topic, privacy/retention, triage/owner/acknowledgment/response/appeal, disposition and reopening. Preserve dissent and contradictory signals; sentiment/volume does not prove intent or consensus. Feedback cannot silently change facts, policy, weights, identity, authority or completion. Sensitive/public responses and high-impact closure need actual human review.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-17/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/373_ROADMAP_MANAGEMENT.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/373_ROADMAP_MANAGEMENT.txt","sha256":"96ea2d8d0113db13e109970c29b5db3a2f64f1023c278150db5eef9ad4426b91","bytes":4837,"section":"373","original_title":"SECTION 373 — Roadmap Management","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":11,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_11_Support_Enterprise_and_Roadmaps.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A roadmap model with objective, horizon, themes, initiatives, outcomes, evidence, dependencies, capacity, risk, decision gates, confidence, ownership, and change history.","original_applicability":"Apply when work is sequenced, prioritized, forecast, committed, funded, deferred, or retired across a portfolio, product, program, or capability.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-37-04","REQ-39-02","REQ-39-04","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-01","REQ-41-02","REQ-41-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01"],"decision_reason":"The declared local Windows CETA product and its mandatory lifecycle carry these bounded responsibilities; this allocates duties without asserting implementation, qualification, or owner acceptance. Keep full 28-package/20-volume/406-source/128-case/eight-gate objective, priorities/dependencies, evidence/confidence, real machine/capacity/cost assumptions, unresolved work, options, decisions, commitments and review triggers. Roadmap position, date or source review is intent, not executable delivery. Do not silently de-scope required hardware/device/distributed/custody/modality/physical/installed/endurance evidence, invent confidence, promise dates, or adopt owner decisions from model prose.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-17/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/374_MAINTENANCE_ENGINEERING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/374_MAINTENANCE_ENGINEERING.txt","sha256":"29798e2b0b488646d05f763118e95a17a4b77daa5622f26b01342608a8c8a423","bytes":4690,"section":"374","original_title":"SECTION 374 — Maintenance Engineering","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":12,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_12_Maintenance_Decommissioning_and_Retirement.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A maintenance model with asset, condition, schedule, preventive and corrective work, dependencies, parts, skills, safety, evidence, backlog, change, and retirement.","original_applicability":"Apply when a system, product, infrastructure, device, service, data pipeline, or process requires planned or unplanned work to remain fit for use.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-08-01","REQ-16-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-20-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-38-04","REQ-39-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The required CETA application, persisted data and qualified adapters have ongoing support, condition, maintenance and lifecycle obligations. Inventory declared software, data, service and actual device assets; condition, schedules, preventive/corrective/adaptive work, parts and skills when relevant, safety, windows, backlog, change and retirement. Maintain accountable authority and actual execution, tests, rollback and return-to-service evidence; a closed maintenance ticket cannot prove restored fitness. Preserve required hardware/physical lanes and exact conditional scope without selecting a manufacturing or facility platform.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-18/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/375_CORRECTIVE_MAINTENANCE.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/375_CORRECTIVE_MAINTENANCE.txt","sha256":"0a5dcf03ceeb7a17e6f63e5625cac4ed2b5de7a457c0dd1ee7d97b6e041e983b","bytes":4592,"section":"375","original_title":"SECTION 375 — Corrective Maintenance","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":12,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_12_Maintenance_Decommissioning_and_Retirement.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A corrective-maintenance model with failure, triage, safety, diagnosis, repair, replacement, rollback, test, verification, communication, and recurrence tracking.","original_applicability":"Apply after failure, defect, incident, nonconformance, degradation, vulnerability, or unsafe condition requires repair or correction.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-20-01","REQ-20-03","REQ-35-01","REQ-36-02","REQ-38-04","REQ-42-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"CETA has known failure/regression inputs and must recover from actual future defects without erasing evidence. Triage, protect safety, preserve failures, diagnose, authorize repair/replacement or substitute, test data/configuration integrity, verify return or rollback, communicate and track recurrence. Separate emergency restoration from permanent correction; qualified specialists decide relevant physical safety. Repair execution, root cause and recurrence prevention retain separate evidence states.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-18/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/376_PREVENTIVE_MAINTENANCE.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/376_PREVENTIVE_MAINTENANCE.txt","sha256":"81fe40376c1ee2fe92dafeaa5ad4d73d9cdb296f79dea03cae2b858fa13a0158","bytes":4692,"section":"376","original_title":"SECTION 376 — Preventive Maintenance","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":12,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_12_Maintenance_Decommissioning_and_Retirement.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A preventive-maintenance model with asset, condition, interval, trigger, procedure, resources, safety, evidence, effectiveness, deferral, and review.","original_applicability":"Apply when planned work can prevent failure, preserve quality, maintain safety, improve security, or extend useful life.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-08-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-23-02","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-03","REQ-38-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The continuing local system and required device/resource lanes need bounded prevention and inspection over their lifecycle. Tie planned work to actual failure history and condition, justified intervals/triggers, parts/skills where relevant, safe windows, authorized scheduling, calibration, execution/tests, effectiveness and deferral. Activity counts and calendar completion cannot stand in for reduced failure. Changes to assets, environment, supplier or design reopen dependent plans.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-18/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/377_ADAPTIVE_MAINTENANCE.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/377_ADAPTIVE_MAINTENANCE.txt","sha256":"660160c779ce42c3441ecf75bc5a9ecca425ac86993f6cba543008b0c79a8ae4","bytes":5036,"section":"377","original_title":"SECTION 377 — Adaptive Maintenance","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":12,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_12_Maintenance_Decommissioning_and_Retirement.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An adaptive-maintenance model with change trigger, current baseline, intended adaptation, impact, compatibility, test, migration, rollout, rollback, evidence, and owner decision.","original_applicability":"Apply when maintenance changes behavior, interfaces, platform, data, security, performance, compliance, usability, or environment in response to changed conditions.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-00-01","REQ-00-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-31-01","REQ-31-04","REQ-36-02","REQ-38-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The rebuild and continuing product must adapt to changed users, dependencies, threats and environments within recorded authority. Record trigger, current exact baseline, changed condition, objective, affected users, design, compatibility, security/privacy, tests, migration/support, rollout/rollback and retirement. Rebuilding is the already authorized objective; additional material scope or production change retains actual required authority. Prove old and new supported journeys without silently preserving or removing behavior.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-18/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/378_SOFTWARE_UPDATES.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/378_SOFTWARE_UPDATES.txt","sha256":"72a373a905d32a9ba286b1f183796f5ee89c674092329c4cdd494c87387e3cc8","bytes":4686,"section":"378","original_title":"SECTION 378 — Software Updates","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":12,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_12_Maintenance_Decommissioning_and_Retirement.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An update model with source, version, artifact, vulnerability or defect, target, prerequisites, rollout, configuration, migration, health, rollback, communication, and owner.","original_applicability":"Apply when software, application, library, operating system, service, model, configuration, or package is updated in any environment or population.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-23-01","REQ-23-04","REQ-31-04","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-38-03","REQ-38-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"CETA build/runtime dependencies, application and qualified assets require exact update identity and recovery. Map current/target versions, artifacts, reason/advisories, targets/prerequisites, data/configuration, compatibility, tests, backup, stage, authorized activation, health, rollback, support and version retirement. Preserve immutable artifact/signature verification choices and actual channel scope; emergency or production update remains separately authorized. A deployment or scan only proves its exact inventory/time.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-18/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/379_FIRMWARE_UPDATES.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/379_FIRMWARE_UPDATES.txt","sha256":"6cdc17212468ba48dadc59a3c8cec69ad7dd3b945d10101cacdd0ff6a12d7a4a","bytes":5024,"section":"379","original_title":"SECTION 379 — Firmware Updates","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":12,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_12_Maintenance_Decommissioning_and_Retirement.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A firmware-update model with image provenance, hardware compatibility, signing, boot trust, target, power and connectivity, staged rollout, rollback, safe state, telemetry, and recovery.","original_applicability":"Apply when firmware, bootloader, device image, microcode, or embedded update mechanism changes on deployed or production hardware.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-19-01","REQ-20-02","REQ-23-02","REQ-33-03","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-04","REQ-38-03","REQ-04-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Required hardware-backed and physical/device lanes must retain firmware identity, compatibility and safe recovery duties when firmware or device trust changes. Retain exact actual device/hardware/current-target image identity, provenance/signing and non-exported key references, boot trust/anti-rollback, power/connectivity, safe state, staged target population, telemetry/reconciliation, local recovery or justified equivalent, rollback and certification impact. This does not select or authorize a firmware writer, fleet, new bootloader, key extraction or flashing. Actual firmware activity requires exact delegated authority and qualified hardware; missing devices keep dependent claims open and unavailable, with representative isolated qualification distinct from real fleet change.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-18/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/380_SECURITY_PATCHING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/380_SECURITY_PATCHING.txt","sha256":"e29e844cf7c75ddb0e7452ce653b047fed50185774808bc90defd33028b607cf","bytes":4801,"section":"380","original_title":"SECTION 380 — Security Patching","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":12,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_12_Maintenance_Decommissioning_and_Retirement.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A security-patching model with advisory, asset, exposure, severity, owner, deadline, compatibility, rollout, mitigation, verification, exception, and evidence.","original_applicability":"Apply when a security fix, mitigation, configuration, or compensating control is required for a known vulnerability or security weakness.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-19-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-38-01","REQ-38-04","REQ-42-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"CETA's direct/transitive dependencies and actual protected assets require known exposure tracking and qualified patching. Bind actual advisory/source/version, inventory/coverage, severity and deadline, owner, patch or mitigation, compatibility/testing, authorized rollout, rollback, verification, expiring residual exception and communication. Unsupported/offline assets cannot disappear from affected scope. Source reconciliation does not establish current advisory absence or authorize exploitation; perform fresh primary-source advisory checks when qualification executes.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-18/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/381_DEPENDENCY_UPDATES.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/381_DEPENDENCY_UPDATES.txt","sha256":"4a95bc286216b973c19a6ba7581b0bd55a5f263c0a53a7e2afd231f0a67c6de5","bytes":4593,"section":"381","original_title":"SECTION 381 — Dependency Updates","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":12,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_12_Maintenance_Decommissioning_and_Retirement.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A dependency-update model with graph, current and target version, reason, advisory, license, compatibility, test, rollout, artifact, owner, and recovery.","original_applicability":"Apply when a package, library, provider, image, model, module, API, or external component is updated.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-23-04","REQ-24-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-02","REQ-38-01","REQ-38-02","REQ-38-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The pinned build/runtime/model closure must preserve behavior, supply-chain trust, licenses and recovery across updates. Record dependency graph, current/target source/version, reason, actual advisory/license, transitive/API/behavior/performance impact, lockfile/SBOM, isolated build/test/scan, actual artifact, staged authorized rollout, monitoring, pin/substitution/rollback and support. Preserve failures and customers/consumers where actually present. A build pass cannot prove license acceptance, security or installed runtime compatibility.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-18/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/382_DATA_MIGRATION_OPERATIONS.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/382_DATA_MIGRATION_OPERATIONS.txt","sha256":"84da22f457a2582b25e4fe9fb16493e0d8c2fcecf695d6816de3b16b0b4ca27b","bytes":4858,"section":"382","original_title":"SECTION 382 — Data Migration Operations","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":12,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_12_Maintenance_Decommissioning_and_Retirement.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A data-migration model with source, target, mapping, scope, quality, privacy, compatibility, rehearsal, cutover, dual-run, rollback, reconciliation, and owner acceptance.","original_applicability":"Apply when data, schema, database, warehouse, lake, archive, provider, format, or location changes through movement or transformation.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-07-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-03","REQ-31-01","REQ-31-02","REQ-31-03","REQ-31-04","REQ-36-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The rebuild explicitly requires schema-specific legacy migration, rehearsal, cutover and preservation. Inventory exact source/target schemas and declared data classes, mapping/meaning/lineage, consumers, privacy/access, snapshots, rehearsal, idempotence, performance, staged or dual-run design where justified, backup, cutover/rollback, category reconciliation, holds/retention/deletion and owner acceptance. Equal row counts are insufficient. Keep unknown/corrupt material and unresolved effects intact; generic implementation does not authorize normal-profile migration, source deletion or cutover.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-18/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/383_PLATFORM_MIGRATION.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/383_PLATFORM_MIGRATION.txt","sha256":"d7f5009c92c83766ca05800df950c6f5ae2e79b58f81e4a56fcb681a1078edb0","bytes":4979,"section":"383","original_title":"SECTION 383 — Platform Migration","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":12,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_12_Maintenance_Decommissioning_and_Retirement.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A platform-migration model with source and target, inventory, equivalence, dependencies, data, identity, compatibility, rehearsal, cutover, rollback, support, cost, and retirement.","original_applicability":"Apply when workloads, applications, data, infrastructure, tooling, or operations move between providers, platforms, runtimes, regions, or architectural foundations.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-00-01","REQ-05-04","REQ-07-01","REQ-31-01","REQ-31-04","REQ-31-05","REQ-36-02","REQ-39-03","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"CETA's ground-up runtime transition changes architectural foundations, identities, data, tooling and operations. Baseline exact old/new local runtime and workload/service identities, dependencies, data/configuration, security, networking/storage, support, equivalence criteria, costs when actual, rehearsal/tests, controlled coexistence, cutover/rollback and source retirement. Cloud/provider/region duties apply only if genuinely selected; this source does not select them. Running on target cannot prove equivalent service, migrated authority or provider exit.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-18/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/384_MODERNIZATION.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/384_MODERNIZATION.txt","sha256":"f2fd2dbfb11eede27c9c538b45060dcf3b831a9f959c9905b203f4a06067ba5c","bytes":4897,"section":"384","original_title":"SECTION 384 — Modernization","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":12,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_12_Maintenance_Decommissioning_and_Retirement.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A modernization model with current state, drivers, outcomes, options, constraints, target state, increments, dependencies, migration, risk, cost, evidence, and exit criteria.","original_applicability":"Apply when a system, platform, process, architecture, product, or operational capability is substantially improved, migrated, replatformed, or replaced.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-00-01","REQ-00-03","REQ-00-04","REQ-31-04","REQ-31-05","REQ-36-02","REQ-39-02","REQ-41-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01"],"decision_reason":"The owner's accepted assignment replaces the patchwork architecture with one coherent system. Retain current-state evidence, user outcomes/constraints, debt/risk, options/target, justified increments, cost/capacity when actual, migration/transition ownership, security/quality/performance/support, communication, rollback and exit criteria. No new technology or generated architecture proves benefit or transition safety. Deliver the full functioning system and deliberate old-path retirement after separately authorized cutover.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-18/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/385_REFACTORING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/385_REFACTORING.txt","sha256":"70b7399ed2bf976a1e4ef3dfe0e09186b02e3671b219fbd57b7358b8ce15a72b","bytes":4558,"section":"385","original_title":"SECTION 385 — Refactoring","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":12,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_12_Maintenance_Decommissioning_and_Retirement.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A refactoring model with invariant, baseline, scope, dependency, tests, increments, review, evidence, rollback, and explicit distinction from behavior change.","original_applicability":"Apply when internal code, architecture, schema, configuration, or structure changes with an intended stable external contract.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-00-04","REQ-05-04","REQ-16-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-02","REQ-39-03","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Implementation maintenance must distinguish internal refactoring from authorized semantic change. Inspect call sites, state actual invariant and baseline, map dependencies and boundary/timing/error/data/security/performance effects, keep changes bounded, preserve tests/public contracts unless explicitly revised, compare/differentially test, review actual diff, retain rollback and residual risk. The rebuild's changed architecture is not mislabeled behavior-preserving refactoring; no passing count proves hidden behavior equality.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-18/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/386_TECHNICAL_DEBT_MANAGEMENT.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/386_TECHNICAL_DEBT_MANAGEMENT.txt","sha256":"9098aaa7eaf292819a1f27581a99c73ba42cb0ac06dd3770f6399621164c0944","bytes":4821,"section":"386","original_title":"SECTION 386 — Technical Debt Management","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":12,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_12_Maintenance_Decommissioning_and_Retirement.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A debt model with item, cause, affected outcome, interest, risk, owner, evidence, priority, remediation, containment, decision, review, and explicit acceptance or closure.","original_applicability":"Apply when a shortcut, obsolete design, deferred maintenance, missing control, workaround, unsupported dependency, or known defect creates ongoing cost or risk.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-35-02","REQ-36-02","REQ-39-04","REQ-41-04","REQ-42-01","REQ-42-02","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01"],"decision_reason":"Known defects, missing controls and unfinished implementation must remain owned rather than dismissed. Identify actual debt/cause, affected components/users/outcomes, evidence, ongoing interest and risk, containment, priority/resource decision, owner, remediation, aging/review/expiry, regression and actual closure or escalation. Deferred debt is distinct from newly unimplemented mandatory scope; neither can be erased by renaming, score or backlog burial. Bounded risk acceptance does not close the full goal.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-18/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/387_COMPATIBILITY_MANAGEMENT.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/387_COMPATIBILITY_MANAGEMENT.txt","sha256":"5136fc3ef2ec9ea438b5498dc41ee506a5db7258c7e07a1b094229aad7498060","bytes":4589,"section":"387","original_title":"SECTION 387 — Compatibility Management","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":12,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_12_Maintenance_Decommissioning_and_Retirement.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A compatibility model with producer, consumer, version, platform, data, interface, support policy, test evidence, migration, fallback, owner, and retirement.","original_applicability":"Apply when versions, platforms, interfaces, formats, providers, devices, users, or consumers must coexist or transition.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-05-03","REQ-06-02","REQ-20-02","REQ-31-04","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-02","REQ-38-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Typed IPC, schemas, model backends and old/new installed data/executables have explicit compatibility relationships. Inventory producer/consumer/platform/device/version/contract/data combinations and actual support policy, breaking changes, tests, negotiation or explicit failure, migration/fallback/security/performance/accessibility, communication, deprecation and retirement. One combination proves only itself. Do not invent universal compatibility, indefinite support, hidden unsafe fallback or an additional cloud platform.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-18/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/388_VERSION_MANAGEMENT.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/388_VERSION_MANAGEMENT.txt","sha256":"dafe9f8afb5e02811e0ab1d729c75c0d817edbbeed8717648ac86951b4c046da","bytes":4668,"section":"388","original_title":"SECTION 388 — Version Management","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":12,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_12_Maintenance_Decommissioning_and_Retirement.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A version model with identity, scheme, source, artifact, compatibility, status, owner, support, lineage, release, change, deprecation, retention, and retirement.","original_applicability":"Apply when an artifact, interface, product, policy, data schema, configuration, or service has distinct states or supported revisions.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-06-01","REQ-06-04","REQ-35-02","REQ-38-02","REQ-38-05","REQ-40-03","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"CETA source, executable, installer, schema, policy, model and evidence need distinct exact revision identities. Define actual scheme, immutable identities/digests/lineage, source-to-artifact correspondence, owners/status/support, consumers/dependencies/compatibility, release/change, rollback, deprecation/retention/retirement and drift. Version labels cannot prove bytes, support or qualification. New development version remains separate from legacy and release publication stays an actual authority boundary.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-18/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/389_DEPRECATION_MANAGEMENT.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/389_DEPRECATION_MANAGEMENT.txt","sha256":"e5bbb908decd974d765f41184e8cf10c84b36a4640bfc46ef211e07ae1c8aef3","bytes":4717,"section":"389","original_title":"SECTION 389 — Deprecation Management","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":12,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_12_Maintenance_Decommissioning_and_Retirement.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A deprecation model with reason, scope, replacement, consumer, notice, support window, compatibility, migration, security, exception, deadline, and retirement.","original_applicability":"Apply when a capability, version, interface, asset, provider, policy, or service is marked for reduced support or eventual removal.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-31-01","REQ-31-05","REQ-36-02","REQ-38-04","REQ-39-03","REQ-40-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Duplicate legacy responsibilities and future unsupported versions require deliberate consumer migration. Inventory actual target/reason/owner/consumers, replacement or exact exception, accessible notice, support/security/contract/data impacts, migration/compatibility/fallback, deadline/expiry, telemetry and verified no-critical-consumer removal. No notice, public communication or withdrawal is implied by source review; customer/billing/contract duties apply to actual relationships, not invented commerce.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-18/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/390_SUNSET_PLANNING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/390_SUNSET_PLANNING.txt","sha256":"fce6d5062958cf781b1ef1bc5c8129cbc5cbed5d9d5da4135729f3018070922c","bytes":4997,"section":"390","original_title":"SECTION 390 — Sunset Planning","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":12,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_12_Maintenance_Decommissioning_and_Retirement.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A sunset plan with reason, scope, owners, consumers, dates, migration, communication, support, data, contract, financial, security, disposal, and completion criteria.","original_applicability":"Apply when an offering, system, service, version, feature, dependency, contract, or capability will stop being available, supported, or used.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-19-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-31-04","REQ-31-05","REQ-36-01","REQ-38-04","REQ-41-02","REQ-04-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Old live paths must be intentionally ended after qualified cutover, and the product needs an operable future sunset capability. Retain target/reason/scope/owner/users/assets, successor or accepted absence, dates, accessibility/communication/support, migration/export, records/holds/data retention/deletion, access/artifact cleanup and actual contracts/billing/licenses/certificate/DNS obligations only where owned. Separate isolated transition qualification from actual owner-authorized sunset. Shutdown alone cannot prove resolved users, data and residual obligations.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-18/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/391_DATA_RETENTION.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/391_DATA_RETENTION.txt","sha256":"629caddb6e8818c2f8b29724fe1993ef3f127dc9bb6ecc702bb402e962b9c902","bytes":4793,"section":"391","original_title":"SECTION 391 — Data Retention","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":12,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_12_Maintenance_Decommissioning_and_Retirement.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A retention model with data class, purpose, owner, authority, period, trigger, location, copies, hold, access, review, extension, expiry, disposition, and evidence.","original_applicability":"Apply when data, records, logs, backups, artifacts, messages, evidence, or personal information is stored beyond immediate operational use.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-07-01","REQ-16-04","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-29-03","REQ-35-03","REQ-36-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"CETA persists conversations, identity, evidence, payloads, indexes, backups and records. Classify actual data/records with purpose/authority/owner, justified period and trigger, exact copies/locations/access, holds, reviews/extensions/expiry, backup/archive distinctions, rights and authorized disposition. Actual law/jurisdiction/retention period/hold/qualified acceptance cannot be fabricated from the source. Metadata policy must be enforced on copies and caches, without whole-drive discovery authority.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-18/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/392_DATA_ARCHIVAL.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/392_DATA_ARCHIVAL.txt","sha256":"57a3e456a2fce25bd356bf19f2c71c6483e157d33c6063ab318ecfff1cc7a3f9","bytes":4884,"section":"392","original_title":"SECTION 392 — Data Archival","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":12,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_12_Maintenance_Decommissioning_and_Retirement.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An archival model with eligibility, authority, metadata, format, integrity, location, access, retrieval, retention, hold, migration, cost, and disposition.","original_applicability":"Apply when data, records, artifacts, evidence, or content leaves active operation but must remain available for a defined purpose or period.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-29-02","REQ-29-03","REQ-31-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-40-03","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Legacy/unknown migration material and retained inactive records need usable provenance-preserving archives. Record eligibility/purpose/authority/class, metadata/format/provenance/fixity, exact location/catalog/access/encryption, retrieval/recovery, cost where actual, holds/retention, format migration and authorized disposition. Archive is neither dump nor backup. Preserve identity and context; verify representative/critical retrieval and authenticity limitations. Bind 004 Evidence to the shared-governance namespace, not lifecycle 004 Mission Strategy.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-18/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/393_DIGITAL_PRESERVATION.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/393_DIGITAL_PRESERVATION.txt","sha256":"9face16de43e951de4ff1194840ece7cc4570ab5cdfb72a8f7b2edc620b20b4f","bytes":4934,"section":"393","original_title":"SECTION 393 — Digital Preservation","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":12,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_12_Maintenance_Decommissioning_and_Retirement.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A preservation model with selection, authority, metadata, fixity, format, context, storage, access, migration, privacy, hold, authenticity, review, and disposition.","original_applicability":"Apply when digital records, evidence, cultural or organizational memory, research, code, data, artifacts, or decisions must remain usable and trustworthy over time.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-02-03","REQ-06-03","REQ-29-02","REQ-31-01","REQ-31-02","REQ-40-03","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The rebuild must preserve originals, history, decisions and retained memory without losing meaning. Select material by actual authority/purpose, capture provenance/context/metadata, format and fixity, protected catalog/storage/access, redundancy where justified, privacy/holds, format/medium monitoring, migration/emulation, interpretation tests, review and disposition. Do not alter originals, infer authenticity or assume indefinite preservation. Bind 004 Evidence to exact shared governance. Bits, backup and preservation remain different claims.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-18/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/394_RECORDS_DISPOSAL.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/394_RECORDS_DISPOSAL.txt","sha256":"6c18eec61c52aed2595bcc6eba096fc85de46db389d4863159f9989d851fef02","bytes":4660,"section":"394","original_title":"SECTION 394 — Records Disposal","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":12,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_12_Maintenance_Decommissioning_and_Retirement.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A records-disposal model with class, authority, retention expiry, hold check, scope, copies, method, vendor, approval, certificate, exception, and evidence.","original_applicability":"Apply when records, documents, logs, archives, messages, media, or evidence are destroyed, deleted, returned, or rendered inaccessible.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-16-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-20-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-29-03","REQ-36-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Eligible records/payload disposal must reconcile privacy, retention, audit and preservation. Retain record classes/scopes/owner/authority, expiry, current hold check, actual copies/backups/archive/derived state, method/assurance, approval, controlled execution, verification and audit/exception. Vendor/certificate duties apply only when an actual vendor/method is selected; no fabricated certificate or lawful-destruction claim. Test representative isolated fixtures; real destructive disposition requires actual scope authority.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-18/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/395_DATA_DELETION.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/395_DATA_DELETION.txt","sha256":"10f1165033c2584ebb30386ec0ae1fdbf9bfef964c8425f5d3fd7ef67b0b2d16","bytes":4887,"section":"395","original_title":"SECTION 395 — Data Deletion","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":12,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_12_Maintenance_Decommissioning_and_Retirement.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A data-deletion model with data subject or scope, source and copies, authority, hold, retention, method, propagation, verification, exception, recovery, and evidence.","original_applicability":"Apply when personal, customer, operational, analytical, cached, replicated, backup, model, or configuration data is deleted, anonymized, purged, or made inaccessible.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-16-04","REQ-19-01","REQ-20-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-29-03","REQ-36-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"CETA's required forgetting/deletion must handle source, derived indexes, logs, caches and backups. Validate actual identity/request/scope/authority, rights/purpose/retention/hold and copy/lineage map; bound orchestration/tombstones or transformation, source/replica/cache/derived/model/vendor/backups where actual, privacy-preserving independent verification, residual exceptions and user communication. Minimal audit metadata is distinguished from sensitive payload; external copies remain explicit. No general deletion or hold release is authorized by this review.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-18/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/396_ACCOUNT_CLOSURE.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/396_ACCOUNT_CLOSURE.txt","sha256":"67df0301304b2b6f7d5e46c9c0ce1024beb2a1eefbfa11cf382abe40816a808f","bytes":4932,"section":"396","original_title":"SECTION 396 — Account Closure","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":12,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_12_Maintenance_Decommissioning_and_Retirement.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An account-closure model with authority, identity, entitlements, sessions, data, subscriptions, billing, dependencies, retention, export, deletion, support, appeal, and evidence.","original_applicability":"Apply when an account, identity, tenant, customer relationship, subscription, supplier access, or service account is suspended, closed, or terminated.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-06-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-19-02","REQ-29-03","REQ-31-03","REQ-36-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Local user/project/worker/service identities and grants need authentic revocation and governed closure. Validate attributable request and exact account/identity/scope/authority, sessions/access/entitlements/dependencies, data/export, holds/retention/deletion, support/appeal/recovery and recorded state. External customer/tenant/subscription/billing/payment/contract closure is conditional on genuine selection, not an adopted commerce subsystem. Closing an account or profile never implies existing normal-profile destruction or permission to fabricate identity.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-18/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/397_SERVICE_DECOMMISSIONING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/397_SERVICE_DECOMMISSIONING.txt","sha256":"4f2b8e399ef6e7c793771d9d8df167812d8ea07c8e66c053ad644a1a8302b867","bytes":4940,"section":"397","original_title":"SECTION 397 — Service Decommissioning","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":12,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_12_Maintenance_Decommissioning_and_Retirement.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A service-decommissioning model with owner, consumers, replacement, dependencies, data, access, DNS, certificates, billing, support, records, shutdown, evidence, and recovery.","original_applicability":"Apply when a service, API, application, platform capability, background job, endpoint, or customer-facing offering stops operating or accepting work.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-05-04","REQ-08-03","REQ-19-02","REQ-20-04","REQ-31-05","REQ-39-03","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"CETA local services, helpers/endpoints and retained legacy entry points require controlled lifecycle removal. Inventory exact service/version/owner/consumers/dependencies/replacement, jobs/queues/transactions, data/records, principal/access, owned endpoints/certificates/DNS and actual support/contracts/billing, notifications/monitoring; drain/migrate/revoke/remove in controlled stages with recovery and independent absence checks. Quiet process or shutdown command cannot prove consumer migration, endpoint cleanup or authority retirement. Real cutover/decommissioning is separately authorized.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-18/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/398_INFRASTRUCTURE_DECOMMISSIONING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/398_INFRASTRUCTURE_DECOMMISSIONING.txt","sha256":"799cbe250b0a768082178fa2eb07922e94017c3bb82c1bd530b5df4ad3e88256","bytes":4994,"section":"398","original_title":"SECTION 398 — Infrastructure Decommissioning","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":12,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_12_Maintenance_Decommissioning_and_Retirement.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An infrastructure-decommissioning model with inventory, ownership, workload migration, data, identity, network, certificates, backup, cost, provider, destruction, evidence, and verification.","original_applicability":"Apply when infrastructure, cloud resource, server, network, storage, account, environment, cluster, or facility resource is removed or made inactive.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-05-03","REQ-07-01","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-31-04","REQ-31-05","REQ-36-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"CETA-owned local principals, IPC, store paths, test/installed environments and required adapters have resource lifecycle duties. Inventory exact owned resources/workloads/dependencies/data/identities/routes/certificates/backup/hold/recovery/cost where actual; migrate/drain, revoke, clean owned controls, verify absence and retained recovery. Cloud/cluster/provider/IaC duties reopen only if actually selected. Do not touch shared/unowned resources or destroy normal data/key material; isolated qualification remains separate from real final resource removal.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-18/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/399_HARDWARE_DISPOSAL.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/399_HARDWARE_DISPOSAL.txt","sha256":"6a5e1e414ad9152706723f9f96c8114214625678b59eb326ddf25deb688dbf66","bytes":4857,"section":"399","original_title":"SECTION 399 — Hardware Disposal","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":12,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_12_Maintenance_Decommissioning_and_Retirement.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A hardware-disposal model with asset identity, owner, data, keys, wipe or destruction, chain of custody, vendor, condition, reuse, environmental method, certificate, and verification.","original_applicability":"Apply when hardware, device, media, component, battery, appliance, or equipment is sold, returned, reused, recycled, destroyed, or abandoned.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-19-01","REQ-23-02","REQ-29-02","REQ-33-03","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Required real hardware-backed, modality and physical device lanes retain asset end-of-life obligations. For actual declared data-bearing hardware/device/media/battery/assets retain serial/owner/condition/identity, data/key references/holds, authorized reuse/return/transfer/recycling/destruction method, qualified secure wipe or justified destruction, controlled custody/vendor/certificate/environmental result and inventory reconciliation. No asset transfer, key deletion or destruction occurs here; isolated capability qualification does not prove an actual disposal event. Recycling is not proof of secure destruction.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-18/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/400_SECURE_DESTRUCTION.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/400_SECURE_DESTRUCTION.txt","sha256":"6afd2a3c8e53899b1d04eadecec22fc9a1725cddc3106c2c6a948158802cd0b7","bytes":4854,"section":"400","original_title":"SECTION 400 — Secure Destruction","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":12,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_12_Maintenance_Decommissioning_and_Retirement.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A secure-destruction model with asset, data, authority, hold, method, assurance, custody, operator, vendor, environmental handling, certificate, and verification.","original_applicability":"Apply when information or physical media must be made unrecoverable or unusable, including when cryptographic erasure is used as the destruction method.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-17-03","REQ-19-01","REQ-20-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-33-03","REQ-36-03","REQ-04-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Protected payload/credential/media lifecycle requires honest destruction assurance for actual selected methods. Bind actual data/key/asset scope, authority/owner, retention/holds, justified method/assurance, copies and residuals, dual or independent control when required, operator/custody/vendor, environmental output and exact certificate/verification. Cryptographic erasure, logical deletion, physical destruction and disposal are not interchangeable. No production key use/destruction or active asset operation is implied; actual recovery-impossibility claims require qualified method/level evidence.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-18/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/401_ENVIRONMENTAL_DISPOSAL_OR_RECYCLING.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/401_ENVIRONMENTAL_DISPOSAL_OR_RECYCLING.txt","sha256":"ac419405f9d22244ff03d6218e98a44547df596b16cf7ed5c7e84cca06d1f292","bytes":5117,"section":"401","original_title":"SECTION 401 — Environmental Disposal or Recycling","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":12,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_12_Maintenance_Decommissioning_and_Retirement.pdf","original_required_outcome":"An environmental-disposition model with material, hazard, asset, data, method, vendor, jurisdiction, chain of custody, recycling or disposal result, certificate, and impact evidence.","original_applicability":"Apply when equipment, electronics, batteries, media, chemicals, packaging, or materials are recycled, disposed, returned, reused, or transferred to a waste channel.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-19-01","REQ-29-02","REQ-33-03","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-04","REQ-42-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"Required hardware/physical lanes retain lawful safe end-of-life material and data obligations. When actual declared equipment/media/battery/material disposition occurs, record exact asset/material/hazard/data/security treatment, owner/qualified authorities, real jurisdiction/vendor/route/custody/method, safe transport, certificate and observed recycling/disposal outcome. No jurisdiction, legal standard, vendor, hazardous method or environmental result is invented or selected by reconciliation. Qualify isolated control pathways separately; real transfer/export/destruction needs actual authority.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-18/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/402_POST_IMPLEMENTATION_REVIEW.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/402_POST_IMPLEMENTATION_REVIEW.txt","sha256":"01392233000aae5ec94f5205f5fd1bcd6f7424a053d84052d3c1ae1202df0f42","bytes":4719,"section":"402","original_title":"SECTION 402 — Post-Implementation Review","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":12,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_12_Maintenance_Decommissioning_and_Retirement.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A review record with objective, baseline, implementation, expected and actual outcome, evidence, variance, user and operator impact, unresolved risk, actions, and decision.","original_applicability":"Apply after a material implementation, launch, migration, policy, process, or operational change when outcome or learning matters.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-00-03","REQ-24-01","REQ-35-03","REQ-36-01","REQ-37-02","REQ-41-04","REQ-42-03","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01"],"decision_reason":"The full rebuild must compare actual results with the original objective and requirements. Retain objective/current baseline, exact implementation, expected/actual outcomes and measured periods, real user/operator feedback where actually obtained, costs/risks/incidents/support/accessibility/privacy/security, variance/harms, causal uncertainty/dissent, actions/owners and follow-up. No launch, generated report, metric or test count substitutes for product outcome or human acceptance.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-18/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/403_POSTMORTEM_ANALYSIS.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/403_POSTMORTEM_ANALYSIS.txt","sha256":"71cad866b1f53658fbb300060c023b439887b476e73035db6a6898e247db83ae","bytes":4754,"section":"403","original_title":"SECTION 403 — Postmortem Analysis","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":12,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_12_Maintenance_Decommissioning_and_Retirement.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A blameless postmortem with scope, timeline, impact, detection, response, contributing conditions, uncertainty, evidence, actions, owners, due dates, and follow-up.","original_applicability":"Apply to material incident, outage, safety event, security event, privacy event, near miss, failed recovery, or recurring problem where learning and action matter.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-24-04","REQ-35-01","REQ-36-02","REQ-39-04","REQ-40-03","REQ-42-01","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"CETA's material failures/security/privacy/recovery incidents require preserved learning and corrective action. Scope actual event/participants, protect evidence and private context, reconstruct time basis/timeline and bounded impact/detection/response, contributing conditions and uncertainty, preserved dissent, qualified human review, action owners/dates/recurrence measures and follow-up. A neat narrative cannot prove root cause; publish/external communication retains actual authority. Bind 004 Evidence to shared governance.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-18/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/404_LESSONS_LEARNED.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/404_LESSONS_LEARNED.txt","sha256":"989ed4a6c6b603a8e9f4ad68e71c10e299f3ec2ec20eef87b5e5de0abfb80868","bytes":4551,"section":"404","original_title":"SECTION 404 — Lessons Learned","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":12,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_12_Maintenance_Decommissioning_and_Retirement.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A lessons-learned model with event, evidence, insight, uncertainty, applicability, action, owner, adoption, measure, review, and knowledge handoff.","original_applicability":"Apply after material work, incident, experiment, review, migration, release, failure, or success where experience can improve future decisions or practice.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-16-04","REQ-24-05","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-02","REQ-39-04","REQ-40-03","REQ-04-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-04"],"decision_reason":"The persistent system and engineering work must use verified experience without stale guidance or anecdotal generalization. Bind actual event/context/participants/source/evidence, bounded insight/confidence/limits/applicability/dissent, action/owner and authorized adoption in knowledge/docs/tests/policy/design, outcome measure/review and stale withdrawal. Feedback does not automatically alter facts, model weights, identity or binding policy; training/policy changes retain separate authority. Bind 004 Evidence to shared governance.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-18/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/405_LIFECYCLE_GOVERNANCE.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/405_LIFECYCLE_GOVERNANCE.txt","sha256":"f8f6c894a6660531456617da1b6e8e2c49f57ab7e44c40dfa393ade61f7794b4","bytes":4940,"section":"405","original_title":"SECTION 405 — Lifecycle Governance","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":12,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_12_Maintenance_Decommissioning_and_Retirement.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A lifecycle-governance model with states, entry and exit criteria, owners, decision rights, evidence, risk, dependencies, review, exceptions, handoff, retention, and retirement.","original_applicability":"Apply to any system, product, service, capability, data set, asset, policy, or relationship that moves through defined states over time.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-06-02","REQ-19-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-39-04","REQ-40-01","REQ-41-01","REQ-41-02","REQ-41-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01"],"decision_reason":"Every declared CETA capability, data/asset/policy/service object needs durable governed lifecycle transitions. Define actual object/state/version, owner/authority, entry/exit/evidence, dependencies/risks/expiry/exceptions, review/support/recovery/handoff, maintenance/debt/security/privacy, retention/deprecation/retirement and audit. Labels do not prove criteria or human acceptance. Keep full 28-work-package/20-volume/406-source/128-case/eight-gate scope and genuine independent/hardware/installed/endurance duties; assessment counts do not close Gate A or full supplemental corpus reconciliation.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-18/read_receipt.json"]},{"original_archive_path":"Thirstys Codex/03_SECTIONS/406_SYSTEM_RETIREMENT.txt","path":"sources/codex/canonical_text/03_SECTIONS/406_SYSTEM_RETIREMENT.txt","sha256":"2535a14b264c99d98313ea859c8624cf489df24fca5826a6c66e7b1edf106fa7","bytes":14981,"section":"406","original_title":"SECTION 406 — System Retirement","original_status":"CONTENT-COMPLETE","applicability":"DIRECT","implementation_status":"NOT_STARTED","conformance_status":"NOT_EVALUATED","reconciliation_instruction":"Read original applicability/prerequisites and map its applicable clauses to exact CETA requirements before coding the affected work package.","volume":12,"volume_pdf":"sources/codex/Thirstys_Codex_Standards_Edition_Volume_12_Maintenance_Decommissioning_and_Retirement.pdf","original_required_outcome":"A system-retirement model with reason, scope, owner, users, dependencies, successor, data, records, access, contracts, finances, operations, migration, decommissioning, disposal, evidence, and final acceptance.","original_applicability":"Apply whenever a system, product, service, platform, application, process, device fleet, data capability, or organizational technology is permanently removed, replaced, or made unavailable for its prior purpose.","original_non_applicability":null,"requirement_ids":["REQ-19-01","REQ-20-01","REQ-20-04","REQ-29-02","REQ-31-04","REQ-31-05","REQ-33-03","REQ-36-03","REQ-37-03","REQ-37-04","REQ-39-03","REQ-40-03","REQ-41-04","REQ-04-02","REQ-29-01","REQ-30-01","REQ-35-02","REQ-36-01","REQ-36-04","REQ-37-01","REQ-40-01"],"decision_reason":"The coherent rebuild must retire duplicate legacy live paths after qualified cutover and provide a governed end-of-life capability without treating the active product as already retired. Preserve all 156 source lines as the full capstone: exact purpose/reason/scope/authority/owner/users/affected parties, approved successor or nonreplacement, complete system/device/data/model/prompt/tool/key/certificate/DNS/vendor/license/contract/subscription/billing/support/backup/archive/monitoring inventory and hidden/shared/physical dependencies; tested migration/export/reconciliation/accessibility/communication/training/appeal/recovery; every data/asset class hold/retention/archive/deletion/destruction/environment; stage drain/transaction disposition/revoke/decommission; actual post-shutdown observation; independent final review and accountable human acceptance with explicit unresolved/residual state. These are capability/representative isolated candidate qualification obligations distinct from any real owner-authorized end-of-life event, production cutover or active data/key/device destruction. Temporary pause, shutdown or missing traffic cannot establish retirement. Exact law, rights, standards, counterparties, periods and acceptance remain actual inputs. All mandatory hardware/physical/distributed/custody/model/human/independent/installed/endurance requirements and supplemental20-volume reconciliation remain open until their own evidence exists.","inspection_evidence_refs":["handoff/source_reconciliation_20261008_16.md","handoff/volumes_x_xi_xii_reconciliation_20261008_16.json",".local-build-cache/working-increment-18/read_receipt.json"]}]}
diff --git a/tools/README.md b/tools/README.md
index 00a5564faf33a896a26e14b262b328cb92aae11e..544b0b25022f1bced9aaae4dac7ddc37e6a80a65 100644
--- a/tools/README.md
+++ b/tools/README.md
@@ -8,3 +8,38 @@ The package checker belongs to specification tooling. Application verification c
 
 
 `python tools/selftest_package_validator.py` reproduces the 15 structural-checker tests using an isolated temporary copy. It deliberately mutates only that copy, leaves the original package unchanged and prints its results. The tests concern document integrity and false-status detection, not application safety. The optional jsonschema library must already be installed for this self-test.
+
+`py -3 -B tools/verify_allocations.py` checks current declared requirement,
+component, work-package, case and gate relationships against the preserved
+manifest-bound identifier sets. It detects missing allocations, unknown or
+duplicate links, mismatched owner/section assignments, missing forward case
+bindings and cycles in the declared component/work-package dependency graphs.
+Inputs are hashed before and after the read. It writes JSON to stdout and never
+changes a requirement, case, gate or runtime status. Contract rejections report
+stable error codes.
+
+The allocation checker is specification tooling. Its PASS means the checked
+registry relationships are consistent within that scope. It does not verify
+interface implementations, actual imports/processes, assigned human reviewers,
+source semantics, test adequacy, runtime behavior or Gate A completion. The
+preserved identifier universe is the current handoff baseline; a deliberate
+baseline amendment requires updating the corresponding baseline evidence,
+rather than silently dropping a requirement or case from the checker.
+
+The source checker command, py -3 -B tools/verify_source_coverage.py, verifies
+supplied immutable source bytes and detailed applicability references. Its
+coverage summary must agree with the detailed rows. The original pending-only
+description is accepted only when every row is unresolved; a stale counted
+summary is rejected. Parsed metadata bytes must match the first input snapshot,
+and all watched inputs must remain unchanged through verification. These checks
+add no source adoption, conformance, runtime qualification or Gate A acceptance.
+The existing --require-reconciliation flag also requires zero unresolved rows.
+The report binds the actual parsed metadata hashes and checker hash. A completed
+unchanged-input check is reported explicitly; failure before that check leaves
+its field unknown rather than claiming unchanged bytes.
+
+Run its targeted integrity and mutation tests with
+py -3 -B -m unittest discover -s tests/contract -p test_source_coverage.py -v.
+
+Run its targeted fault-injection tests with
+`py -3 -B -m unittest discover -s tests/contract -p test_allocations.py -v`.
